rn recognition angle."},{"span":"c13","atoms":["kin.speed","rel.occupies","st.intersection"],"derived":["drv.motion.moving"],"justification":"Yielding is granting precedence (DEF-NRS-484A-210, \"unless one grants precedence to the other\"): x does not proceed into a conflict. Judged at every observation of the passage at which x occupies i (rel.occupies) and is in motion (drv.motion.moving: \"its speed exceeds speed_floor\", kin.speed); a halted person grants precedence."},{"span":"c15","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian","rel.occupies","st.crosswalk","st.entrance_of","st.lane_enters","st.intersection"],"derived":[],"justification":"'pedestrians' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian (\"a person afoot, a person in a manual or motorized wheelchair\"); 'within an adjacent crosswalk' is the pedestrian's footprint overlapping (rel.occupies) a st.crosswalk recorded as marking the entrance of a carrier entering i (st.entrance_of: \"the carrier whose entrance into an intersection a stop line or a crosswalk marks\"; st.lane_enters). Distance is not used for adjacency."},{"span":"c16","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","rel.occupies","st.intersection"],"derived":[],"justification":"'other traffic' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic (\"pedestrians, ridden or herded animals, vehicles and other conveyances\"), every member other than x; 'using the intersection' is its footprint overlapping i (rel.occupies)."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"c14","standard":"the right-of-way: proceeding where the parties' \"direction, speed and proximity\" \"give rise to the danger of a crash unless one grants precedence\" (DEF-NRS-484A-210)","concepts":["prim.closest_approach_within","prim.closest_approach_distance"],"params":["p.immediate_hazard_gap","p.conflict_clearance"],"convention":"Gap-acceptance and surrogate-safety convention: the danger of a crash between the person and another party is their predicted closest approach under constant velocities, within the critical gap, coming nearer than the conflict radius; direction, speed and proximity all enter the prediction by their degree.","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[{"span":"c3","why":"Every trimobile, a motor vehicle with a seat designed to travel on three wheels, is already a member of the motorcycle aggregate claimed on span c2 (\"every motor vehicle equipped with a seat or saddle for the use of the driver and designed to travel on not more than three wheels in contact with the ground\"): the duty is the same whether or not the word is read.","scope":"none"}],"binders":[{"name":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"]}],"applicability":"As NRS_484B_307_9b_o1: x carries one of the five aggregates of spans c2 and c4; at the observation x leaves intersection i (drv.motion.leaving_region(x, i)); at its latest entry into i (read through a past operator) it came in through carrier c with st.lane_enters(c, i) (drv.position.entered_via(x, i, c)) while a traffic signal s that governs c or i (dev.governs) displayed circular_red together with green_arrow(d), d left or right; and at the leaving the heading change since that entry (drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry(x, i) with step p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph) shows a straight-through passage (absolute value below p.turn_recognition_angle) or a turn opposite d.","obligation":"At every observation from that entry up to the leaving (read through a past operator from the leaving observation) at which x occupies i and is moving (drv.motion.moving with p.speed_resolution): for every road user p carrying ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian that occupies a crosswalk w recorded as marking the entrance of some carrier c2 entering i (st.entrance_of(w, c2), st.lane_enters(c2, i)), and for every road user u other than x carrying ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic that occupies i, it is not the case that x and that road user approach within p.immediate_hazard_gap (prim.closest_approach_within) with a closest-approach centre distance (prim.closest_approach_distance) below p.conflict_clearance.","params":["p.speed_resolution","p.immediate_hazard_gap","p.conflict_clearance","p.turn_recognition_angle","p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph"],"narrowings":[{"span":"c2","why":"'A person driving' is read through the machine's controlled motion.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"c4","why":"'riding' is read through the machine's controlled motion.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"c15","why":"'lawfully' is not read: every pedestrian in such a crosswalk is yielded to. 'an adjacent crosswalk' is read as a crosswalk recorded as marking the entrance of a carrier entering the intersection; a crosswalk across the exit of a one-way leg is not read.","kind":"reading"},{"span":"c16","why":"'lawfully' is not read: every other member of traffic inside the intersection is yielded to.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"x (ru.motorcycle) goes straight through i under circular_red with green_arrow(left); while it moves inside i a ru.pedestrian occupies the crosswalk at the far side, marking the entrance of the opposing carrier, and prim.closest_approach_within holds over p.immediate_hazard_gap with a prim.closest_approach_distance below p.conflict_clearance."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"x (ru.bicycle) goes straight through i under circular_red with green_arrow(left) with no other road user in the scene."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"x (ru.motorcycle) enters i under circular_red with green_arrow(left) and turns left, the movement the arrow indicates."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x goes straight through i under circular_red with green_arrow(left) near a crossing pedestrian, but the source does not observe x's footprint overlap with i.","masked":["rel.occupies"]}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.speed_resolution","unit":"m/s","value":0.2,"convention":"Sensor resolution: the smallest speed the acquisition standard separates from standstill; a speed at or below it counts as no motion.","source":"speed resolution of the carla_scene_graph acquisition standard"},{"name":"p.immediate_hazard_gap","unit":"s","value":4.1,"convention":"Critical gap: the time within which another road user's arrival at the conflict area, or its predicted closest approach, counts as an immediate hazard to a road user about to cross or join its path.","source":"Highway Capacity Manual critical-gap values"},{"name":"p.conflict_clearance","unit":"m","value":3.0,"convention":"Conflict radius: the centre distance at predicted closest approach below which two road users' paths count as in conflict; about the half-length plus half-width of two passenger cars.","source":"surrogate safety measures (closest-approach conflict radius)"},{"name":"p.turn_recognition_angle","unit":"deg","value":45,"convention":"Turn recognition: the heading change through an intersection beyond which a passage counts as a turn rather than a straight crossing; half the right angle of a turn at a right-angled junction, leaving room for skewed junctions and lane offsets.","source":"intersection geometry design conventions (AASHTO Green Book)"}],"gaps":[]}
{"concept_id":"drv.motion.u_turn","kind":"formula","contract":"Road user x has turned so as to proceed in the opposite direction: the turning that the corpus defines as \"the turning of a vehicle upon a highway so as to proceed in the opposite direction, whether accomplished by one continuous movement or not\", observed as a reversal of x's heading. It holds at an observation where the absolute value of x's signed heading change over the window behind it (prim.heading_change with window; degrees, left positive) differs from the literal half turn by no more than reversal_tolerance: the heading now points the opposite way within the tolerance, and a heading change that has gone past the half turn by more than the tolerance (a loop back toward the first direction) does not count. A turning made in several movements, forward and backing, counts, since the heading change is integrated through all of them. The act begins within the window behind the observation of recognition; it is recognized at the observation at which this condition rises; it holds at the later observations at which the reversal still lies within the window behind them, which are not the act again, and it ends when the reversal leaves that window. Unknown where the window is truncated, sampled too sparsely, or a yaw rate is missing. Not denoted: a turning by less than a reversal, or the place of the turning: the caller states the highway or the zone.","definition":"DEF-NRS-484B-077","args":[{"name":"x","sort":"track"}],"params":[{"name":"window","unit":"s","meaning":"the longest time over which a reversal of heading, in one movement or several, is recognized as one turning: the window behind the observation over which the heading change is integrated"},{"name":"reversal_tolerance","unit":"deg","meaning":"the largest difference between the size of the heading change and the half turn within which the road user counts as proceeding in the opposite direction"}],"act":{"boundary":"window","window":"window","onset":"The act begins within the window behind the observation of recognition","recognition":"it is recognized at the observation at which this condition rises","extent":"it holds at the later observations at which the reversal still lies within the window behind them, which are not the act again, and it ends when the reversal leaves that window","history":"Unknown where the window is truncated, sampled too sparsely, or a yaw rate is missing"},"elements":[{"span":"the absolute value of x's signed heading change over the window behind it (prim.heading_change with window; degrees, left positive)","atoms":["prim.heading_change"],"concepts":[],"justification":"prim.heading_change: \"the signed heading change (degrees, left positive) of a road user over the window behind the observation, integrated from kin.yaw_rate; unknown where the window is truncated, sampled too sparsely, or a yaw rate is missing\"; its window is the formal window. Integration through forward and backing movements carries \"whether accomplished by one continuous movement or not\"."}],"residues":[{"span":"upon a highway","why":"The place is the caller's: the concept reads x's heading only, and the calling rule states the region (the highway or the zone) the turning is made in."},{"span":"so as to proceed in the opposite direction","why":"Read as the reversal of x's own heading. A road user following a bend of the way that itself turns through a half turn within the window also reverses its heading; no atom of the closed set states the course of the way along x's path, so the two are not told apart."}],"literals":[{"value":180,"unit":"deg","why":"the half turn: a heading pointing the opposite way"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"holds","expected":"compliant","narrative":"x drives along a street, swings left across the centre line and completes the turning heading the opposite way within the window; the size of prim.heading_change differs from the half turn by less than reversal_tolerance."},{"name":"fails","expected":"violated","narrative":"x turns right at a junction; the size of prim.heading_change over the window is about a quarter turn."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x reverses its heading, but its yaw rate is missing during the window.","masked":["kin.yaw_rate"]}],"used_by":["NRS_484B_363_3"],"supersedes":null}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_363_3","law_refs":["NRS-484B-363-3"],"subject":{"binder":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"d1","text":"The driver of a vehicle","role":"subject"},{"id":"d2","text":"shall not make a U-turn","role":"obligation"},{"id":"d3","text":"in an area designated as a school zone or school crossing zone","role":"trigger"},{"id":"d4","text":"except:","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"d5","text":"(a) When there are no children present;","role":"exception"},{"id":"d6","text":"(b) On a day on which school is not in session;","role":"exception"},{"id":"d7","text":"(c) During the period from a half hour after school is no longer in operation to a half hour before school is next in operation;","role":"exception"},{"id":"d8","text":"(d) If the zone is designated by an operational speed limit beacon,","role":"exception"},{"id":"d9","text":"during the hours when the pupils of the school are in class","role":"exception"},{"id":"d10","text":"and the yellow lights of the speed limit beacon are not flashing in the manner which indicates that the speed limit is in effect;","role":"exception"},{"id":"d11","text":"or","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"d12","text":"(e) If the zone is not designated by an operational speed limit beacon,","role":"exception"},{"id":"d13","text":"during the times when the sign designating the school zone or school crossing zone indicates that the speed limit is not in effect.","role":"exception"},{"id":"d14","text":"As used in this section, “speed limit beacon” means a device which is used in conjunction with a sign and equipped with two or more yellow lights that flash alternately to indicate when the speed limit in a school zone or school crossing zone is in effect.","role":"definitional"}],"elements":[{"span":"d1","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle (\"every device in, upon or by which any person or property is or may be transported or drawn upon a highway\", with its exceptions), claimed by id. 'The driver of' names who controls it (DEF-NRS-484A-080, \"every person who drives or is in actual physical control of a vehicle\"), a role read through the vehicle's controlled motion (observable_reading agency), not a membership."},{"span":"d2","atoms":["prim.heading_change"],"derived":["drv.motion.u_turn"],"justification":"'U-turn' is defined by DEF-NRS-484B-077 (\"the turning of a vehicle upon a highway so as to proceed in the opposite direction, whether accomplished by one continuous movement or not\"); the proposed definition-born concept drv.motion.u_turn carries it, recognizing the reversal of x's heading over a window through prim.heading_change. The place, upon a highway inside the zone, is stated by span d3."},{"span":"d3","atoms":["dev.zone_sign","dev.governs","rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"A school zone or school crossing zone (DEF-NRS-484B-063 \"those sections of streets which are adjacent to school property\"; DEF-NRS-484B-060) is a legal region class that is also marked on the road; the ontology's section on what is not an atom: \"Where the same category is also marked on the road by a sign (dev.zone_sign), the sign is the atom and the category is not.\" dev.zone_sign: \"a sign that begins or ends a signed zone along the road; kind ∈ {school, school_crossing, ...}\". The area designated is the travel regions the sign governs (dev.governs: \"the travel regions whose traffic the device controls\"), and x is in it where its footprint overlaps one (rel.occupies). dev.zone_sign is 'not a stand-in' for whether its condition holds now; that is read only in span d13 through prim.conditions_hold."},{"span":"d5","atoms":["ru.child","st.region_geometry","dev.zone_sign","dev.governs","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"Children present in the zone: a road user of class ru.child (\"pedestrian who is visibly a child\") whose body lies within the presence reach of a travel region the zone sign governs (st.region_geometry: \"the ground distance from a road user's body outline to it (zero when they overlap)\"), so that children on the sidewalks beside the zone's lanes count. A reach relates the region to the child, not two regions. No children present: no such road user."},{"span":"d8","atoms":["dev.speed_limit_beacon","dev.governs","rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"The zone designated by a speed limit beacon: a dev.speed_limit_beacon (\"a pair or more of yellow lamps mounted with a speed sign, flashing alternately when the sign's limit is in effect\", which is the section's own definition in span d14) governing (dev.governs) the travel region x occupies (rel.occupies) or a region the zone sign governs. 'operational' is read through the beacon's presence (observable_reading status)."},{"span":"d10","atoms":["dev.speed_limit_beacon"],"derived":[],"justification":"dev.speed_limit_beacon \"flashing attribute\": the beacon's lights not flashing in the manner that indicates the limit is in effect is its flashing attribute false."},{"span":"d12","atoms":["dev.speed_limit_beacon","dev.governs","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"A zone not designated by a speed limit beacon: no dev.speed_limit_beacon governs (dev.governs) the travel region x occupies or a region the zone sign governs."},{"span":"d13","atoms":["dev.zone_sign","prim.conditions_hold"],"derived":[],"justification":"The sign designating the zone is the dev.zone_sign of span d3, whose \"conditions attribute: a structured reading of the sign's legend\" states when its limit is in effect; that it indicates the limit is not in effect is prim.conditions_hold (\"the structured conditions of a device ... hold at the observation for a road user\") false for x. The sign is 'not a stand-in' for the condition holding, which is why the primitive reads it."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[{"span":"d6","id":"asm.school_not_in_session_day","meaning":"The calendar day of the observation is one on which the school the zone serves is not in session, as declared for the map or the trace."},{"span":"d7","id":"asm.outside_school_operation_margin","meaning":"The time of the observation lies at least a half hour after the school the zone serves last ceased operation and at least a half hour before it next begins operation, as declared for the map or the trace."},{"span":"d9","id":"asm.pupils_in_class","meaning":"The time of the observation lies within the hours during which the pupils of the school the zone serves are in class, as declared for the map or the trace."}],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"x carries ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; at the observation x's U-turn is recognized (drv.motion.u_turn(x) with p.u_turn_window and p.u_turn_reversal_tolerance rises there); and at some observation of that act (an observation within p.u_turn_window behind the recognition at which x yaws, drv.motion.yawing with p.yaw_rate_resolution) x's footprint overlapped a travel region r governed (dev.governs) by a dev.zone_sign z of kind school or school_crossing that is not an end sign.","obligation":"The U-turn is made only where one exception covers the whole act: for one of the alternatives below, that alternative holds at every observation of the act (each observation within p.u_turn_window behind the recognition at which x yaws). (a) No road user of class ru.child lies within p.child_presence_reach (st.region_geometry distance) of a travel region z governs. (b) asm.school_not_in_session_day holds. (c) asm.outside_school_operation_margin holds. (d) A dev.speed_limit_beacon governs the region x occupies or a region z governs, asm.pupils_in_class holds, and that beacon is not flashing. (e) No dev.speed_limit_beacon governs the region x occupies or a region z governs, and z's conditions do not hold for x (prim.conditions_hold false). Where none of them covers the whole act, the duty is violated.","params":["p.u_turn_window","p.u_turn_reversal_tolerance","p.yaw_rate_resolution","p.child_presence_reach"],"narrowings":[{"span":"d1","why":"'The driver of a vehicle' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion: the duty binds the vehicle's conduct whoever or whatever controls it.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"d3","why":"'an area designated as a school zone or school crossing zone' is read through the zone sign on the road and the travel regions it governs; the designation is presumed from the sign's presence.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"status"},{"span":"d8","why":"'operational' is read through the beacon's presence governing the zone's regions; a beacon that is installed but out of order is not told apart.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"status"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"x (ru.motor_vehicle) makes a U-turn on a lane governed by a school zone sign z; a ru.child stands within p.child_presence_reach of z's lane at every observation, asm.school_not_in_session_day and asm.outside_school_operation_margin are declared false, and a speed limit beacon governing the lane is flashing."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"x makes a U-turn on z's lane while no ru.child lies within p.child_presence_reach of any region z governs at any observation of the act."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"x makes a U-turn on a street no school zone or school crossing zone sign governs."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x drives along z's lane with children on the sidewalk and turns about, but its yaw rate is missing, so whether a U-turn was made is unknown.","masked":["kin.yaw_rate"]},{"name":"occasion_d3","expected":"violated","narrative":"Baseline as in forbid (children present, school in session, inside the operation margin, beacon flashing): x begins its U-turn on z's lane and completes it on a lane beyond the stretch z governs; it occupied z's lane for part of the act only."},{"name":"occasion_d3_outside","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"x drove along z's lane, left the governed stretch, and only afterwards, on a lane no zone sign governs, makes its U-turn: it was in the zone before the act began only."},{"name":"occasion_d5","expected":"violated","narrative":"U-turn on z's lane; no ru.child is within p.child_presence_reach at the first observations of the act, then a child walks up beside the lane before the act is recognized; the other alternatives fail throughout."},{"name":"occasion_d5_outside","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Children stood beside z's lane before the act began and left; at every observation of the U-turn none lies within p.child_presence_reach; the other alternatives fail."},{"name":"occasion_d6","expected":"violated","narrative":"U-turn on z's lane across midnight: asm.school_not_in_session_day is declared true at the first observations of the act and false at the rest; children present and the other alternatives fail."},{"name":"occasion_d6_outside","expected":"compliant","narrative":"asm.school_not_in_session_day is declared false before the act and true at every observation of the U-turn; children present."},{"name":"occasion_d7","expected":"violated","narrative":"asm.outside_school_operation_margin is declared true for the first part of the U-turn and false for the rest; children present and the other alternatives fail."},{"name":"occasion_d7_outside","expected":"compliant","narrative":"asm.outside_school_operation_margin is declared false before the act and true at every observation of the U-turn; children present."},{"name":"occasion_d8","expected":"violated","narrative":"A beacon governs the region x occupies at the start of the U-turn only; x ends the turn on a region no beacon governs; asm.pupils_in_class holds and the beacon is not flashing; z's conditions hold; children present, school in session, inside the margin: neither (d) nor (e) covers the whole act."},{"name":"occasion_d8_outside","expected":"compliant","narrative":"No beacon governs the region x occupied before the act; a non-flashing beacon governs every region x occupies during the U-turn and asm.pupils_in_class holds throughout it; children present."},{"name":"occasion_d9","expected":"violated","narrative":"A non-flashing beacon governs z's lane throughout; asm.pupils_in_class is declared true for part of the U-turn only; children present, school in session, inside the margin."},{"name":"occasion_d9_outside","expected":"compliant","narrative":"A non-flashing beacon governs z's lane throughout; asm.pupils_in_class is declared false before the act and true at every observation of the U-turn; children present."},{"name":"occasion_d10","expected":"violated","narrative":"A beacon governs z's lane and asm.pupils_in_class holds throughout; the beacon is not flashing for the first part of the U-turn and flashing for the rest; children present."},{"name":"occasion_d10_outside","expected":"compliant","narrative":"A beacon governs z's lane and asm.pupils_in_class holds throughout; the beacon was flashing before the act and is not flashing at any observation of the U-turn; children present."},{"name":"occasion_d12","expected":"violated","narrative":"No beacon governs the region x occupies at the start of the U-turn, a flashing beacon governs the region it ends on; z's conditions do not hold throughout; children present, school in session, inside the margin."},{"name":"occasion_d12_outside","expected":"compliant","narrative":"A beacon governed the region x occupied before the act; no beacon governs any region x occupies or z governs during the U-turn; z's conditions do not hold throughout; children present."},{"name":"occasion_d13","expected":"violated","narrative":"No beacon; env.civil_time leaves z's posted window during the U-turn, so z's conditions hold for the first part of the act and not for the rest; children present, school in session, inside the margin."},{"name":"occasion_d13_outside","expected":"compliant","narrative":"No beacon; z's conditions held before the act and do not hold at any observation of the U-turn; children present."}],"occasion":{"act":"drv.motion.u_turn","boundary":"window","window":"p.u_turn_window","under_way":{"words":"make a U-turn","atoms":["kin.yaw_rate"],"derived":["drv.motion.yawing"],"justification":"An observation inside the act is one within the U-turn window behind the recognition at which x's heading is changing (drv.motion.yawing: \"the absolute value of its yaw rate exceeds yaw_floor\", kin.yaw_rate): the turning is motion, and x occupied the zone's lanes before the turning began, so no region alone tells the act apart."},"spans":{"d3":"some_moment","d5":"throughout","d6":"throughout","d7":"throughout","d8":"throughout","d9":"throughout","d10":"throughout","d12":"throughout","d13":"throughout"}},"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.u_turn_window","unit":"s","value":20,"convention":"U-turn recognition window: the longest time over which a reversal of heading, made in one movement or in several forward and backing movements, is recognized as one turning; a multi-point turn on a narrow street.","source":"observed durations of three-point turns (naturalistic driving studies)"},{"name":"p.u_turn_reversal_tolerance","unit":"deg","value":30,"convention":"Reversal tolerance: the largest difference between the size of the heading change over the window and a half turn within which the road user counts as proceeding in the opposite direction; covers the offset of a turn into a lane of the opposite direction and heading noise.","source":"trajectory-classification practice for U-turn detection"},{"name":"p.yaw_rate_resolution","unit":"deg/s","value":2.0,"convention":"Sensor resolution: the smallest yaw rate the acquisition standard separates from a straight path; a yaw rate at or below it counts as no heading change.","source":"yaw-rate resolution of the carla_scene_graph acquisition standard"},{"name":"p.child_presence_reach","unit":"m","value":5.0,"convention":"Presence reach: the ground distance from a child's body to a travel region of a school zone within which the child counts as present in the zone; the width of a sidewalk and verge beside the roadway.","source":"urban street cross-section conventions (sidewalk and buffer widths)"}],"gaps":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_400_1_o1","law_refs":["NRS-484B-400-1"],"subject":{"binder":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"e1","text":"If the driver of a vehicle","role":"subject"},{"id":"e2","text":"intends to turn","role":"trigger"},{"id":"e3","text":"at an intersection","role":"trigger"},{"id":"e4","text":"and:","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"e5","text":"The turn is a right turn,","role":"trigger"},{"id":"e6","text":"both the approach for the right turn and the right turn must be made from the right turn lane","role":"obligation"},{"id":"e7","text":"if the highway has a right turn lane","role":"condition"},{"id":"e8","text":"as set forth in subsection 4 of NRS 484B.223 [NRS-484B-223-4a, NRS-484B-223-4b],","role":"reference"},{"id":"e9","text":"or must be made from the extreme right lane.","role":"sibling"}],"elements":[{"span":"e1","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle (\"every device in, upon or by which any person or property is or may be transported or drawn upon a highway\"), claimed by id. 'the driver of' is a role read through the vehicle's controlled motion (observable_reading agency)."},{"span":"e3","atoms":["st.intersection","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region","rel.occupies"],"derived":["drv.motion.entering_region"],"justification":"The intersection the intention is declared at and the turn is made in: st.intersection (\"the region where two roadways meet\"), entered by x (drv.motion.entering_region: \"its footprint overlaps r (rel.occupies) at the observation and did not at the observation before\") from the approach carrier it occupies whose entrance end is i (st.lane_enters: \"the intersection region a directed approach carrier runs into at its entrance end\")."},{"span":"e5","atoms":["kin.yaw_rate","rel.occupies"],"derived":["drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry"],"justification":"The turn made is a right turn where the heading change of x since it entered i (drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry: \"The signed heading change of road user x since its footprint last began to overlap region r, in degrees, left positive\", from kin.yaw_rate) reaches the turn recognition angle to the right. The concept is 'not' a turn by itself; the rule compares it with its bound."},{"span":"e6","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.turn_lane","st.lane_enters","st.intersection","kin.path_length"],"derived":[],"justification":"The approach for the turn and the turn are made from the right turn lane R where x's footprint overlaps R (rel.occupies) at its entry into i and at every observation of the approach length of path travelled before it at which x occupies a carrier entering i (a .path window, which reads kin.path_length, \"distance travelled along the body's path\"). R is the st.turn_lane (\"a lane designated only for turning; side ∈ {left, right}\") of side right that enters i (st.lane_enters)."},{"span":"e7","atoms":["st.highway","st.on_way","st.turn_lane","st.lane_enters","st.lane_direction"],"derived":["drv.road.opposed_directions"],"source_spans":["e8"],"justification":"The highway has a right turn lane as subsection 4 of NRS 484B.223 sets forth, whose words are borrowed: NRS-484B-223-4a and NRS-484B-223-4b both quote \"a single right lane to be used only for turning\". That is a st.turn_lane (\"a lane designated only for turning\") of side right, entering i (st.lane_enters), lying on the same highway (st.on_way: \"the public way (a highway region) a structure region lies on\"; st.highway) as the carrier x approached through, and serving x's direction: its designated direction (st.lane_direction) not opposed to that carrier's (drv.road.opposed_directions false), so that a turn lane on the opposing approach of the same way is not read."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[{"span":"e2","id":"int.turn","meaning":"The source's current plan for the road user includes a turn, to either hand, at the target region."}],"compositions":[{"span":"e8","as":"definition","source":"NRS-484B-223-4a","quote":"a single right lane to be used only for turning"},{"span":"e8","as":"definition","source":"NRS-484B-223-4b","quote":"a single right lane to be used only for turning"}],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"x carries ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; at the observation x's right turn in intersection i is recognized: the heading change since x's latest entry into i (drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry(x, i) with step p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph) is at most minus p.turn_recognition_angle there and was not at the observation before; the source declared int.turn for x at i at the observation of that entry (Formula.intent, read through a past operator); and the highway has a right turn lane for x's approach: x entered i from a carrier c with st.lane_enters(c, i) lying on a highway h (st.on_way(c, h)), and some st.turn_lane R of side right enters i (st.lane_enters(R, i)), lies on h (st.on_way(R, h)) and has a designated direction not opposed to c's (drv.road.opposed_directions(R, c) with p.opposed_carriers_cosine false).","obligation":"At the observation of that entry into i (read through a past operator), x's footprint overlaps such a lane R, and at every observation of the path window of length p.turn_approach_length behind the entry (measured in x's path, kin.path_length) at which x occupies a carrier entering i, it occupies that R: both the approach and the turn are made from the right turn lane.","params":["p.turn_recognition_angle","p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph","p.opposed_carriers_cosine","p.turn_approach_length"],"narrowings":[{"span":"e1","why":"'the driver of a vehicle' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"e6","why":"'the approach for the right turn' is read as the stretch of path, of the approach length, just before the entry into the intersection, during which every carrier of the intersection x is on must be the right turn lane; a lane change into the turn lane earlier than that stretch complies.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"x (ru.motor_vehicle) approaches i on a through lane c of highway h whose approach also has a right st.turn_lane R entering i; int.turn is declared for x at i; x enters i from c and turns right beyond p.turn_recognition_angle."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same highway; x, with int.turn declared at i, is on R for the whole approach length before its entry, enters i from R and turns right."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"x, with int.turn declared at i, turns left in i (heading change positive beyond p.turn_recognition_angle)."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x turns right in i from a through lane with int.turn declared, but the source does not record which intersection the turn lane beside it enters, so whether the highway has a right turn lane for this approach is unknown.","masked":["st.lane_enters"]}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.turn_recognition_angle","unit":"deg","value":45,"convention":"Turn recognition: the heading change through an intersection beyond which a passage counts as a turn rather than a straight crossing; half the right angle of a turn at a right-angled junction, leaving room for skewed junctions and lane offsets.","source":"intersection geometry design conventions (AASHTO Green Book)"},{"name":"p.opposed_carriers_cosine","unit":"ratio","value":0.7,"convention":"Direction tolerance: minus the cosine of the narrowest angle between two carriers' designated directions that counts as opposite directions; carriers within about 45 degrees of exactly opposed count.","source":"road-network direction conventions of map data"},{"name":"p.turn_approach_length","unit":"m","value":15.0,"convention":"Turn approach: the distance travelled just before entering an intersection over which a turning vehicle's approach is judged; about two passenger-car lengths, shorter than the storage of a short turn bay.","source":"AASHTO Green Book turn-lane storage practice"}],"gaps":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_400_1_o2","law_refs":["NRS-484B-400-1"],"subject":{"binder":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"e1","text":"If the driver of a vehicle","role":"subject"},{"id":"e2","text":"intends to turn","role":"trigger"},{"id":"e3","text":"at an intersection","role":"trigger"},{"id":"e4","text":"and:","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"e5","text":"The turn is a right turn,","role":"trigger"},{"id":"e6","text":"both the approach for the right turn and the right turn must be made from the right turn lane","role":"sibling"},{"id":"e7","text":"if the highway has a right turn lane","role":"condition"},{"id":"e8","text":"as set forth in subsection 4 of NRS 484B.223 [NRS-484B-223-4a, NRS-484B-223-4b],","role":"reference"},{"id":"e9","text":"or must be made from the extreme right lane.","role":"obligation"}],"elements":[{"span":"e1","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle (\"every device in, upon or by which any person or property is or may be transported or drawn upon a highway\"), claimed by id. 'the driver of' is a role read through the vehicle's controlled motion."},{"span":"e3","atoms":["st.intersection","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region","rel.occupies"],"derived":["drv.motion.entering_region"],"justification":"st.intersection (\"the region where two roadways meet\"), entered by x (drv.motion.entering_region) from the approach carrier whose entrance end is i (st.lane_enters)."},{"span":"e5","atoms":["kin.yaw_rate","rel.occupies"],"derived":["drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry"],"justification":"A right turn: the heading change since x entered i (drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry, \"in degrees, left positive\", from kin.yaw_rate) reaches the turn recognition angle to the right."},{"span":"e7","atoms":["st.highway","st.on_way","st.turn_lane","st.lane_enters","st.lane_direction"],"derived":["drv.road.opposed_directions"],"source_spans":["e8"],"justification":"Read negated here: the 'or' alternative applies where the highway has no right turn lane as subsection 4 of NRS 484B.223 sets forth, borrowing \"a single right lane to be used only for turning\" (NRS-484B-223-4a, NRS-484B-223-4b): no st.turn_lane of side right enters i (st.lane_enters) on the same highway (st.on_way, st.highway) with a designated direction (st.lane_direction) not opposed to x's approach (drv.road.opposed_directions)."},{"span":"e9","atoms":["st.lane","st.lane_adjacency","st.lane_enters","rel.occupies","kin.path_length"],"derived":[],"justification":"The extreme right lane: a st.lane entering i whose ordinal within the carriageway equals the count of lanes in its direction (st.lane_adjacency: \"lane ordinal within the carriageway and the count of lanes in that direction; ordinal 1 is the leftmost lane, looking along the lane's direction\"). The approach and the turn are made from it where x's footprint overlaps it (rel.occupies) at the entry and over the approach length of path before it (.path window, kin.path_length). Lane adjacency is 'not a stand-in' for a marking and is not used as one."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[{"span":"e2","id":"int.turn","meaning":"The source's current plan for the road user includes a turn, to either hand, at the target region."}],"compositions":[{"span":"e8","as":"definition","source":"NRS-484B-223-4a","quote":"a single right lane to be used only for turning"},{"span":"e8","as":"definition","source":"NRS-484B-223-4b","quote":"a single right lane to be used only for turning"}],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"x carries ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; at the observation x's right turn in intersection i is recognized (drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry(x, i) with step p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph at most minus p.turn_recognition_angle there and not at the observation before); int.turn was declared for x at i at the observation of its latest entry into i (read through a past operator); x entered i from a carrier c with st.lane_enters(c, i) on highway h (st.on_way(c, h)); and no st.turn_lane of side right enters i on h with a designated direction not opposed to c's (drv.road.opposed_directions with p.opposed_carriers_cosine).","obligation":"At the observation of that entry into i (read through a past operator), x's footprint overlaps a st.lane L that enters i (st.lane_enters(L, i)), lies on h, has a designated direction not opposed to c's, and whose st.lane_adjacency ordinal equals its lane count (the rightmost lane looking along its direction); and at every observation of the path window of length p.turn_approach_length behind the entry (kin.path_length) at which x occupies a carrier entering i, it occupies that L.","params":["p.turn_recognition_angle","p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph","p.opposed_carriers_cosine","p.turn_approach_length"],"narrowings":[{"span":"e1","why":"'the driver of a vehicle' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"e9","why":"'the extreme right lane' is read as the lane whose ordinal equals the count of lanes in its direction on the approach; the approach is the stretch of path of the approach length before the entry. An approach with no lanes mapped has no such lane, and the duty is not decided there.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"x (ru.motor_vehicle) approaches i on a two-lane approach with no right turn lane, in the lane of ordinal one of two; int.turn is declared at i; x turns right from that lane."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same approach; x is in the lane whose ordinal equals the lane count for the whole approach length, enters i from it and turns right."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The approach has a right st.turn_lane entering i on the same highway in x's direction; x turns right (NRS_484B_400_1_o1 governs that case)."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x turns right from a two-lane approach with no right turn lane, with int.turn declared, but the source does not observe lane ordinals and counts.","masked":["st.lane_adjacency"]}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.turn_recognition_angle","unit":"deg","value":45,"convention":"Turn recognition: the heading change through an intersection beyond which a passage counts as a turn rather than a straight crossing; half the right angle of a turn at a right-angled junction, leaving room for skewed junctions and lane offsets.","source":"intersection geometry design conventions (AASHTO Green Book)"},{"name":"p.opposed_carriers_cosine","unit":"ratio","value":0.7,"convention":"Direction tolerance: minus the cosine of the narrowest angle between two carriers' designated directions that counts as opposite directions; carriers within about 45 degrees of exactly opposed count.","source":"road-network direction conventions of map data"},{"name":"p.turn_approach_length","unit":"m","value":15.0,"convention":"Turn approach: the distance travelled just before entering an intersection over which a turning vehicle's approach is judged; about two passenger-car lengths, shorter than the storage of a short turn bay.","source":"AASHTO Green Book turn-lane storage practice"}],"gaps":[]}
{"concept_id":"drv.motion.veering_left","kind":"formula","contract":"Road user x departs to the left of a travel carrier's designated direction at the observation: it moves forward along the carrier while its velocity points to the left of the carrier's direction by more than a tolerance. It holds where x is moving (drv.motion.moving with speed_floor), the component of its velocity (kin.velocity, m/s, world frame) along the carrier's designated direction (st.lane_direction, read normalised) is positive, and the cross product of that direction with the velocity, left positive, exceeds sine_tolerance times x's speed (kin.speed): the sine of the angle from the designated direction to the velocity is above sine_tolerance. Unknown where the carrier carries no designated direction. Not denoted: x's heading (a body may point across a carrier while moving along it), motion against the carrier's direction, x being on the carrier (the caller states occupancy), a signal, or how far x has moved sideways.","definition":null,"args":[{"name":"x","sort":"track"},{"name":"c","sort":"region"}],"params":[{"name":"speed_floor","unit":"m/s","meaning":"the source's speed resolution, below which a reading counts as no motion"},{"name":"sine_tolerance","unit":"ratio","meaning":"the sine of the angle between the velocity and the designated direction above which the motion counts as departing to one side rather than tracking the carrier"}],"elements":[{"span":"x is moving (drv.motion.moving with speed_floor)","atoms":[],"concepts":["drv.motion.moving"],"justification":"drv.motion.moving: \"A road user is in motion at the observation: its speed exceeds speed_floor\"."},{"span":"its velocity (kin.velocity, m/s, world frame)","atoms":["kin.velocity"],"concepts":[],"justification":"kin.velocity: \"velocity vector\", m/s, world frame; the direction of motion, not the heading."},{"span":"the carrier's designated direction (st.lane_direction, read normalised)","atoms":["st.lane_direction"],"concepts":[],"justification":"st.lane_direction: \"direction of travel designated for a structure a vehicle travels in\", read normalised; unknown where the carrier carries none."},{"span":"x's speed (kin.speed)","atoms":["kin.speed"],"concepts":[],"justification":"kin.speed: \"magnitude of velocity\"; the cross product is compared with the tolerance times the speed, so no division by a measurement."}],"residues":[],"scenarios":[{"name":"holds","expected":"compliant","narrative":"x moves along lane c with its velocity turned to the left of c's designated direction by more than the angle whose sine is sine_tolerance, as at the start of a lane change to the left."},{"name":"fails","expected":"violated","narrative":"x moves along lane c with its velocity parallel to c's designated direction."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x moves to the left across lane c, but c's designated direction is not observed.","masked":["st.lane_direction"]}],"used_by":["NRS_484B_413_2"],"supersedes":null}
{"concept_id":"drv.motion.veering_right","kind":"formula","contract":"Road user x departs to the right of a travel carrier's designated direction at the observation: it moves forward along the carrier while its velocity points to the right of the carrier's direction by more than a tolerance. It holds where x is moving (drv.motion.moving with speed_floor), the component of its velocity (kin.velocity, m/s, world frame) along the carrier's designated direction (st.lane_direction, read normalised) is positive, and the cross product of that direction with the velocity, left positive, is below minus sine_tolerance times x's speed (kin.speed): the sine of the angle from the designated direction to the velocity is below minus sine_tolerance. Unknown where the carrier carries no designated direction. Not denoted: x's heading (a body may point across a carrier while moving along it), motion against the carrier's direction, x being on the carrier (the caller states occupancy), a signal, or how far x has moved sideways.","definition":null,"args":[{"name":"x","sort":"track"},{"name":"c","sort":"region"}],"params":[{"name":"speed_floor","unit":"m/s","meaning":"the source's speed resolution, below which a reading counts as no motion"},{"name":"sine_tolerance","unit":"ratio","meaning":"the sine of the angle between the velocity and the designated direction above which the motion counts as departing to one side rather than tracking the carrier"}],"elements":[{"span":"x is moving (drv.motion.moving with speed_floor)","atoms":[],"concepts":["drv.motion.moving"],"justification":"drv.motion.moving: \"A road user is in motion at the observation: its speed exceeds speed_floor\"."},{"span":"its velocity (kin.velocity, m/s, world frame)","atoms":["kin.velocity"],"concepts":[],"justification":"kin.velocity: \"velocity vector\", m/s, world frame; the direction of motion, not the heading."},{"span":"the carrier's designated direction (st.lane_direction, read normalised)","atoms":["st.lane_direction"],"concepts":[],"justification":"st.lane_direction: \"direction of travel designated for a structure a vehicle travels in\", read normalised; unknown where the carrier carries none."},{"span":"x's speed (kin.speed)","atoms":["kin.speed"],"concepts":[],"justification":"kin.speed: \"magnitude of velocity\"; the cross product is compared with the tolerance times the speed, so no division by a measurement."}],"residues":[],"scenarios":[{"name":"holds","expected":"compliant","narrative":"x moves along lane c with its velocity turned to the right of c's designated direction by more than the angle whose sine is sine_tolerance, as at the start of a turn into a side street on the right."},{"name":"fails","expected":"violated","narrative":"x moves along lane c with its velocity parallel to c's designated direction."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x moves to the right across lane c, but c's designated direction is not observed.","masked":["st.lane_direction"]}],"used_by":["NRS_484B_413_2"],"supersedes":null}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_413_2","law_refs":["NRS-484B-413-2"],"subject":{"binder":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"f1","text":"A signal of intention to turn right or left, or otherwise turn","role":"obligation"},{"id":"f2","text":"a vehicle","role":"subject"},{"id":"f3","text":"from a direct course,","role":"trigger"},{"id":"f4","text":"shall be given continuously during not less than the last 100 feet traveled","role":"obligation"},{"id":"f5","text":"in a business or residential district","role":"condition"},{"id":"f6","text":"and not less than the last 300 feet traveled","role":"obligation"},{"id":"f7","text":"in any other area","role":"condition"},{"id":"f8","text":"prior to changing the course","role":"trigger"},{"id":"f9","text":"of a vehicle.","role":"subject"},{"id":"f10","text":"This rule shall be observed, regardless of the weather.","role":"condition"}],"elements":[{"span":"f1","atoms":["sig.turn_indicator","sig.hand_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"A signal of intention to turn is the signal itself, not a declared intention (the ontology: \"a signal 'of intention' is the signal\"): sig.turn_indicator (\"the turn indicator state ∈ {off, left, right}\") or sig.hand_signal (\"a driver's or rider's arm signal; meaning ∈ {no_signal, left, right, stop_or_slow, re_enter}\") showing the side of the change of course. sig.turn_indicator is 'not a stand-in' for the turn itself; the turn is read separately in spans f3 and f8."},{"span":"f2","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle (\"every device in, upon or by which any person or property is or may be transported or drawn upon a highway\"), claimed by id."},{"span":"f3","atoms":["st.lane_direction","kin.velocity","kin.speed","rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":["drv.motion.veering_left","drv.motion.veering_right"],"justification":"A direct course is travel along the designated direction of the carrier x occupies (rel.occupies a st.travel_region carrying st.lane_direction); turning from it is x's velocity departing to one side of that direction, the proposed concepts drv.motion.veering_left and drv.motion.veering_right (\"it moves forward along the carrier while its velocity points to the left [right] of the carrier's direction by more than a tolerance\"). Following a bend of the carrier is not a departure, since the designated direction bends with it."},{"span":"f4","atoms":["kin.path_length","sig.turn_indicator","sig.hand_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"'given continuously during not less than the last 100 feet traveled' is a window measured in distance travelled (a .path window, which reads kin.path_length: \"distance travelled along the body's path since the start of the trace, monotone\") at every observation of which the signal of the side of the departure is shown; the figure is the law's literal."},{"span":"f6","atoms":["kin.path_length"],"derived":[],"justification":"The same .path window (kin.path_length) with the law's other literal, selected where the place is not in a business or residence district."},{"span":"f8","atoms":["rel.occupies"],"derived":["drv.motion.veering_left","drv.motion.veering_right"],"justification":"Changing the course is the observation at which a departure to one side begins: drv.motion.veering_left or drv.motion.veering_right holds for a carrier x occupies (rel.occupies) and held for none at the observation before. The window of span f4 ends there."},{"span":"f9","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"The vehicle whose course changes: the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, the subject x."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[{"span":"f5","id":"asm.within_business_or_residence_district","meaning":"The place of the observation lies inside a business district or a residence district declared for the map or the trace."},{"span":"f7","id":"asm.within_business_or_residence_district","meaning":"The place of the observation lies inside a business district or a residence district declared for the map or the trace."}],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[{"span":"f10","why":"The duty is the same in every weather: the words exclude no weather and add no condition, so no environment atom is read.","scope":"none"}],"binders":[{"name":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"x carries ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle and at the observation begins a change of course: for some travel region c that x occupies (rel.occupies), drv.motion.veering_left(x, c) or drv.motion.veering_right(x, c) (with p.speed_resolution and p.course_departure_sine) holds there, and at the observation before neither held for any region x occupied.","obligation":"For a departure to the left, x showed a left signal (sig.turn_indicator left, or sig.hand_signal left) at every observation of the window behind the observation measured in x's distance travelled (.path, kin.path_length), whose length is the literal of span f4 where asm.within_business_or_residence_district holds at the observation and the literal of span f6 where it does not (a bound selected by the condition); for a departure to the right, the right signal likewise. A departure to both sides at once owes the signal of either.","params":["p.speed_resolution","p.course_departure_sine"],"narrowings":[{"span":"f1","why":"'otherwise turn a vehicle from a direct course' is read as the velocity departing to one side of the designated direction of the carrier the vehicle occupies, on lanes, roadways and other carriers that carry a direction; a turn begun where the vehicle occupies only an intersection, which carries no direction, is not recognized.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"x (ru.motor_vehicle) on a rural road (asm.within_business_or_residence_district declared false) begins a lane change to the left; its sig.turn_indicator showed left only over a path shorter than the literal of span f6 before the departure began, off before that."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same rural lane change; sig.turn_indicator showed left at every observation of a path longer than the literal of span f6 before the departure."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"x drives along its lane following its designated direction, never departing to either side."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x begins a lane change to the left, but the source observes neither its turn indicator nor any arm signal.","masked":["sig.turn_indicator","sig.hand_signal"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"compliant","narrative":"In a declared business district x begins a departure to the right with sig.turn_indicator right shown over a path longer than the literal of span f4 but shorter than that of span f6."},{"name":"branch_2","expected":"violated","narrative":"x begins a departure to the right with sig.turn_indicator left shown over the whole window: the signal is not of the side of the change."}],"literals":[{"span":"f4","text":"100 feet","value":100,"unit":"ft"},{"span":"f6","text":"300 feet","value":300,"unit":"ft"}],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.speed_resolution","unit":"m/s","value":0.2,"convention":"Sensor resolution: the smallest speed the acquisition standard separates from standstill; a speed at or below it counts as no motion.","source":"speed resolution of the carla_scene_graph acquisition standard"},{"name":"p.course_departure_sine","unit":"ratio","value":0.05,"convention":"Course-departure tolerance: the sine of the angle between a road user's velocity and its carrier's designated direction beyond which it counts as leaving its direct course rather than tracking the carrier; about three degrees, above heading noise and lane-keeping drift.","source":"lane-change onset detection practice in naturalistic driving studies"}],"gaps":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_440_1_o1","law_refs":["NRS-484B-440-1"],"subject":{"binder":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"g1","text":"Upon any highway","role":"trigger"},{"id":"g2","text":"outside of a business or residence district","role":"condition"},{"id":"g3","text":"no person shall stop, park or leave standing","role":"obligation"},{"id":"g4","text":"any vehicle, whether attended or unattended,","role":"subject"},{"id":"g5","text":"upon the paved or main-traveled part of the highway","role":"obligation"},{"id":"g6","text":"when it is practicable to stop, park or so leave such vehicle off such part of the highway,","role":"standard"},{"id":"g7","text":"but in every event","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"g8","text":"an unobstructed width of the highway","role":"sibling"},{"id":"g9","text":"opposite a standing vehicle","role":"sibling"},{"id":"g10","text":"shall be left for the free passage of other vehicles","role":"sibling"},{"id":"g11","text":"and","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"g12","text":"a clear view of such stopped vehicles shall be available from a distance of 200 feet in each direction upon such highway.","role":"sibling"},{"id":"g13","text":"This section shall not apply to the driver of any vehicle which is disabled while on the paved or main-traveled portion of a highway in such manner and to such extent that it is impossible to avoid stopping and temporarily leaving such disabled vehicle in such position.","role":"exception"}],"elements":[{"span":"g1","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.highway"],"derived":[],"justification":"st.highway: \"the entire public way between its boundary lines, including sidewalks and shoulders\" (DEF-NRS-484A-095, \"the entire width between the boundary lines of every way\"); x is upon it where its footprint overlaps it (rel.occupies)."},{"span":"g3","atoms":["kin.speed","rel.ahead_behind_in_lane","rel.surface_gap","dev.human_direction","dev.traffic_signal","dev.stop_sign","dev.governs","rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":["drv.motion.halted"],"justification":"'stop', prohibited here, takes DEF-NRS-484A-260 (\"any halting, even momentarily, of a vehicle, whether occupied or not, except when necessary to avoid conflict with other traffic or in compliance with the directions of a police officer or official traffic-control device\"); 'park' (DEF-NRS-484A-155, \"the standing of a vehicle\") and 'leave standing' (DEF-NRS-484A-250, \"the halting of a vehicle\") are halts too. The halt is drv.motion.halted (\"speed ... at or below speed_floor ... with no minimum duration\", kin.speed), which observes any halting, even momentary. The definition's exclusions are carried beside it: a halt behind another road user ahead in the same lane (rel.ahead_behind_in_lane) within the conflict standoff gap (rel.surface_gap) avoids a conflict; a halt while a police officer's stop direction (dev.human_direction, indication stop) or a signal showing a red indication or a stop sign (dev.traffic_signal, dev.stop_sign) governs (dev.governs) the travel region x occupies is in compliance with directions. Purposes of parking and standing (loading, passengers) are not observable and are read through the halt (observable_reading purpose)."},{"span":"g4","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, claimed by id; 'whether attended or unattended' excludes no member."},{"span":"g5","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.roadway"],"derived":[],"justification":"The paved or main-traveled part of the highway is the st.roadway (\"the part of a highway improved for vehicular traffic, excluding shoulder\"); x halts upon it where its footprint overlaps it (rel.occupies). st.roadway is 'not a stand-in' for the sidewalk, and the shoulder is off it."},{"span":"g13","atoms":["kin.engine_running","sig.hazard","rel.occupies","st.roadway"],"derived":[],"justification":"A vehicle disabled on the roadway so that stopping cannot be avoided is read through its nearest observables, the same as the earlier mapping of 'a disabled vehicle' in this iteration: its engine or motor not running, so that propulsion is unavailable (kin.engine_running: \"the vehicle's engine or motor is running, so that propulsion is available\", false), with its hazard lamps flashing (sig.hazard: \"both indicators flashing together\"), while it occupies the roadway (rel.occupies, st.roadway). kin.engine_running is 'not a stand-in' for motion or a halt, and is not used as either; the gap records that the disability itself has no atom."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"g6","standard":"practicable to stop, park or so leave such vehicle off such part of the highway","concepts":["st.shoulder","st.region_geometry"],"params":["p.offroad_stop_reach"],"convention":"Off-road stopping convention: moving off the main-traveled part is practicable where a shoulder lies within the reach of a short lateral move from the halted vehicle's body; the ground distance from the body to the nearest shoulder is the measured magnitude compared with the reach.","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[{"span":"g2","id":"asm.within_business_or_residence_district","meaning":"The place of the observation lies inside a business district or a residence district declared for the map or the trace."}],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"x carries ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; at the observation x's footprint overlaps a st.highway (rel.occupies) and asm.within_business_or_residence_district does not hold; and x is not disabled there: not (kin.engine_running false and sig.hazard on while x occupies a st.roadway).","obligation":"It is not the case that, at the observation, x is halted (drv.motion.halted with p.speed_resolution) with its footprint overlapping a st.roadway, while some st.shoulder lies within p.offroad_stop_reach of x's body (st.region_geometry distance), unless the halt falls under the exclusions of the defined 'stop': some other road user is ahead of x in the same lane (rel.ahead_behind_in_lane) with a surface gap (rel.surface_gap) at most p.stopping_conflict_gap, or a dev.human_direction with indication stop, a dev.traffic_signal displaying circular_red, a red_arrow or flashing_red, or a dev.stop_sign governs (dev.governs) a travel region x occupies.","params":["p.speed_resolution","p.offroad_stop_reach","p.stopping_conflict_gap"],"narrowings":[{"span":"g3","why":"'stop, park or leave standing' are read through the halt itself; the purposes that set parking and standing apart (loading, receiving passengers) are not observable, and every halt is a stop under the definition that applies, so none is lost.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"purpose"},{"span":"g5","why":"'the paved or main-traveled part of the highway' is read as the roadway; a paved shoulder is off it.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"x (ru.motor_vehicle) on a rural highway (asm.within_business_or_residence_district declared false) halts with its footprint on the st.roadway, engine running, no hazard lamps, nothing ahead and no device governing; a st.shoulder lies within p.offroad_stop_reach of its body."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"x halts on the roadway of a rural bridge with no shoulder within p.offroad_stop_reach; no other road user is in the scene."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"x halts on the roadway in a declared residence district (asm.within_business_or_residence_district true)."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x halts on the rural roadway beside a mapped shoulder, but the source maps regions without their outline, so the distance to the shoulder is unknown.","masked":["st.region_geometry"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"x halts on the rural roadway with its engine not running and its hazard lamps flashing: the disabled-vehicle exception applies."},{"name":"branch_2","expected":"compliant","narrative":"x halts on the rural roadway behind a halted truck ahead in its lane at a surface gap below p.stopping_conflict_gap, a shoulder within reach: the halt avoids a conflict and is no prohibited stop."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.speed_resolution","unit":"m/s","value":0.2,"convention":"Sensor resolution: the smallest speed the acquisition standard separates from standstill; a speed at or below it counts as no motion.","source":"speed resolution of the carla_scene_graph acquisition standard"},{"name":"p.offroad_stop_reach","unit":"m","value":5.0,"convention":"Off-road stopping reach: the ground distance from a halted vehicle's body to a shoulder within which moving off the main-traveled part counts as practicable; about one lane width of lateral movement.","source":"AASHTO Green Book lane and shoulder widths"},{"name":"p.stopping_conflict_gap","unit":"m","value":5.0,"convention":"Conflict standoff: the largest surface gap from a halted road user's body to another road user ahead of it at which the halt counts as necessary to avoid a conflict; a queue spacing at standstill.","source":"queue spacing at standstill (traffic-flow jam-density conventions)"}],"gaps":[{"span":"g13","kind":"atom","proposal":"`ru.disabled` | a vehicle that cannot proceed under its own power, by a mechanical failure, crash damage or a flat tyre, as the source records it **Not a stand-in for:** a vehicle parked with its engine off, or one showing hazard lamps | general — decides whether moving the vehicle off the roadway can be carried out, which the disabled-vehicle exception turns on","nearest":["kin.engine_running","sig.hazard"]}]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_440_1_o2","law_refs":["NRS-484B-440-1"],"subject":{"binder":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"g1","text":"Upon any highway","role":"trigger"},{"id":"g2","text":"outside of a business or residence district","role":"condition"},{"id":"g3","text":"no person shall stop, park or leave standing","role":"sibling"},{"id":"g4","text":"any vehicle, whether attended or unattended,","role":"subject"},{"id":"g5","text":"upon the paved or main-traveled part of the highway","role":"trigger"},{"id":"g6","text":"when it is practicable to stop, park or so leave such vehicle off such part of the highway,","role":"sibling"},{"id":"g7","text":"but in every event","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"g8","text":"an unobstructed width of the highway","role":"obligation"},{"id":"g9","text":"opposite a standing vehicle","role":"trigger"},{"id":"g10","text":"shall be left for the free passage of other vehicles","role":"standard"},{"id":"g11","text":"and","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"g12","text":"a clear view of such stopped vehicles shall be available from a distance of 200 feet in each direction upon such highway.","role":"sibling"},{"id":"g13","text":"This section shall not apply to the driver of any vehicle which is disabled while on the paved or main-traveled portion of a highway in such manner and to such extent that it is impossible to avoid stopping and temporarily leaving such disabled vehicle in such position.","role":"exception"}],"elements":[{"span":"g1","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.highway"],"derived":[],"justification":"st.highway: \"the entire public way between its boundary lines, including sidewalks and shoulders\"; x is upon it where its footprint overlaps it (rel.occupies)."},{"span":"g4","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, claimed by id; 'whether attended or unattended' excludes no member."},{"span":"g5","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.roadway"],"derived":[],"justification":"The standing vehicles 'in every event' are those of the first clause, upon the paved or main-traveled part: the st.roadway (\"the part of a highway improved for vehicular traffic, excluding shoulder\"), overlapped by x's footprint (rel.occupies)."},{"span":"g8","atoms":["st.lane","st.on_way","st.highway","rel.occupies","st.region_geometry"],"derived":[],"justification":"A width of the highway opposite the vehicle is a lane beside it: a st.lane (\"a longitudinal strip of roadway for one line of vehicles\") on the same highway (st.on_way, st.highway) whose ground distance from x's body (st.region_geometry) is at most the beside reach, so that a lane segment far along the way is not read, and that x's footprint does not overlap (rel.occupies). Unobstructed: no other halted road user beside x (its footprint overlapping x along x's heading) occupies it."},{"span":"g9","atoms":["kin.speed","rel.longitudinal_overlap"],"derived":["drv.motion.halted"],"justification":"'a standing vehicle' (DEF-NRS-484A-250, \"the halting of a vehicle, whether occupied or not\") is x halted (drv.motion.halted, kin.speed at or below the resolution); its purpose is not observable (observable_reading purpose). Opposite it is the stretch alongside its body: another halted road user is opposite where their footprints overlap along x's heading (rel.longitudinal_overlap positive), a projection, 'not' a contact or a distance."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"g10","standard":"an unobstructed width left for the free passage of other vehicles","concepts":["st.lane_width","rel.longitudinal_overlap","drv.motion.halted"],"params":["p.free_passage_width","p.opposite_lane_reach","p.speed_resolution"],"convention":"Free-passage convention: the width left for passage is a lane beside the standing vehicle, not overlapped by it and not taken by another halted road user alongside it, whose measured width (st.lane_width) is at least a design passenger-car width plus lateral clearance.","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[{"span":"g2","id":"asm.within_business_or_residence_district","meaning":"The place of the observation lies inside a business district or a residence district declared for the map or the trace."}],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"x carries ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; at the observation x is halted (drv.motion.halted with p.speed_resolution) with its footprint overlapping a st.roadway of a st.highway h (rel.occupies, st.on_way); asm.within_business_or_residence_district does not hold; and x is not disabled there: not (kin.engine_running false and sig.hazard on).","obligation":"Some st.lane L on h (st.on_way(L, h)) that x's footprint does not overlap, within p.opposite_lane_reach of x's body (st.region_geometry distance), has st.lane_width at least p.free_passage_width, and no road user other than x that is halted (drv.motion.halted with p.speed_resolution) and overlaps x along x's heading (rel.longitudinal_overlap positive) occupies L.","params":["p.speed_resolution","p.free_passage_width","p.opposite_lane_reach"],"narrowings":[{"span":"g8","why":"'an unobstructed width of the highway' is read as a whole lane beside the vehicle, free of halted road users alongside it; a part-lane, a shoulder, or an obstruction that is not a road user (st.obstruction) is not counted.","kind":"reading"},{"span":"g9","why":"'a standing vehicle' is read through the halt; whether it is receiving or discharging passengers is not observable.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"purpose"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"On a rural two-lane highway x (ru.motor_vehicle) halts in one lane while another vehicle halts in the other lane alongside it (rel.longitudinal_overlap positive): no lane beside x is free."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"x halts in one lane of a rural two-lane highway; the other lane, within p.opposite_lane_reach, has st.lane_width above p.free_passage_width and no other road user is in the scene."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"x drives along the rural roadway without halting."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x halts in one lane of a rural two-lane highway with the other lane empty, but the source does not observe lane widths.","masked":["st.lane_width"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"x halts with its engine not running and its hazard lamps flashing: the disabled-vehicle exception applies."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.speed_resolution","unit":"m/s","value":0.2,"convention":"Sensor resolution: the smallest speed the acquisition standard separates from standstill; a speed at or below it counts as no motion.","source":"speed resolution of the carla_scene_graph acquisition standard"},{"name":"p.free_passage_width","unit":"m","value":3.0,"convention":"Free-passage width: the smallest width of an unoccupied lane beside a standing vehicle that lets another vehicle pass; a design passenger-car width plus lateral clearance.","source":"AASHTO Green Book design-vehicle widths and lane widths"},{"name":"p.opposite_lane_reach","unit":"m","value":1.0,"convention":"Beside reach: the largest ground distance from a standing vehicle's body to a lane within which the lane counts as opposite the vehicle; covers the lateral gap between the body and the next lane's edge.","source":"lane-keeping offset conventions"}],"gaps":[{"span":"g13","kind":"atom","proposal":"`ru.disabled` | a vehicle that cannot proceed under its own power, by a mechanical failure, crash damage or a flat tyre, as the source records it **Not a stand-in for:** a vehicle parked with its engine off, or one showing hazard lamps | general — decides whether moving the vehicle off the roadway can be carried out, which the disabled-vehicle exception turns on","nearest":["kin.engine_running","sig.hazard"]}]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_440_1_o3","law_refs":["NRS-484B-440-1"],"subject":{"binder":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"g1","text":"Upon any highway","role":"trigger"},{"id":"g2","text":"outside of a business or residence district","role":"condition"},{"id":"g3","text":"no person shall stop, park or leave standing","role":"sibling"},{"id":"g4","text":"any vehicle, whether attended or unattended,","role":"subject"},{"id":"g5","text":"upon the paved or main-traveled part of the highway","role":"trigger"},{"id":"g6","text":"when it is practicable to stop, park or so leave such vehicle off such part of the highway,","role":"sibling"},{"id":"g7","text":"but in every event","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"g8","text":"an unobstructed width of the highway","role":"sibling"},{"id":"g9","text":"opposite a standing vehicle","role":"sibling"},{"id":"g10","text":"shall be left for the free passage of other vehicles","role":"sibling"},{"id":"g11","text":"and","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"g12","text":"a clear view of such stopped vehicles shall be available from a distance of 200 feet in each direction upon such highway.","role":"obligation"},{"id":"g13","text":"This section shall not apply to the driver of any vehicle which is disabled while on the paved or main-traveled portion of a highway in such manner and to such extent that it is impossible to avoid stopping and temporarily leaving such disabled vehicle in such position.","role":"exception"}],"elements":[{"span":"g1","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.highway"],"derived":[],"justification":"st.highway: \"the entire public way between its boundary lines, including sidewalks and shoulders\"; x is upon it where its footprint overlaps it (rel.occupies)."},{"span":"g4","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, claimed by id; 'whether attended or unattended' excludes no member."},{"span":"g5","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.roadway"],"derived":[],"justification":"'such stopped vehicles' are those of the first clause, upon the paved or main-traveled part: the st.roadway (\"the part of a highway improved for vehicular traffic, excluding shoulder\"), overlapped by x's footprint (rel.occupies)."},{"span":"g12","atoms":["st.sight_distance","kin.speed"],"derived":["drv.motion.halted"],"justification":"A stopped vehicle is x halted (drv.motion.halted, kin.speed at or below the resolution); the stop is not a prohibited one here, so the definition of stopping when prohibited adds no exclusion. A clear view of it from a distance along the highway is st.sight_distance at its place: \"the distance along the road within which a vehicle at a point and another vehicle on the road could see each other ... both the view of approaching traffic from that point and its being seen by drivers approaching it\"; it is at least the law's literal. It is 'not a stand-in' for whether an actual road user saw x (rel.visible), and is not used as one."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[{"span":"g2","id":"asm.within_business_or_residence_district","meaning":"The place of the observation lies inside a business district or a residence district declared for the map or the trace."}],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"x carries ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; at the observation x is halted (drv.motion.halted with p.speed_resolution) with its footprint overlapping a st.roadway of a st.highway (rel.occupies); asm.within_business_or_residence_district does not hold; and x is not disabled there: not (kin.engine_running false and sig.hazard on).","obligation":"The sight distance at x's place (st.sight_distance) is at least the literal of span g12.","params":["p.speed_resolution"],"narrowings":[{"span":"g12","why":"'in each direction' is read through the sight distance the source reports for the place, which states both the view from it and its being seen along the road without separating the two directions of the way.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"x (ru.motor_vehicle) halts on the roadway of a rural highway just beyond a crest, where st.sight_distance is below the literal of span g12."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"x halts on a straight, level rural roadway where st.sight_distance is well above the literal."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"x drives along the rural roadway without halting."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x halts on the rural roadway near a crest, but the source does not supply sight distances.","masked":["st.sight_distance"]}],"literals":[{"span":"g12","text":"200 feet","value":200,"unit":"ft"}],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.speed_resolution","unit":"m/s","value":0.2,"convention":"Sensor resolution: the smallest speed the acquisition standard separates from standstill; a speed at or below it counts as no motion.","source":"speed resolution of the carla_scene_graph acquisition standard"}],"gaps":[{"span":"g13","kind":"atom","proposal":"`ru.disabled` | a vehicle that cannot proceed under its own power, by a mechanical failure, crash damage or a flat tyre, as the source records it **Not a stand-in for:** a vehicle parked with its engine off, or one showing hazard lamps | general — decides whether moving the vehicle off the roadway can be carried out, which the disabled-vehicle exception turns on","nearest":["kin.engine_running","sig.hazard"]}]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_450_1c","law_refs":["NRS-484B-450-1c"],"subject":{"binder":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"h1","text":"A person shall not stop, stand or park","role":"obligation"},{"id":"h2","text":"a vehicle,","role":"subject"},{"id":"h3","text":"except when necessary to avoid conflict with","role":"standard"},{"id":"h4","text":"other traffic","role":"exception"},{"id":"h5","text":"or in compliance with law","role":"exception"},{"id":"h6","text":"or the directions of a police officer or official traffic-control device,","role":"exception"},{"id":"h7","text":"in any of the following places:","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"h8","text":"Within an intersection.","role":"trigger"}],"elements":[{"span":"h1","atoms":["kin.speed"],"derived":["drv.motion.halted"],"justification":"'stop', prohibited here, takes DEF-NRS-484A-260 (\"any halting, even momentarily, of a vehicle, whether occupied or not\"), whose exclusions the law's own spans h3 to h6 restate; 'stand' (DEF-NRS-484A-250, \"the halting of a vehicle\") and 'park' (DEF-NRS-484A-155, \"the standing of a vehicle\") are halts too. The halt is drv.motion.halted (kin.speed at or below the resolution, \"with no minimum duration\"), observing any halting, even momentary. 'A person' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion (observable_reading agency); the purposes setting parking and standing apart are read through the halt (observable_reading purpose)."},{"span":"h2","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, claimed by id."},{"span":"h4","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic"],"derived":[],"justification":"'other traffic' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic (\"pedestrians, ridden or herded animals, vehicles and other conveyances\"), every member other than x."},{"span":"h5","atoms":["ru.emergency_vehicle","sig.warning_lamp","sig.siren"],"derived":[],"justification":"A halt in compliance with law is a halt some rule requires. The nearest observables are those of the commonest such halt inside an intersection, yielding to an emergency vehicle showing its warning lamps or sounding its siren (ru.emergency_vehicle with sig.warning_lamp flashing or rotating, or sig.siren); ru.emergency_vehicle is 'not a stand-in' for a responding vehicle, which is why its lamp or siren is read. The gap records that no operator reads whether any rule requires the halt."},{"span":"h6","atoms":["dev.human_direction","dev.traffic_signal","dev.stop_sign","dev.governs","rel.occupies","st.travel_region","st.lane_enters","st.intersection"],"derived":[],"justification":"The directions of a police officer: dev.human_direction (\"a person directing traffic and the direction given; role ∈ {police_officer, ...}; indication ∈ {stop, ...}\") with role police_officer and indication stop; of an official traffic-control device: a dev.traffic_signal displaying circular_red, a red_arrow or flashing_red, or a dev.stop_sign; either governing (dev.governs) the intersection x occupies or the carrier it entered through (st.lane_enters, rel.occupies). The device's presence is the evidence of its official status (observable_reading status)."},{"span":"h8","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.intersection"],"derived":[],"justification":"Within an intersection: x's footprint overlaps (rel.occupies) a st.intersection (\"the region where two roadways meet\"; DEF-NRS-484A-105). st.intersection is 'not a stand-in' for a crosswalk or a stop line, which are not read."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"h3","standard":"necessary to avoid conflict","concepts":["rel.bearing","rel.surface_gap"],"params":["p.stopping_conflict_gap"],"convention":"Conflict-standoff convention: a halt is necessary to avoid a conflict where another member of traffic lies ahead of the halted vehicle (the longitudinal component of rel.bearing positive, in the vehicle's frame) at a surface gap no greater than a queue spacing at standstill; the measured gap is compared with the bound.","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"x carries ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle and at the observation its footprint overlaps an intersection i (rel.occupies, st.intersection).","obligation":"It is not the case that x is halted (drv.motion.halted with p.speed_resolution) at the observation, unless: some road user other than x carrying ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic lies ahead of x (rel.bearing longitudinal component positive) at a surface gap (rel.surface_gap) at most p.stopping_conflict_gap; or a ru.emergency_vehicle showing sig.warning_lamp flashing or rotating or sounding sig.siren is in the scene; or a dev.human_direction of role police_officer with indication stop, a dev.traffic_signal displaying circular_red, a red_arrow or flashing_red, or a dev.stop_sign governs (dev.governs) i or the carrier x entered i through.","params":["p.speed_resolution","p.stopping_conflict_gap"],"narrowings":[{"span":"h1","why":"'A person' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion; the purposes that set standing and parking apart from stopping are not observable and every halt is read as a stop.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"h6","why":"'official' is read through the device's presence on the road.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"status"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"x (ru.motor_vehicle) halts inside intersection i with nothing ahead of it, no emergency vehicle in the scene and no device or officer directing a stop."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"x crosses i without halting; no other road user is in the scene."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"x halts in a lane away from any intersection."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x halts at the edge of i, but the source does not observe whether its footprint overlaps i.","masked":["rel.occupies"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"compliant","narrative":"x halts inside i behind a halted car ahead of it at a surface gap below p.stopping_conflict_gap."},{"name":"branch_2","expected":"compliant","narrative":"x halts inside i while a dev.human_direction of role police_officer with indication stop governs i."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.speed_resolution","unit":"m/s","value":0.2,"convention":"Sensor resolution: the smallest speed the acquisition standard separates from standstill; a speed at or below it counts as no motion.","source":"speed resolution of the carla_scene_graph acquisition standard"},{"name":"p.stopping_conflict_gap","unit":"m","value":5.0,"convention":"Conflict standoff: the largest surface gap from a halted road user's body to another road user ahead of it at which the halt counts as necessary to avoid a conflict; a queue spacing at standstill.","source":"queue spacing at standstill (traffic-flow jam-density conventions)"}],"gaps":[{"span":"h5","kind":"operator","proposal":"`Formula.haltRequired (subject)` — true at an observation where some rule of the set, engaged for the subject there, is complied with only if the subject is halted; decides whether a halt was made in compliance with law, the action the law requires, which the exception 'in compliance with law' turns on and which no single composed rule names","nearest":["ru.emergency_vehicle","sig.warning_lamp","sig.siren"]}]}

