{"concept_id":"drv.interaction.overtaking_alongside","kind":"formula","contract":"Road user x is overtaking road user y alongside at the observation: the side-by-side phase of an overtaking, on either side of y. It holds where their headings are aligned (rel.same_direction, with aligned_cosine as the relation's tolerance), their bodies overlap along x's heading (rel.longitudinal_overlap positive), and x's speed exceeds y's (kin.speed, m/s) by more than speed_margin, the speed resolution below which the two count as keeping pace. Either side of y counts. Not denoted: the approach from behind or the return ahead of y, the side on which x passes, where either body is on the road, a lane change, contact, or the clearance between the bodies.","definition":null,"args":[{"name":"x","sort":"track"},{"name":"y","sort":"track"}],"params":[{"name":"aligned_cosine","unit":"ratio","meaning":"the tolerance of rel.same_direction: the cosine of the largest angle between the two headings that still counts as travelling the same way"},{"name":"speed_margin","unit":"m/s","meaning":"the speed resolution of a speed difference: the smallest excess of x's speed over y's that counts as gaining on y rather than keeping pace"}],"elements":[{"span":"their headings are aligned (rel.same_direction, with aligned_cosine as the relation's tolerance)","atoms":["rel.same_direction"],"concepts":[],"justification":"rel.same_direction: \"headings aligned: the cosine of the angle between the headings is above its tolerance\"; the tolerance is the formal aligned_cosine."},{"span":"their bodies overlap along x's heading (rel.longitudinal_overlap positive)","atoms":["rel.longitudinal_overlap"],"concepts":[],"justification":"rel.longitudinal_overlap: \"the bodies overlap along the subject's heading (side by side): the length the two footprints' projections on that axis share, negative for the gap between the projections\"; a positive value is the side-by-side phase. Not a stand-in for contact or a distance: the concept states neither."},{"span":"x's speed exceeds y's (kin.speed, m/s) by more than speed_margin","atoms":["kin.speed"],"concepts":[],"justification":"kin.speed: \"magnitude of velocity\", m/s, read for both road users; gaining on y is x's speed above y's by more than the resolution."}],"residues":[],"scenarios":[{"name":"holds","expected":"compliant","narrative":"x and y head the same way within aligned_cosine, their footprints share a positive length along x's heading, and x's kin.speed exceeds y's by more than speed_margin: x is overtaking y alongside."},{"name":"fails","expected":"violated","narrative":"x follows y in the same lane with a negative rel.longitudinal_overlap (a gap between the projections) at a higher speed: x has not drawn alongside, so the concept does not hold."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x and y head the same way and x is faster, but the source does not observe rel.longitudinal_overlap: whether they are side by side is unknown.","masked":["rel.longitudinal_overlap"]}],"used_by":["NRS_484B_270_7b"],"supersedes":null}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_270_7b","law_refs":["NRS-484B-270-7b"],"subject":{"binder":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"a1","text":"The operator of a bicycle, an electric bicycle or an electric scooter","role":"subject"},{"id":"a2","text":"shall not: Overtake and pass","role":"obligation"},{"id":"a3","text":"a motor vehicle","role":"obligation"},{"id":"a4","text":"unless the operator can do so safely without endangering himself or herself or the occupants of the motor vehicle.","role":"standard"}],"elements":[{"span":"a1","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"],"derived":[],"justification":"The three machines are the admitted aggregates of the definitions that apply: DEF-NRS-484A-025 (\"a device propelled by human power upon which a person may ride\"), DEF-NRS-484B-017 (\"a device upon which a person may ride, having two or three wheels\") and DEF-NRS-484B-018 (\"a vehicle with handlebars and an electric motor\"). ru.aggregate: \"membership of a legal aggregate\"; each is claimed by its admitted id and never expanded into class atoms. 'The operator of' names who controls the machine, a role and not a membership, read through the machine's controlled motion (observable_reading agency)."},{"span":"a2","atoms":["rel.same_direction","rel.longitudinal_overlap","kin.speed"],"derived":["drv.interaction.overtaking_alongside"],"justification":"Overtaking and passing is the manoeuvre the proposed concept drv.interaction.overtaking_alongside denotes in its side-by-side phase: \"Road user x is overtaking road user y alongside at the observation: the side-by-side phase of an overtaking, on either side of y\". The words name no side, so the concept counts either side (unlike drv.interaction.passing_on_right). Its atoms rel.same_direction, rel.longitudinal_overlap and kin.speed are claimed as the concept reads them; rel.longitudinal_overlap is 'not a stand-in' for contact or a distance and is used for neither."},{"span":"a3","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'a motor vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle (\"every vehicle which is self-propelled but not operated upon rails\"; \"does not include an electric bicycle or an electric scooter\"); the road user overtaken is quantified in the rule and must carry it. ru.aggregate is never replaced by ru.motor_vehicle."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"a4","standard":"safely without endangering himself or herself or the occupants of the motor vehicle","concepts":["rel.surface_gap","prim.closest_approach_within","prim.closest_approach_distance"],"params":["p.passing_lateral_clearance","p.conflict_clearance","p.immediate_hazard_gap"],"convention":"Passing-clearance convention for cycles passing motor vehicles (the endangerment of the occupants and of the rider by the vehicle passed): the surface gap between the two bodies while side by side is at least the passing clearance, read by its degree. Surrogate-safety closest-approach convention (the endangerment of the rider by other traffic): no other road user is predicted, under constant velocities within the critical gap, to come nearer the rider than the conflict radius.","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"]}],"applicability":"x carries ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle, ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle or ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter, and at the observation some road user y other than x that carries ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle is being overtaken alongside by x (drv.interaction.overtaking_alongside(x, y) with p.same_direction_cosine and p.overtaking_speed_margin).","obligation":"For every road user y other than x that carries ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle and that x is overtaking alongside at the observation: the surface gap between x and y (rel.surface_gap) is at least p.passing_lateral_clearance; and for every road user z other than x and y it is not the case that x and z approach each other within p.immediate_hazard_gap (prim.closest_approach_within) with a closest-approach centre distance (prim.closest_approach_distance) below p.conflict_clearance.","params":["p.same_direction_cosine","p.overtaking_speed_margin","p.passing_lateral_clearance","p.conflict_clearance","p.immediate_hazard_gap"],"narrowings":[{"span":"a1","why":"'The operator' is read through the machine's controlled motion: the duty binds the conduct of the bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter whoever controls it.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"a2","why":"'Overtake and pass' is judged in its side-by-side phase, where the clearance to the vehicle passed and the exposure to other traffic arise; the approach from behind and the return ahead are not judged on their own.","kind":"reading"},{"span":"a4","why":"'safely without endangering himself or herself or the occupants of the motor vehicle' is read through two contracts only: the surface gap kept to the motor vehicle passed (the exposure of its occupants and of the rider to that vehicle) and the predicted closest approach to every other road user (the rider's exposure to other traffic). The road surface, the sight available and the rider's balance are not read.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"x (ru.bicycle) travels with rel.same_direction to a passenger car y (ru.motor_vehicle), rel.longitudinal_overlap positive and x's kin.speed above y's by more than p.overtaking_speed_margin, with rel.surface_gap between them below p.passing_lateral_clearance; no other road user is in the scene."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"The same overtaking alongside with rel.surface_gap above p.passing_lateral_clearance and no other road user in the scene: the duty binds x alone and is met."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"x (ru.bicycle) rides behind car y in the same lane with a negative rel.longitudinal_overlap and never draws alongside: no overtaking takes place."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x rides faster than car y in the same direction close beside it, but the source does not observe rel.longitudinal_overlap: whether x is overtaking alongside is unknown.","masked":["rel.longitudinal_overlap"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"violated","narrative":"x (ru.electric_scooter) overtakes car y alongside with rel.surface_gap above p.passing_lateral_clearance, but an oncoming ru.motor_vehicle z satisfies prim.closest_approach_within with x over p.immediate_hazard_gap at a prim.closest_approach_distance below p.conflict_clearance."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.same_direction_cosine","unit":"ratio","value":0.9,"convention":"Heading alignment tolerance: the cosine of the largest angle between two headings that still counts as travelling the same way.","source":"heading-alignment conventions of trajectory analysis"},{"name":"p.overtaking_speed_margin","unit":"m/s","value":0.5,"convention":"Speed resolution of a speed difference: the smallest excess of the subject's speed over the other's that counts as gaining on it rather than keeping pace.","source":"speed resolution of the carla_scene_graph acquisition standard"},{"name":"p.passing_lateral_clearance","unit":"m","value":0.9,"convention":"Passing clearance: the smallest surface gap between a cycle or scooter and a motor vehicle it passes alongside at which the pass endangers neither the rider nor the vehicle's occupants; the three-foot passing-clearance convention applied from the rider's side.","source":"three-foot passing-clearance statutes and AASHTO Guide for the Development of Bicycle Facilities"},{"name":"p.conflict_clearance","unit":"m","value":3.0,"convention":"Conflict radius: the centre distance at predicted closest approach below which two road users' paths count as in conflict; about the half-length plus half-width of two passenger cars.","source":"surrogate safety measures (closest-approach conflict radius)"},{"name":"p.immediate_hazard_gap","unit":"s","value":4.1,"convention":"Critical gap: the time within which another road user's arrival at the conflict area, or its predicted closest approach, counts as an immediate hazard to a road user about to cross or join its path.","source":"Highway Capacity Manual critical-gap values"}],"gaps":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_307_9a_o1","law_refs":["NRS-484B-307-9a"],"subject":{"binder":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"b1","text":"Where the signal is a steady red with a green turn arrow:","role":"trigger"},{"id":"b2","text":"Except as otherwise provided in paragraph (b) [NRS-484B-307-9b],","role":"reference"},{"id":"b3","text":"vehicular traffic","role":"subject"},{"id":"b4","text":"facing the signal","role":"trigger"},{"id":"b5","text":"may enter the intersection","role":"trigger"},{"id":"b6","text":"only to make the movement indicated by the green turn arrow,","role":"obligation"},{"id":"b7","text":"but must yield","role":"sibling"},{"id":"b8","text":"the right-of-way","role":"sibling"},{"id":"b9","text":"to pedestrians lawfully within an adjacent crosswalk","role":"sibling"},{"id":"b10","text":"and to other traffic lawfully using the intersection.","role":"sibling"},{"id":"b11","text":"Drivers turning in the direction of the arrow are thereby advised that so long as the turn arrow is illuminated, oncoming or opposing traffic simultaneously faces a steady red signal.","role":"definitional"}],"elements":[{"span":"b1","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"dev.traffic_signal: \"a signal head; state ∈ {circular_green, circular_yellow, circular_red, green_arrow(dir), ...}\" and \"several states may be displayed at once\": a steady red with a green turn arrow is a head displaying circular_red together with green_arrow(dir), dir left or right. 'The signal' is the head tied to the subject's approach in span b4. No 'not a stand-in' clause applies."},{"span":"b3","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"],"derived":[],"justification":"'traffic' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic (\"pedestrians, ridden or herded animals, vehicles and other conveyances either singly or together using any highway for purposes of travel\"). The law's own qualifier 'vehicular' leaves out the members that are not conveyances: pedestrians (\"a person afoot, a person in a manual or motorized wheelchair\", the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian, which the rule requires the subject not to carry) and ridden or herded animals, for which the ontology has no class and nothing is read. Cycles and scooters stay in, as 'other conveyances'; paragraph (b) is written as an exception for them, which confirms they are vehicular traffic here."},{"span":"b4","atoms":["dev.governs","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region","st.intersection","rel.occupies"],"derived":["drv.position.entered_via"],"justification":"Facing the signal is the signal governing the approach the subject enters through. dev.governs: \"the travel regions whose traffic the device controls ... or an intersection, read as control of the junction itself\"; st.lane_enters: \"the intersection region a directed approach carrier runs into at its entrance end\"; drv.position.entered_via (proposed this iteration): \"x is inside region r on its current entry and came in through region c\". The approach carrier c is the one x occupied at its entry with st.lane_enters(c, i); the signal governs c or i. dev.governs is 'not a stand-in' for a position and is not used as one."},{"span":"b5","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.intersection"],"derived":["drv.motion.entering_region"],"justification":"drv.motion.entering_region (proposed this iteration): \"Road user x enters structure region r at the observation: its footprint overlaps r (rel.occupies) at the observation and did not at the observation before\"; r is the st.intersection, \"the region where two roadways meet\"."},{"span":"b6","atoms":["kin.yaw_rate","rel.occupies","st.intersection"],"derived":["drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry","drv.motion.leaving_region"],"justification":"The movement made through the intersection is read at x's leaving of it (drv.motion.leaving_region: \"its footprint overlapped r (rel.occupies) at the observation before and does not overlap it at the observation\") by drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry: \"The signed heading change of road user x since its footprint last began to overlap region r, in degrees, left positive\", integrated from kin.yaw_rate. A left arrow indicates a change of at least the turn recognition angle to the left, a right arrow one to the right. The concept is 'not' a turn by itself; the rule compares it with its own bound."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[{"span":"b2","rule":"NRS_484B_307_9b_o1","map":{"x":"x"},"as":"exception"}],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic"]}],"applicability":"x carries ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic and does not carry ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian; at the observation x leaves an intersection i (drv.motion.leaving_region(x, i)); at the observation of its latest entry into i (drv.motion.entering_region(x, i), read through a past operator) x came in through a carrier c with st.lane_enters(c, i) (drv.position.entered_via(x, i, c)), and a traffic signal s that governs c or i (dev.governs) displayed circular_red together with green_arrow(d), d left or right. Not engaged where NRS_484B_307_9b_o1 applies to x (composition, exception).","obligation":"At that leaving observation the heading change of x since that entry (drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry(x, i) with step p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph) shows the movement a green arrow displayed at the entry indicates: at least p.turn_recognition_angle where d is left, at most minus p.turn_recognition_angle where d is right. Where arrows of both directions were displayed, the movement either indicates complies.","params":["p.turn_recognition_angle","p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph"],"narrowings":[{"span":"b6","why":"The movement indicated by the arrow is read as the side and the size of the heading change through the intersection, judged when the subject leaves it: a passage turning at least the turn recognition angle toward the arrow's side complies, whatever lane it exits into.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"x (ru.motor_vehicle) enters intersection i from lane c that a signal s governs; s displays circular_red with green_arrow(left) at the entry; x crosses i and leaves it with a heading change since entry well inside p.turn_recognition_angle (straight through)."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"The same entry under circular_red with green_arrow(left); x leaves i with a heading change since entry above p.turn_recognition_angle to the left."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"s displays circular_green at x's entry into i; x crosses straight through."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x enters i from lane c and crosses straight through, but the source does not observe s's state at the entry.","masked":["dev.traffic_signal"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"x is a ru.bicycle; it enters i under circular_red with green_arrow(left) and leaves straight through: paragraph (b) applies (NRS_484B_307_9b_o1 engaged), so this duty does not."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.turn_recognition_angle","unit":"deg","value":45,"convention":"Turn recognition: the heading change through an intersection beyond which a passage counts as a turn rather than a straight crossing; half the right angle of a turn at a right-angled junction, leaving room for skewed junctions and lane offsets.","source":"intersection geometry design conventions (AASHTO Green Book)"}],"gaps":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_307_9a_o2","law_refs":["NRS-484B-307-9a"],"subject":{"binder":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"b1","text":"Where the signal is a steady red with a green turn arrow:","role":"trigger"},{"id":"b2","text":"Except as otherwise provided in paragraph (b) [NRS-484B-307-9b],","role":"reference"},{"id":"b3","text":"vehicular traffic","role":"subject"},{"id":"b4","text":"facing the signal","role":"trigger"},{"id":"b5","text":"may enter the intersection","role":"trigger"},{"id":"b6","text":"only to make the movement indicated by the green turn arrow,","role":"sibling"},{"id":"b7","text":"but must yield","role":"obligation"},{"id":"b8","text":"the right-of-way","role":"standard"},{"id":"b9","text":"to pedestrians lawfully within an adjacent crosswalk","role":"obligation"},{"id":"b10","text":"and to other traffic lawfully using the intersection.","role":"obligation"},{"id":"b11","text":"Drivers turning in the direction of the arrow are thereby advised that so long as the turn arrow is illuminated, oncoming or opposing traffic simultaneously faces a steady red signal.","role":"definitional"}],"elements":[{"span":"b1","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"dev.traffic_signal: \"a signal head; state ∈ {circular_green, circular_yellow, circular_red, green_arrow(dir), ...}\" and \"several states may be displayed at once\": a steady red with a green turn arrow is a head displaying circular_red together with green_arrow(dir), dir left or right. No 'not a stand-in' clause applies."},{"span":"b3","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"],"derived":[],"justification":"'traffic' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic (\"pedestrians, ridden or herded animals, vehicles and other conveyances\"). The qualifier 'vehicular' leaves out pedestrians (DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian, \"a person afoot\", which the subject must not carry) and ridden or herded animals, which have no class atom; cycles and scooters stay in as 'other conveyances'."},{"span":"b4","atoms":["dev.governs","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region","st.intersection","rel.occupies"],"derived":["drv.position.entered_via"],"justification":"Facing the signal is the signal governing the approach the subject enters through: dev.governs (\"the travel regions whose traffic the device controls ... or an intersection\") on the carrier c with st.lane_enters(c, i) (\"the intersection region a directed approach carrier runs into at its entrance end\") that x came in through (drv.position.entered_via: \"x is inside region r on its current entry and came in through region c\"), or on i itself."},{"span":"b5","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.intersection"],"derived":["drv.motion.entering_region"],"justification":"drv.motion.entering_region: \"its footprint overlaps r (rel.occupies) at the observation and did not at the observation before\", r the st.intersection."},{"span":"b7","atoms":["kin.speed","rel.occupies","st.intersection"],"derived":["drv.motion.moving"],"justification":"Yielding is granting precedence (DEF-NRS-484A-210, \"unless one grants precedence to the other\"): the subject does not proceed into a conflict. It is judged at each observation at which x, inside i on the passage entered under the arrow (rel.occupies), is in motion (drv.motion.moving: \"its speed exceeds speed_floor\", kin.speed); a halted subject grants precedence."},{"span":"b9","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian","rel.occupies","st.crosswalk","st.entrance_of","st.lane_enters","st.intersection"],"derived":[],"justification":"'pedestrians' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian (\"a person afoot, a person in a manual or motorized wheelchair\"). 'within an adjacent crosswalk' is the pedestrian's footprint overlapping (rel.occupies) a st.crosswalk (\"marked crossing, or the unmarked prolongation of sidewalks at an intersection\") adjacent to i: a crosswalk recorded as marking the entrance of a carrier entering i (st.entrance_of: \"the carrier whose entrance into an intersection a stop line or a crosswalk marks\"; st.lane_enters). Distance is not used for adjacency."},{"span":"b10","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","rel.occupies","st.intersection"],"derived":[],"justification":"'other traffic' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic, every member other than x; 'using the intersection' is its footprint overlapping i (rel.occupies)."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"b8","standard":"the right-of-way: proceeding where the parties' \"direction, speed and proximity\" \"give rise to the danger of a crash unless one grants precedence\" (DEF-NRS-484A-210)","concepts":["prim.closest_approach_within","prim.closest_approach_distance"],"params":["p.immediate_hazard_gap","p.conflict_clearance"],"convention":"Gap-acceptance and surrogate-safety convention: the danger of a crash between the subject and another party is their predicted closest approach under constant velocities, within the critical gap, coming nearer than the conflict radius; direction, speed and proximity all enter the prediction by their degree.","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[{"span":"b2","rule":"NRS_484B_307_9b_o1","map":{"x":"x"},"as":"exception"}],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic"]}],"applicability":"x carries ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic and does not carry ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian; at the observation x occupies an intersection i on a passage whose entry (drv.motion.entering_region(x, i), the latest, read through a past operator) came through a carrier c with st.lane_enters(c, i) (drv.position.entered_via(x, i, c)), and at that entry a traffic signal s that governs c or i (dev.governs) displayed circular_red together with green_arrow(d), d left or right. Not engaged where NRS_484B_307_9b_o1 applies to x (composition, exception).","obligation":"Where x is moving at the observation (drv.motion.moving with p.speed_resolution): for every road user p carrying ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian that occupies a crosswalk w recorded as marking the entrance of some carrier c2 entering i (st.entrance_of(w, c2), st.lane_enters(c2, i)), and for every road user u other than x carrying ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic that occupies i, it is not the case that x and that road user approach within p.immediate_hazard_gap (prim.closest_approach_within) with a closest-approach centre distance (prim.closest_approach_distance) below p.conflict_clearance.","params":["p.speed_resolution","p.immediate_hazard_gap","p.conflict_clearance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"b9","why":"'lawfully' is not read: every pedestrian in such a crosswalk is yielded to, which no lawfulness of the pedestrian's own conduct could make stricter than the words. 'an adjacent crosswalk' is read as a crosswalk recorded as marking the entrance of a carrier entering the intersection; a crosswalk across the exit of a one-way leg marks no entrance and is not read.","kind":"reading"},{"span":"b10","why":"'lawfully' is not read: every other member of traffic inside the intersection is yielded to.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"x (ru.motor_vehicle) entered i under circular_red with green_arrow(left) and is turning left, moving; a ru.pedestrian occupies the crosswalk that marks the entrance of the carrier on the leg x turns into, and prim.closest_approach_within holds over p.immediate_hazard_gap with a prim.closest_approach_distance below p.conflict_clearance."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"x enters i under circular_red with green_arrow(left) and turns left with no other road user in the scene."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"x enters i while s displays circular_green."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x moves through i with a pedestrian approaching in a crosswalk at the entrance of the leg x turns into, but the source does not observe s's state at x's entry.","masked":["dev.traffic_signal"]}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.speed_resolution","unit":"m/s","value":0.2,"convention":"Sensor resolution: the smallest speed the acquisition standard separates from standstill; a speed at or below it counts as no motion.","source":"speed resolution of the carla_scene_graph acquisition standard"},{"name":"p.immediate_hazard_gap","unit":"s","value":4.1,"convention":"Critical gap: the time within which another road user's arrival at the conflict area, or its predicted closest approach, counts as an immediate hazard to a road user about to cross or join its path.","source":"Highway Capacity Manual critical-gap values"},{"name":"p.conflict_clearance","unit":"m","value":3.0,"convention":"Conflict radius: the centre distance at predicted closest approach below which two road users' paths count as in conflict; about the half-length plus half-width of two passenger cars.","source":"surrogate safety measures (closest-approach conflict radius)"}],"gaps":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_307_9b_o1","law_refs":["NRS-484B-307-9b"],"subject":{"binder":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"c1","text":"Where the signal is a steady red with a green turn arrow:","role":"trigger"},{"id":"c2","text":"A person driving a motorcycle, moped or","role":"subject"},{"id":"c3","text":"trimobile","role":"subject"},{"id":"c4","text":"or riding a bicycle, an electric bicycle or an electric scooter","role":"subject"},{"id":"c5","text":"facing the signal","role":"trigger"},{"id":"c6","text":"may proceed straight through or turn in the direction opposite that indicated by the green turn arrow","role":"trigger"},{"id":"c7","text":"if:","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"c8","text":"(1) The person stops before entering the crosswalk on the nearest side of the intersection where the sign or pavement marking indicates where the stop must be made or, in the absence of any such crosswalk, sign or marking, before entering the intersection;","role":"obligation"},{"id":"c9","text":"(2) The person waits for two complete cycles of the lights or lighted arrows of the applicable official traffic-control device","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c10","text":"and the signal does not change because of a malfunction or because the signal failed to detect the presence of the motorcycle, moped, trimobile, bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter;","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c11","text":"(3) No other device at the place prohibits the turn, if applicable;","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c12","text":"and","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"c13","text":"(4) The person yields","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c14","text":"the right-of-way","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c15","text":"to pedestrians lawfully within an adjacent crosswalk","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c16","text":"and to other traffic lawfully using the intersection.","role":"sibling"}],"elements":[{"span":"c1","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"dev.traffic_signal: \"a signal head; state ∈ {... circular_red, ... green_arrow(dir) ...}\" and \"several states may be displayed at once\": a steady red with a green turn arrow is circular_red displayed together with green_arrow(dir), dir left or right. No 'not a stand-in' clause applies."},{"span":"c2","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped"],"derived":[],"justification":"The admitted aggregates DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle (\"every motor vehicle equipped with a seat or saddle for the use of the driver and designed to travel on not more than three wheels in contact with the ground\") and DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped (\"a motor-driven scooter, motor-driven cycle or similar vehicle\"), claimed by id and never expanded. 'A person driving' names who controls the machine, read through its controlled motion (observable_reading agency)."},{"span":"c4","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"],"derived":[],"justification":"The admitted aggregates DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle (\"a device propelled by human power upon which a person may ride\"), DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle (\"a device upon which a person may ride, having two or three wheels\") and DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter (\"a vehicle with handlebars and an electric motor\"). 'riding' is read through the machine's controlled motion (observable_reading agency)."},{"span":"c5","atoms":["dev.governs","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region","st.intersection","rel.occupies"],"derived":["drv.position.entered_via"],"justification":"Facing the signal is the signal governing the approach the person enters through: dev.governs (\"the travel regions whose traffic the device controls ... or an intersection\") on the carrier c with st.lane_enters(c, i) (\"the intersection region a directed approach carrier runs into at its entrance end\") that x came in through (drv.position.entered_via: \"x is inside region r on its current entry and came in through region c\"), or on i itself. dev.governs is 'not a stand-in' for a position and is not used as one."},{"span":"c6","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.intersection","kin.yaw_rate"],"derived":["drv.motion.entering_region","drv.motion.leaving_region","drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry"],"justification":"Proceeding through the intersection is the passage from x's entry (drv.motion.entering_region: \"its footprint overlaps r (rel.occupies) at the observation and did not at the observation before\") to its leaving (drv.motion.leaving_region). Straight through or a turn opposite the arrow is read at the leaving by drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry (\"The signed heading change of road user x since its footprint last began to overlap region r, in degrees, left positive\", from kin.yaw_rate): straight where its size stays below the turn recognition angle, opposite where it reaches that angle on the side away from the arrow."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[{"span":"c3","why":"Every trimobile, a motor vehicle with a seat designed to travel on three wheels, is already a member of the motorcycle aggregate claimed on span c2, whose definition takes \"every motor vehicle equipped with a seat or saddle for the use of the driver and designed to travel on not more than three wheels in contact with the ground\": the duty is the same whether or not the word is read.","scope":"none"}],"binders":[{"name":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"]}],"applicability":"x carries ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle, ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped, ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle, ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle or ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter; at the observation x leaves an intersection i (drv.motion.leaving_region(x, i)); at the observation of its latest entry into i (drv.motion.entering_region(x, i), read through a past operator) x came in through a carrier c with st.lane_enters(c, i) (drv.position.entered_via(x, i, c)) and a traffic signal s that governs c or i (dev.governs) displayed circular_red together with green_arrow(d), d left or right; and at the leaving observation the heading change since that entry (drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry(x, i) with step p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph) shows a straight-through passage (its absolute value below p.turn_recognition_angle) or a turn opposite d (at most minus p.turn_recognition_angle where d is left, at least p.turn_recognition_angle where d is right).","obligation":"A halt before the entry, searched in the past (the approach convention). Event: x's entry into i that the applicability names, made through carrier c (the carrier x occupied at the observation before the entry with st.lane_enters(c, i)). Place, in order: a stop line recorded as marking c (st.entrance_of(line, c)); where c's marks are observed and include no stop line, a crosswalk recorded as marking c; where neither is recorded for c, the entrance end of c at i. Act: an observation at which x is halted (drv.motion.halted with p.speed_resolution) while occupying c, its body within p.stop_point_tolerance of the place (st.region_geometry distance), not past it along c's designated direction (prim.region_offset_along of the place from x not negative), and its footprint overlapping neither i nor, where the place is a crosswalk, that crosswalk. Search: back from the entry, ending at the approach start (the last observation before the entry at which x, on c, is outside the place's stopping zone upstream: off the mark, short of it and farther from it than p.stop_point_tolerance) or at x's previous entry into i through the same place; nothing else ends it. Verdict: complied where the search finds the act; violated where it reaches either end without it; unknown only where it reaches neither (the recording begins inside the approach) or where c's association with a mark, c's direction or x's place relative to the mark is unobserved and the verdict turns on it. Judged at the leaving observation, the search running from the entry.","params":["p.speed_resolution","p.stop_point_tolerance","p.turn_recognition_angle","p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph"],"narrowings":[{"span":"c2","why":"'A person driving' is read through the machine's controlled motion: the duty binds the motorcycle's or moped's conduct whoever controls it.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"c4","why":"'riding' is read through the machine's controlled motion: the duty binds the conduct of the bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter whoever rides it.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"c8","why":"The places are read in the order the words give them under the ontology's approach convention: the pavement marking indicating where the stop must be made is the stop line marking the approach; failing one, the crosswalk on the near side is the crosswalk marking the approach; failing both, the entrance of the intersection. A sign that indicates a stopping point without a line is not carried by any atom and is not read.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"x (ru.motorcycle) approaches i on lane c, which a stop line marks (st.entrance_of); it never halts on c, enters i while s governing c displays circular_red with green_arrow(left), and leaves straight through. The search back from the entry reaches the approach start without a halt."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"x (ru.bicycle) halts on c within p.stop_point_tolerance of the stop line marking c, short of it, then enters i under circular_red with green_arrow(left) and leaves straight through."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"x (ru.motorcycle) enters i while s displays circular_green and leaves straight through."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x halts on c short of a stop line within p.stop_point_tolerance and then goes straight through under circular_red with green_arrow(left), but the source does not observe which carriers the line marks, so whether the halt was at the governing place is unknown.","masked":["st.entrance_of"]},{"name":"history_boundary","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x's recording begins with x already on c inside the stopping zone of the stop line, rolling slowly; no halt is recorded before it enters i under circular_red with green_arrow(left) and leaves straight through. The search reaches neither the approach start nor a previous entry.","boundary":"the start of x's approach on c, outside the stop line's stopping zone upstream, which lies before the recording"}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.speed_resolution","unit":"m/s","value":0.2,"convention":"Sensor resolution: the smallest speed the acquisition standard separates from standstill; a speed at or below it counts as no motion.","source":"speed resolution of the carla_scene_graph acquisition standard"},{"name":"p.stop_point_tolerance","unit":"m","value":2.0,"convention":"Stop-point tolerance: the largest ground distance between a halted body and the line, crossing or intersection edge at which the halt counts as made at that place; a body farther upstream is outside the stopping zone.","source":"MUTCD stop-line placement practice"},{"name":"p.turn_recognition_angle","unit":"deg","value":45,"convention":"Turn recognition: the heading change through an intersection beyond which a passage counts as a turn rather than a straight crossing; half the right angle of a turn at a right-angled junction, leaving room for skewed junctions and lane offsets.","source":"intersection geometry design conventions (AASHTO Green Book)"}],"gaps":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_307_9b_o2","law_refs":["NRS-484B-307-9b"],"subject":{"binder":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"c1","text":"Where the signal is a steady red with a green turn arrow:","role":"trigger"},{"id":"c2","text":"A person driving a motorcycle, moped or","role":"subject"},{"id":"c3","text":"trimobile","role":"subject"},{"id":"c4","text":"or riding a bicycle, an electric bicycle or an electric scooter","role":"subject"},{"id":"c5","text":"facing the signal","role":"trigger"},{"id":"c6","text":"may proceed straight through or turn in the direction opposite that indicated by the green turn arrow","role":"trigger"},{"id":"c7","text":"if:","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"c8","text":"(1) The person stops before entering the crosswalk on the nearest side of the intersection where the sign or pavement marking indicates where the stop must be made or, in the absence of any such crosswalk, sign or marking, before entering the intersection;","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c9","text":"(2) The person waits for two complete cycles of the lights or lighted arrows of the applicable official traffic-control device","role":"obligation"},{"id":"c10","text":"and the signal does not change because of a malfunction or because the signal failed to detect the presence of the motorcycle, moped, trimobile, bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter;","role":"obligation"},{"id":"c11","text":"(3) No other device at the place prohibits the turn, if applicable;","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c12","text":"and","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"c13","text":"(4) The person yields","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c14","text":"the right-of-way","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c15","text":"to pedestrians lawfully within an adjacent crosswalk","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c16","text":"and to other traffic lawfully using the intersection.","role":"sibling"}],"elements":[{"span":"c1","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"dev.traffic_signal: \"a signal head; state ∈ {... circular_red, ... green_arrow(dir) ...}\" and \"several states may be displayed at once\": a steady red with a green turn arrow is circular_red displayed together with green_arrow(dir), dir left or right."},{"span":"c2","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped"],"derived":[],"justification":"The admitted aggregates DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle (\"every motor vehicle equipped with a seat or saddle for the use of the driver and designed to travel on not more than three wheels in contact with the ground\") and DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped (\"a motor-driven scooter, motor-driven cycle or similar vehicle\"), claimed by id. 'A person driving' is read through the machine's controlled motion."},{"span":"c4","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"],"derived":[],"justification":"The admitted aggregates DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle (\"a device propelled by human power upon which a person may ride\"), DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle (\"a device upon which a person may ride, having two or three wheels\") and DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter (\"a vehicle with handlebars and an electric motor\")."},{"span":"c5","atoms":["dev.governs","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region","st.intersection","rel.occupies"],"derived":["drv.position.entered_via"],"justification":"Facing the signal: dev.governs (\"the travel regions whose traffic the device controls ... or an intersection\") on the carrier c with st.lane_enters(c, i) that x came in through (drv.position.entered_via: \"came in through region c\"), or on i itself."},{"span":"c6","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.intersection","kin.yaw_rate"],"derived":["drv.motion.entering_region","drv.motion.leaving_region","drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry"],"justification":"The passage from x's entry into i (drv.motion.entering_region) to its leaving (drv.motion.leaving_region); straight through or opposite the arrow is read at the leaving by drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry (\"in degrees, left positive\", from kin.yaw_rate) against the turn recognition angle."},{"span":"c9","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal","dev.governs","kin.speed","rel.occupies","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region"],"derived":["drv.motion.halted"],"justification":"Waiting is remaining halted (drv.motion.halted: \"complete cessation from movement\", kin.speed at or below the resolution) on the approach carrier c (rel.occupies, st.lane_enters). The applicable official traffic-control device is the signal s facing x (dev.governs on c or i; its presence is the evidence of its official status). A complete cycle of its lights is the span between two successive rises of the same display; the rises of s's circular_red with green_arrow(d) display (dev.traffic_signal) are counted from the start of the wait, the first rise opening the first complete cycle, so two complete cycles need more rises than the literal."},{"span":"c10","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"That the signal does not change because it malfunctions or fails to detect x is read through its outcome on the head (observable_reading): during the wait s never displays an indication permitting x's movement, neither circular_green nor a green_arrow in the direction of x's movement (dev.traffic_signal state). Why the head stayed as it was (a fault, a detector) is not observable."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[{"span":"c3","why":"Every trimobile, a motor vehicle with a seat designed to travel on three wheels, is already a member of the motorcycle aggregate claimed on span c2 (\"every motor vehicle equipped with a seat or saddle for the use of the driver and designed to travel on not more than three wheels in contact with the ground\"): the duty is the same whether or not the word is read.","scope":"none"}],"binders":[{"name":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"]}],"applicability":"As NRS_484B_307_9b_o1: x carries one of the five aggregates of spans c2 and c4; at the observation x leaves intersection i (drv.motion.leaving_region(x, i)); at its latest entry into i (read through a past operator) it came in through carrier c with st.lane_enters(c, i) (drv.position.entered_via(x, i, c)) while a traffic signal s that governs c or i (dev.governs) displayed circular_red together with green_arrow(d), d left or right; and at the leaving the heading change since that entry (drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry(x, i) with step p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph) shows a straight-through passage (absolute value below p.turn_recognition_angle) or a turn opposite d.","obligation":"Read at the observation of x's latest entry into i, through a past operator from the leaving observation. Let the wait be the latest run of consecutive observations before the entry at which x is halted (drv.motion.halted with p.speed_resolution) while occupying c. Counted from the start of that run (Formula.count with edge: s displays circular_red together with green_arrow(d) and did not at the observation before; since: x halted while occupying c), the rises of that display number more than the literal of span c9 (comparison gt): the first rise counted opens the first complete cycle and each later one closes a cycle. And at no observation of the wait does s display circular_green, or green_arrow in the direction of x's movement (straight for a straight-through passage, the side of the turn for a turn). Where the wait began before the recording (x halted on c at its first observation), the count is unknown, not a violation.","params":["p.speed_resolution","p.turn_recognition_angle","p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph"],"narrowings":[{"span":"c2","why":"'A person driving' is read through the machine's controlled motion.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"c4","why":"'riding' is read through the machine's controlled motion.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"c9","why":"'the applicable official traffic-control device' is the signal head governing the person's approach; its presence on the road is read as the evidence of its official status.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"status"},{"span":"c10","why":"'does not change because of a malfunction or because the signal failed to detect the presence' turns on the device's detection, which is not observable; it is read through the outcome the condition secures: throughout the wait the head never displays an indication that permits the person's movement. A wait the signal ends by serving the person is not a failure to detect, and the permission then does not cover a later entry against the red.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"perception"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"x (ru.motorcycle) halts on c; s governing c rises to circular_red with green_arrow(left) once during the wait; x then enters i under that display and leaves straight through: the rises counted do not exceed the literal."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"x (ru.bicycle) halts on c and stays halted while s's circular_red with green_arrow(left) display rises more times than the literal, never showing circular_green or green_arrow(straight); x then enters under the display and leaves straight through."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"x is a ru.motor_vehicle that carries none of the five aggregates (a passenger car); it waits and then goes straight through under circular_red with green_arrow(left)."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x halts on c, waits and then goes straight through, but the source does not observe s's state during the wait.","masked":["dev.traffic_signal"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"violated","narrative":"x halts on c through more rises of circular_red with green_arrow(left) than the literal, but during the wait s also displays circular_green for c, which x lets pass; x later enters straight through under the red with the arrow: the signal did change, so the condition fails."},{"name":"history_boundary","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x's recording begins with x already halted on c; fewer rises than the literal plus the opening rise are recorded before x enters i straight through under circular_red with green_arrow(left), and the start of the wait is not recorded.","boundary":"the start of x's halt on c, which lies before the recording"}],"literals":[{"span":"c9","text":"two","value":2,"unit":"count"}],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.speed_resolution","unit":"m/s","value":0.2,"convention":"Sensor resolution: the smallest speed the acquisition standard separates from standstill; a speed at or below it counts as no motion.","source":"speed resolution of the carla_scene_graph acquisition standard"},{"name":"p.turn_recognition_angle","unit":"deg","value":45,"convention":"Turn recognition: the heading change through an intersection beyond which a passage counts as a turn rather than a straight crossing; half the right angle of a turn at a right-angled junction, leaving room for skewed junctions and lane offsets.","source":"intersection geometry design conventions (AASHTO Green Book)"}],"gaps":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_307_9b_o3","law_refs":["NRS-484B-307-9b"],"subject":{"binder":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"c1","text":"Where the signal is a steady red with a green turn arrow:","role":"trigger"},{"id":"c2","text":"A person driving a motorcycle, moped or","role":"subject"},{"id":"c3","text":"trimobile","role":"subject"},{"id":"c4","text":"or riding a bicycle, an electric bicycle or an electric scooter","role":"subject"},{"id":"c5","text":"facing the signal","role":"trigger"},{"id":"c6","text":"may proceed straight through or turn in the direction opposite that indicated by the green turn arrow","role":"trigger"},{"id":"c7","text":"if:","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"c8","text":"(1) The person stops before entering the crosswalk on the nearest side of the intersection where the sign or pavement marking indicates where the stop must be made or, in the absence of any such crosswalk, sign or marking, before entering the intersection;","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c9","text":"(2) The person waits for two complete cycles of the lights or lighted arrows of the applicable official traffic-control device","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c10","text":"and the signal does not change because of a malfunction or because the signal failed to detect the presence of the motorcycle, moped, trimobile, bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter;","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c11","text":"(3) No other device at the place prohibits the turn, if applicable;","role":"obligation"},{"id":"c12","text":"and","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"c13","text":"(4) The person yields","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c14","text":"the right-of-way","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c15","text":"to pedestrians lawfully within an adjacent crosswalk","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c16","text":"and to other traffic lawfully using the intersection.","role":"sibling"}],"elements":[{"span":"c1","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"dev.traffic_signal: \"several states may be displayed at once\": circular_red displayed together with green_arrow(dir), dir left or right."},{"span":"c2","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped"],"derived":[],"justification":"The admitted aggregates DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle (\"every motor vehicle equipped with a seat or saddle for the use of the driver\") and DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped (\"a motor-driven scooter, motor-driven cycle or similar vehicle\"), claimed by id."},{"span":"c4","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"],"derived":[],"justification":"The admitted aggregates DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle (\"a device propelled by human power upon which a person may ride\"), DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle (\"a device upon which a person may ride, having two or three wheels\") and DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter (\"a vehicle with handlebars and an electric motor\")."},{"span":"c5","atoms":["dev.governs","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region","st.intersection","rel.occupies"],"derived":["drv.position.entered_via"],"justification":"Facing the signal: dev.governs (\"the travel regions whose traffic the device controls ... or an intersection\") on the carrier c with st.lane_enters(c, i) that x came in through (drv.position.entered_via), or on i itself."},{"span":"c6","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.intersection","kin.yaw_rate"],"derived":["drv.motion.entering_region","drv.motion.leaving_region","drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry"],"justification":"The passage from x's entry into i to its leaving; straight through or opposite the arrow read at the leaving by drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry (\"in degrees, left positive\", from kin.yaw_rate) against the turn recognition angle."},{"span":"c11","atoms":["dev.regulatory_sign","dev.traffic_signal","dev.governs","prim.conditions_hold","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region","st.intersection"],"derived":[],"justification":"A device at the place that prohibits the turn: a dev.regulatory_sign (\"a point regulation by catalogue code\") of code no_left_turn for a left turn or no_right_turn for a right turn, whose structured conditions hold for x at the entry (prim.conditions_hold: \"the structured conditions of a device ... hold at the observation for a road user\"), or a traffic signal head other than the one that shows the arrow displaying red_arrow(dir) in the turn's direction (dev.traffic_signal); either governing (dev.governs) the carrier c x entered through (st.lane_enters(c, i)) or the intersection i. 'if applicable': a straight-through passage makes no turn, and the condition is met. A prohibition sign is 'not a stand-in' for a manoeuvre: it is read as the condition it is."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[{"span":"c3","why":"Every trimobile, a motor vehicle with a seat designed to travel on three wheels, is already a member of the motorcycle aggregate claimed on span c2 (\"every motor vehicle equipped with a seat or saddle for the use of the driver and designed to travel on not more than three wheels in contact with the ground\"): the duty is the same whether or not the word is read.","scope":"none"}],"binders":[{"name":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"]}],"applicability":"As NRS_484B_307_9b_o1: x carries one of the five aggregates of spans c2 and c4; at the observation x leaves intersection i (drv.motion.leaving_region(x, i)); at its latest entry into i (read through a past operator) it came in through carrier c with st.lane_enters(c, i) (drv.position.entered_via(x, i, c)) while a traffic signal s that governs c or i (dev.governs) displayed circular_red together with green_arrow(d), d left or right; and at the leaving the heading change since that entry (drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry(x, i) with step p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph) shows a straight-through passage (absolute value below p.turn_recognition_angle) or a turn opposite d.","obligation":"Where the passage is a turn (the heading change since the entry at least p.turn_recognition_angle in absolute value; its sign gives the side): at the observation of x's entry into i (read through a past operator) no device governing c or i (dev.governs) prohibits a turn to that side: no dev.regulatory_sign of code no_left_turn (for a left turn) or no_right_turn (for a right turn) whose conditions hold for x there (prim.conditions_hold), and no traffic signal head displaying red_arrow toward that side. A straight-through passage meets this condition.","params":["p.turn_recognition_angle","p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph"],"narrowings":[{"span":"c2","why":"'A person driving' is read through the machine's controlled motion.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"c4","why":"'riding' is read through the machine's controlled motion.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"c11","why":"'No other device at the place prohibits the turn' is read as the turn prohibitions the closed set carries: a no-left-turn or no-right-turn sign whose posted conditions hold, or a red arrow toward the turn's side, governing the approach or the intersection, at the entry.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"x (ru.motorcycle) enters i through c under circular_red with green_arrow(left) and turns right; a dev.regulatory_sign of code no_right_turn with empty conditions governs c."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"x (ru.bicycle) enters i through c under circular_red with green_arrow(left) and turns right; no sign or red arrow prohibiting a right turn governs c or i."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"x (ru.motorcycle) enters under circular_red with green_arrow(left) and turns left, the movement the arrow indicates."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x turns right under circular_red with green_arrow(left); a no_right_turn sign stands at the approach but the source does not observe which regions it governs.","masked":["dev.governs"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"compliant","narrative":"x (ru.moped) enters under circular_red with green_arrow(left) and goes straight through while a no_right_turn sign governs c: no turn is made, so the condition is met."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.turn_recognition_angle","unit":"deg","value":45,"convention":"Turn recognition: the heading change through an intersection beyond which a passage counts as a turn rather than a straight crossing; half the right angle of a turn at a right-angled junction, leaving room for skewed junctions and lane offsets.","source":"intersection geometry design conventions (AASHTO Green Book)"}],"gaps":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_307_9b_o4","law_refs":["NRS-484B-307-9b"],"subject":{"binder":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"c1","text":"Where the signal is a steady red with a green turn arrow:","role":"trigger"},{"id":"c2","text":"A person driving a motorcycle, moped or","role":"subject"},{"id":"c3","text":"trimobile","role":"subject"},{"id":"c4","text":"or riding a bicycle, an electric bicycle or an electric scooter","role":"subject"},{"id":"c5","text":"facing the signal","role":"trigger"},{"id":"c6","text":"may proceed straight through or turn in the direction opposite that indicated by the green turn arrow","role":"trigger"},{"id":"c7","text":"if:","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"c8","text":"(1) The person stops before entering the crosswalk on the nearest side of the intersection where the sign or pavement marking indicates where the stop must be made or, in the absence of any such crosswalk, sign or marking, before entering the intersection;","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c9","text":"(2) The person waits for two complete cycles of the lights or lighted arrows of the applicable official traffic-control device","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c10","text":"and the signal does not change because of a malfunction or because the signal failed to detect the presence of the motorcycle, moped, trimobile, bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter;","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c11","text":"(3) No other device at the place prohibits the turn, if applicable;","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c12","text":"and","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"c13","text":"(4) The person yields","role":"obligation"},{"id":"c14","text":"the right-of-way","role":"standard"},{"id":"c15","text":"to pedestrians lawfully within an adjacent crosswalk","role":"obligation"},{"id":"c16","text":"and to