{"concept_id":"drv.interaction.overtaking_alongside","kind":"formula","contract":"Road user x is overtaking road user y alongside at the observation: the side-by-side phase of an overtaking, on either side of y. It holds where their headings are aligned (rel.same_direction, with aligned_cosine as the relation's tolerance), their bodies overlap along x's heading (rel.longitudinal_overlap positive), and x's speed exceeds y's (kin.speed, m/s) by more than speed_margin, the speed resolution below which the two count as keeping pace. Either side of y counts. Not denoted: the approach from behind or the return ahead of y, the side on which x passes, where either body is on the road, a lane change, contact, or the clearance between the bodies.","definition":null,"args":[{"name":"x","sort":"track"},{"name":"y","sort":"track"}],"params":[{"name":"aligned_cosine","unit":"ratio","meaning":"the tolerance of rel.same_direction: the cosine of the largest angle between the two headings that still counts as travelling the same way"},{"name":"speed_margin","unit":"m/s","meaning":"the speed resolution of a speed difference: the smallest excess of x's speed over y's that counts as gaining on y rather than keeping pace"}],"elements":[{"span":"their headings are aligned (rel.same_direction, with aligned_cosine as the relation's tolerance)","atoms":["rel.same_direction"],"concepts":[],"justification":"rel.same_direction: \"headings aligned: the cosine of the angle between the headings is above its tolerance\"; the tolerance is the formal aligned_cosine."},{"span":"their bodies overlap along x's heading (rel.longitudinal_overlap positive)","atoms":["rel.longitudinal_overlap"],"concepts":[],"justification":"rel.longitudinal_overlap: \"the bodies overlap along the subject's heading (side by side): the length the two footprints' projections on that axis share, negative for the gap between the projections\"; a positive value is the side-by-side phase. Not a stand-in for contact or a distance: the concept states neither."},{"span":"x's speed exceeds y's (kin.speed, m/s) by more than speed_margin","atoms":["kin.speed"],"concepts":[],"justification":"kin.speed: \"magnitude of velocity\", m/s, read for both road users; gaining on y is x's speed above y's by more than the resolution."}],"residues":[],"scenarios":[{"name":"holds","expected":"compliant","narrative":"x and y head the same way within aligned_cosine, their footprints share a positive length along x's heading, and x's kin.speed exceeds y's by more than speed_margin: x is overtaking y alongside."},{"name":"fails","expected":"violated","narrative":"x follows y in the same lane with a negative rel.longitudinal_overlap (a gap between the projections) at a higher speed: x has not drawn alongside, so the concept does not hold."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x and y head the same way and x is faster, but the source does not observe rel.longitudinal_overlap: whether they are side by side is unknown.","masked":["rel.longitudinal_overlap"]}],"used_by":["NRS_484B_270_7b"],"supersedes":null}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_270_7b","law_refs":["NRS-484B-270-7b"],"subject":{"binder":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"a1","text":"The operator of a bicycle, an electric bicycle or an electric scooter","role":"subject"},{"id":"a2","text":"shall not: Overtake and pass a motor vehicle","role":"obligation"},{"id":"a4","text":"unless the operator can do so safely without endangering himself or herself or the occupants of the motor vehicle.","role":"standard"}],"elements":[{"span":"a1","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"],"derived":[],"justification":"The three machines are the admitted aggregates of the definitions that apply: DEF-NRS-484A-025 (\"a device propelled by human power upon which a person may ride\"), DEF-NRS-484B-017 (\"a device upon which a person may ride, having two or three wheels\") and DEF-NRS-484B-018 (\"a vehicle with handlebars and an electric motor\"). ru.aggregate: \"membership of a legal aggregate\"; each is claimed by its admitted id and never expanded into class atoms. 'The operator of' names who controls the machine, a role and not a membership, read through the machine's controlled motion (observable_reading agency)."},{"span":"a2","atoms":["rel.same_direction","rel.longitudinal_overlap","kin.speed","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle"],"derived":["drv.interaction.overtaking_alongside"],"justification":"Overtaking and passing is the manoeuvre the proposed concept drv.interaction.overtaking_alongside denotes in its side-by-side phase: \"Road user x is overtaking road user y alongside at the observation: the side-by-side phase of an overtaking, on either side of y\". The words name no side, so the concept counts either side (unlike drv.interaction.passing_on_right). Its atoms rel.same_direction, rel.longitudinal_overlap and kin.speed are claimed as the concept reads them; rel.longitudinal_overlap is 'not a stand-in' for contact or a distance and is used for neither. 'a motor vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle (\"every vehicle which is self-propelled but not operated upon rails\"; \"does not include an electric bicycle or an electric scooter\"), which the road user overtaken, quantified in the rule, must carry; it is never replaced by ru.motor_vehicle."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"a4","standard":"safely without endangering himself or herself or the occupants of the motor vehicle","concepts":["rel.surface_gap","prim.closest_approach_within","prim.closest_approach_distance"],"params":["p.passing_lateral_clearance","p.conflict_clearance","p.immediate_hazard_gap"],"convention":"Passing-clearance convention for cycles passing motor vehicles (the endangerment of the occupants and of the rider by the vehicle passed): the surface gap between the two bodies while side by side is at least the passing clearance, read by its degree. Surrogate-safety closest-approach convention (the endangerment of the rider by other traffic): no other road user is predicted, under constant velocities within the critical gap, to come nearer the rider than the conflict radius.","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"]}],"applicability":"x carries ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle, ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle or ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter, and at the observation some road user y other than x that carries ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle is being overtaken alongside by x (drv.interaction.overtaking_alongside(x, y) with p.same_direction_cosine and p.overtaking_speed_margin).","obligation":"For every road user y other than x that carries ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle and that x is overtaking alongside at the observation: the surface gap between x and y (rel.surface_gap) is at least p.passing_lateral_clearance; and for every road user z other than x and y it is not the case that x and z approach each other within p.immediate_hazard_gap (prim.closest_approach_within) with a closest-approach centre distance (prim.closest_approach_distance) below p.conflict_clearance.","params":["p.same_direction_cosine","p.overtaking_speed_margin","p.passing_lateral_clearance","p.conflict_clearance","p.immediate_hazard_gap"],"narrowings":[{"span":"a1","why":"'The operator' is read through the machine's controlled motion: the duty binds the conduct of the bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter whoever controls it.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"a2","why":"'Overtake and pass' is judged in its side-by-side phase, where the clearance to the vehicle passed and the exposure to other traffic arise; the approach from behind and the return ahead are not judged on their own.","kind":"reading"},{"span":"a4","why":"'safely without endangering himself or herself or the occupants of the motor vehicle' is read through two contracts only: the surface gap kept to the motor vehicle passed (the exposure of its occupants and of the rider to that vehicle) and the predicted closest approach to every other road user (the rider's exposure to other traffic). The road surface, the sight available and the rider's balance are not read.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"x (ru.bicycle) travels with rel.same_direction to a passenger car y (ru.motor_vehicle), rel.longitudinal_overlap positive and x's kin.speed above y's by more than p.overtaking_speed_margin, with rel.surface_gap between them below p.passing_lateral_clearance; no other road user is in the scene."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"The same overtaking alongside with rel.surface_gap above p.passing_lateral_clearance and no other road user in the scene: the duty binds x alone and is met."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"x (ru.bicycle) rides behind car y in the same lane with a negative rel.longitudinal_overlap and never draws alongside: no overtaking takes place."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x rides faster than car y in the same direction close beside it, but the source does not observe rel.longitudinal_overlap: whether x is overtaking alongside is unknown.","masked":["rel.longitudinal_overlap"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"violated","narrative":"x (ru.electric_scooter) overtakes car y alongside with rel.surface_gap above p.passing_lateral_clearance, but an oncoming ru.motor_vehicle z satisfies prim.closest_approach_within with x over p.immediate_hazard_gap at a prim.closest_approach_distance below p.conflict_clearance."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.same_direction_cosine","unit":"ratio","value":0.9,"convention":"Heading alignment tolerance: the cosine of the largest angle between two headings that still counts as travelling the same way.","source":"heading-alignment conventions of trajectory analysis"},{"name":"p.overtaking_speed_margin","unit":"m/s","value":0.5,"convention":"Speed resolution of a speed difference: the smallest excess of the subject's speed over the other's that counts as gaining on it rather than keeping pace.","source":"speed resolution of the carla_scene_graph acquisition standard"},{"name":"p.passing_lateral_clearance","unit":"m","value":0.9,"convention":"Passing clearance: the smallest surface gap between a cycle or scooter and a motor vehicle it passes alongside at which the pass endangers neither the rider nor the vehicle's occupants; the three-foot passing-clearance convention applied from the rider's side.","source":"three-foot passing-clearance statutes and AASHTO Guide for the Development of Bicycle Facilities"},{"name":"p.conflict_clearance","unit":"m","value":3.0,"convention":"Conflict radius: the centre distance at predicted closest approach below which two road users' paths count as in conflict; about the half-length plus half-width of two passenger cars.","source":"surrogate safety measures (closest-approach conflict radius)"},{"name":"p.immediate_hazard_gap","unit":"s","value":4.1,"convention":"Critical gap: the time within which another road user's arrival at the conflict area, or its predicted closest approach, counts as an immediate hazard to a road user about to cross or join its path.","source":"Highway Capacity Manual critical-gap values"}],"gaps":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_307_9a_o1","law_refs":["NRS-484B-307-9a"],"subject":{"binder":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"b1","text":"Where the signal is a steady red with a green turn arrow:","role":"trigger"},{"id":"b2","text":"Except as otherwise provided in paragraph (b) [NRS-484B-307-9b],","role":"reference"},{"id":"b3","text":"vehicular traffic","role":"subject"},{"id":"b4","text":"facing the signal","role":"trigger"},{"id":"b5","text":"may enter the intersection","role":"trigger"},{"id":"b6","text":"only to make the movement indicated by the green turn arrow,","role":"obligation"},{"id":"b7","text":"but must yield the right-of-way","role":"sibling"},{"id":"b9","text":"to pedestrians lawfully within an adjacent crosswalk and to other traffic lawfully using the intersection.","role":"sibling"},{"id":"b11","text":"Drivers turning in the direction of the arrow are thereby advised that so long as the turn arrow is illuminated, oncoming or opposing traffic simultaneously faces a steady red signal.","role":"definitional"}],"elements":[{"span":"b1","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"dev.traffic_signal: \"a signal head; state ∈ {circular_green, circular_yellow, circular_red, green_arrow(dir), ...}\" and \"several states may be displayed at once\": a steady red with a green turn arrow is a head displaying circular_red together with green_arrow(dir), dir left or right. 'The signal' is the head tied to the subject's approach in span b4. No 'not a stand-in' clause applies."},{"span":"b3","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"],"derived":[],"justification":"'traffic' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic (\"pedestrians, ridden or herded animals, vehicles and other conveyances either singly or together using any highway for purposes of travel\"). The law's own qualifier 'vehicular' leaves out the members that are not conveyances: pedestrians (\"a person afoot, a person in a manual or motorized wheelchair\", the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian, which the rule requires the subject not to carry) and ridden or herded animals, for which the ontology has no class and nothing is read. Cycles and scooters stay in, as 'other conveyances'; paragraph (b) is written as an exception for them, which confirms they are vehicular traffic here."},{"span":"b4","atoms":["dev.governs","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region","st.intersection","rel.occupies"],"derived":["drv.position.entered_via"],"justification":"Facing the signal is the signal governing the approach the subject enters through. dev.governs: \"the travel regions whose traffic the device controls ... or an intersection, read as control of the junction itself\"; st.lane_enters: \"the intersection region a directed approach carrier runs into at its entrance end\"; drv.position.entered_via (proposed this iteration): \"x is inside region r on its current entry and came in through region c\". The approach carrier c is the one x occupied at its entry with st.lane_enters(c, i); the signal governs c or i. dev.governs is 'not a stand-in' for a position and is not used as one."},{"span":"b5","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.intersection"],"derived":["drv.motion.entering_region"],"justification":"drv.motion.entering_region (proposed this iteration): \"Road user x enters structure region r at the observation: its footprint overlaps r (rel.occupies) at the observation and did not at the observation before\"; r is the st.intersection, \"the region where two roadways meet\"."},{"span":"b6","atoms":["kin.yaw_rate","rel.occupies","st.intersection"],"derived":["drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry","drv.motion.leaving_region"],"justification":"The movement made through the intersection is read at x's leaving of it (drv.motion.leaving_region: \"its footprint overlapped r (rel.occupies) at the observation before and does not overlap it at the observation\") by drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry: \"The signed heading change of road user x since its footprint last began to overlap region r, in degrees, left positive\", integrated from kin.yaw_rate. A left arrow indicates a change of at least the turn recognition angle to the left, a right arrow one to the right. The concept is 'not' a turn by itself; the rule compares it with its own bound."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[{"span":"b2","rule":"NRS_484B_307_9b_o1","map":{"x":"x"},"as":"exception"}],"residues":[{"span":"b11","why":"An advisory to drivers turning with the arrow about what opposing traffic faces at the same time; it permits, requires and forbids nothing, and no rule reads it."}],"binders":[{"name":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic"]}],"applicability":"x carries ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic and does not carry ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian; at the observation x leaves an intersection i (drv.motion.leaving_region(x, i)); at the observation of its latest entry into i (drv.motion.entering_region(x, i), read through a past operator) x came in through a carrier c with st.lane_enters(c, i) (drv.position.entered_via(x, i, c)), and a traffic signal s that governs c or i (dev.governs) displayed circular_red together with green_arrow(d), d left or right. Not engaged where NRS_484B_307_9b_o1 applies to x (composition, exception).","obligation":"At that leaving observation the heading change of x since that entry (drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry(x, i) with step p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph) shows the movement a green arrow displayed at the entry indicates: at least p.turn_recognition_angle where d is left, at most minus p.turn_recognition_angle where d is right. Where arrows of both directions were displayed, the movement either indicates complies.","params":["p.turn_recognition_angle","p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph"],"narrowings":[{"span":"b6","why":"The movement indicated by the arrow is read as the side and the size of the heading change through the intersection, judged when the subject leaves it: a passage turning at least the turn recognition angle toward the arrow's side complies, whatever lane it exits into.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"x (ru.motor_vehicle) enters intersection i from lane c that a signal s governs; s displays circular_red with green_arrow(left) at the entry; x crosses i and leaves it with a heading change since entry well inside p.turn_recognition_angle (straight through)."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"The same entry under circular_red with green_arrow(left); x leaves i with a heading change since entry above p.turn_recognition_angle to the left."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"s displays circular_green at x's entry into i; x crosses straight through."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x enters i from lane c and crosses straight through, but the source does not observe s's state at the entry.","masked":["dev.traffic_signal"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"x is a ru.bicycle; it enters i under circular_red with green_arrow(left) and leaves straight through: paragraph (b) applies (NRS_484B_307_9b_o1 engaged), so this duty does not."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.turn_recognition_angle","unit":"deg","value":45,"convention":"Turn recognition: the heading change through an intersection beyond which a passage counts as a turn rather than a straight crossing; half the right angle of a turn at a right-angled junction, leaving room for skewed junctions and lane offsets.","source":"intersection geometry design conventions (AASHTO Green Book)"}],"gaps":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_307_9a_o2","law_refs":["NRS-484B-307-9a"],"subject":{"binder":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"b1","text":"Where the signal is a steady red with a green turn arrow:","role":"trigger"},{"id":"b2","text":"Except as otherwise provided in paragraph (b) [NRS-484B-307-9b],","role":"reference"},{"id":"b3","text":"vehicular traffic","role":"subject"},{"id":"b4","text":"facing the signal","role":"trigger"},{"id":"b5","text":"may enter the intersection","role":"trigger"},{"id":"b6","text":"only to make the movement indicated by the green turn arrow,","role":"sibling"},{"id":"b7","text":"but must yield the right-of-way","role":"standard"},{"id":"b9","text":"to pedestrians lawfully within an adjacent crosswalk and to other traffic lawfully using the intersection.","role":"obligation"},{"id":"b11","text":"Drivers turning in the direction of the arrow are thereby advised that so long as the turn arrow is illuminated, oncoming or opposing traffic simultaneously faces a steady red signal.","role":"definitional"}],"elements":[{"span":"b1","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"dev.traffic_signal: \"a signal head; state ∈ {circular_green, circular_yellow, circular_red, green_arrow(dir), ...}\" and \"several states may be displayed at once\": a steady red with a green turn arrow is a head displaying circular_red together with green_arrow(dir), dir left or right. No 'not a stand-in' clause applies."},{"span":"b3","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"],"derived":[],"justification":"'traffic' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic (\"pedestrians, ridden or herded animals, vehicles and other conveyances\"). The qualifier 'vehicular' leaves out pedestrians (DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian, \"a person afoot\", which the subject must not carry) and ridden or herded animals, which have no class atom; cycles and scooters stay in as 'other conveyances'."},{"span":"b4","atoms":["dev.governs","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region","st.intersection","rel.occupies"],"derived":["drv.position.entered_via"],"justification":"Facing the signal is the signal governing the approach the subject enters through: dev.governs (\"the travel regions whose traffic the device controls ... or an intersection\") on the carrier c with st.lane_enters(c, i) (\"the intersection region a directed approach carrier runs into at its entrance end\") that x came in through (drv.position.entered_via: \"x is inside region r on its current entry and came in through region c\"), or on i itself."},{"span":"b5","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.intersection"],"derived":["drv.motion.entering_region"],"justification":"drv.motion.entering_region: \"its footprint overlaps r (rel.occupies) at the observation and did not at the observation before\", r the st.intersection."},{"span":"b9","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","rel.occupies","st.crosswalk","st.entrance_of","st.lane_enters","st.intersection"],"derived":[],"justification":"The parties yielded to. 'pedestrians' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian (\"a person afoot, a person in a manual or motorized wheelchair\"); 'within an adjacent crosswalk' is the pedestrian's footprint overlapping (rel.occupies) a st.crosswalk (\"marked crossing, or the unmarked prolongation of sidewalks at an intersection\") adjacent to i: a crosswalk recorded as marking the entrance of a carrier entering i (st.entrance_of: \"the carrier whose entrance into an intersection a stop line or a crosswalk marks\"; st.lane_enters). Distance is not used for adjacency. 'other traffic' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic, every member other than x; 'using the intersection' is its footprint overlapping i (rel.occupies)."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"b7","standard":"yield the right-of-way: not proceeding where the parties' \"direction, speed and proximity\" \"give rise to the danger of a crash unless one grants precedence to the other\" (DEF-NRS-484A-210)","concepts":["drv.motion.moving","kin.speed","prim.closest_approach_within","prim.closest_approach_distance"],"params":["p.speed_resolution","p.immediate_hazard_gap","p.conflict_clearance"],"convention":"Gap-acceptance and surrogate-safety convention: the subject grants precedence where it does not proceed (it is not moving, drv.motion.moving) while a party is in danger of a crash with it; that danger is their predicted closest approach under constant velocities, within the critical gap, coming nearer than the conflict radius, so direction, speed and proximity all enter the prediction by their degree.","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[{"span":"b2","rule":"NRS_484B_307_9b_o1","map":{"x":"x"},"as":"exception"}],"residues":[{"span":"b11","why":"An advisory to drivers turning with the arrow about what opposing traffic faces at the same time; it permits, requires and forbids nothing, and no rule reads it."}],"binders":[{"name":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic"]}],"applicability":"x carries ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic and does not carry ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian; at the observation x occupies an intersection i on a passage whose entry (drv.motion.entering_region(x, i), the latest, read through a past operator) came through a carrier c with st.lane_enters(c, i) (drv.position.entered_via(x, i, c)), and at that entry a traffic signal s that governs c or i (dev.governs) displayed circular_red together with green_arrow(d), d left or right. Not engaged where NRS_484B_307_9b_o1 applies to x (composition, exception).","obligation":"Where x is moving at the observation (drv.motion.moving with p.speed_resolution): for every road user p carrying ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian that occupies a crosswalk w recorded as marking the entrance of some carrier c2 entering i (st.entrance_of(w, c2), st.lane_enters(c2, i)), and for every road user u other than x carrying ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic that occupies i, it is not the case that x and that road user approach within p.immediate_hazard_gap (prim.closest_approach_within) with a closest-approach centre distance (prim.closest_approach_distance) below p.conflict_clearance.","params":["p.speed_resolution","p.immediate_hazard_gap","p.conflict_clearance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"b9","why":"'lawfully' is not read: every pedestrian in such a crosswalk and every other member of traffic inside the intersection is yielded to. 'an adjacent crosswalk' is read as a crosswalk recorded as marking the entrance of a carrier entering the intersection; a crosswalk across the exit of a one-way leg marks no entrance and is not read.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"x (ru.motor_vehicle) entered i under circular_red with green_arrow(left) and is turning left, moving; a ru.pedestrian occupies the crosswalk that marks the entrance of the carrier on the leg x turns into, and prim.closest_approach_within holds over p.immediate_hazard_gap with a prim.closest_approach_distance below p.conflict_clearance."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"x enters i under circular_red with green_arrow(left) and turns left with no other road user in the scene."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"x enters i while s displays circular_green."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x moves through i with a pedestrian approaching in a crosswalk at the entrance of the leg x turns into, but the source does not observe s's state at x's entry.","masked":["dev.traffic_signal"]}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.speed_resolution","unit":"m/s","value":0.2,"convention":"Sensor resolution: the smallest speed the acquisition standard separates from standstill; a speed at or below it counts as no motion.","source":"speed resolution of the carla_scene_graph acquisition standard"},{"name":"p.immediate_hazard_gap","unit":"s","value":4.1,"convention":"Critical gap: the time within which another road user's arrival at the conflict area, or its predicted closest approach, counts as an immediate hazard to a road user about to cross or join its path.","source":"Highway Capacity Manual critical-gap values"},{"name":"p.conflict_clearance","unit":"m","value":3.0,"convention":"Conflict radius: the centre distance at predicted closest approach below which two road users' paths count as in conflict; about the half-length plus half-width of two passenger cars.","source":"surrogate safety measures (closest-approach conflict radius)"}],"gaps":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_307_9b_o1","law_refs":["NRS-484B-307-9b"],"subject":{"binder":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"c1","text":"Where the signal is a steady red with a green turn arrow:","role":"trigger"},{"id":"c2","text":"A person driving a motorcycle, moped or","role":"subject"},{"id":"c3","text":"trimobile","role":"subject"},{"id":"c4","text":"or riding a bicycle, an electric bicycle or an electric scooter","role":"subject"},{"id":"c5","text":"facing the signal","role":"trigger"},{"id":"c6","text":"may proceed straight through or turn in the direction opposite that indicated by the green turn arrow","role":"trigger"},{"id":"c7","text":"if:","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"c8","text":"(1) The person stops before entering the crosswalk on the nearest side of the intersection where the sign or pavement marking indicates where the stop must be made or, in the absence of any such crosswalk, sign or marking, before entering the intersection;","role":"obligation"},{"id":"c9","text":"(2) The person waits for two complete cycles of the lights or lighted arrows of the applicable official traffic-control device and the signal does not change because of a malfunction or because the signal failed to detect the presence of the motorcycle, moped, trimobile, bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter;","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c11","text":"(3) No other device at the place prohibits the turn, if applicable;","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c12","text":"and","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"c13","text":"(4) The person yields the right-of-way","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c15","text":"to pedestrians lawfully within an adjacent crosswalk and to other traffic lawfully using the intersection.","role":"sibling"}],"elements":[{"span":"c1","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"dev.traffic_signal: \"a signal head; state ∈ {... circular_red, ... green_arrow(dir) ...}\" and \"several states may be displayed at once\": a steady red with a green turn arrow is circular_red displayed together with green_arrow(dir), dir left or right. No 'not a stand-in' clause applies."},{"span":"c2","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped"],"derived":[],"justification":"The admitted aggregates DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle (\"every motor vehicle equipped with a seat or saddle for the use of the driver and designed to travel on not more than three wheels in contact with the ground\") and DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped (\"a motor-driven scooter, motor-driven cycle or similar vehicle\"), claimed by id and never expanded. 'A person driving' names who controls the machine, read through its controlled motion (observable_reading agency)."},{"span":"c4","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"],"derived":[],"justification":"The admitted aggregates DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle (\"a device propelled by human power upon which a person may ride\"), DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle (\"a device upon which a person may ride, having two or three wheels\") and DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter (\"a vehicle with handlebars and an electric motor\"). 'riding' is read through the machine's controlled motion (observable_reading agency)."},{"span":"c5","atoms":["dev.governs","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region","st.intersection","rel.occupies"],"derived":["drv.position.entered_via"],"justification":"Facing the signal is the signal governing the approach the person enters through: dev.governs (\"the travel regions whose traffic the device controls ... or an intersection\") on the carrier c with st.lane_enters(c, i) (\"the intersection region a directed approach carrier runs into at its entrance end\") that x came in through (drv.position.entered_via: \"x is inside region r on its current entry and came in through region c\"), or on i itself. dev.governs is 'not a stand-in' for a position and is not used as one."},{"span":"c6","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.intersection","kin.yaw_rate"],"derived":["drv.motion.entering_region","drv.motion.leaving_region","drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry"],"justification":"Proceeding through the intersection is the passage from x's entry (drv.motion.entering_region: \"its footprint overlaps r (rel.occupies) at the observation and did not at the observation before\") to its leaving (drv.motion.leaving_region). Straight through or a turn opposite the arrow is read at the leaving by drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry (\"The signed heading change of road user x since its footprint last began to overlap region r, in degrees, left positive\", from kin.yaw_rate): straight where its size stays below the turn recognition angle, opposite where it reaches that angle on the side away from the arrow."},{"span":"c8","atoms":["kin.speed","prim.region_offset_along","rel.occupies","st.crosswalk","st.stop_line","st.entrance_of","st.lane_enters","st.region_geometry","st.intersection","st.travel_region"],"derived":["drv.motion.halted"],"justification":"'stops', a stop required, takes DEF-NRS-484A-255 (\"complete cessation from movement\"): drv.motion.halted (kin.speed at or below the resolution). The places: the pavement marking indicating where the stop must be made is a st.stop_line (\"the transverse line marking where vehicles halt for a device\") recorded as marking x's approach carrier c (st.entrance_of: \"exactly that carrier's entrance, the line or crossing a vehicle approaching through that carrier halts at or before\"); the crosswalk on the nearest side is a st.crosswalk recorded as marking c; failing both, the entrance end of c at the st.intersection (st.lane_enters). Before entering is read along c's designated direction (prim.region_offset_along) with the distance to the place (st.region_geometry) within the stop-point tolerance, and the footprint not yet overlapping the crosswalk or the intersection (rel.occupies). st.intersection is 'not a stand-in' for a crosswalk or a stop line: each place is read on its own."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[{"span":"c3","why":"Every trimobile, a motor vehicle with a seat designed to travel on three wheels, is already a member of the motorcycle aggregate claimed on span c2, whose definition takes \"every motor vehicle equipped with a seat or saddle for the use of the driver and designed to travel on not more than three wheels in contact with the ground\": the duty is the same whether or not the word is read.","scope":"none"}],"binders":[{"name":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"]}],"applicability":"x carries ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle, ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped, ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle, ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle or ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter; at the observation x leaves an intersection i (drv.motion.leaving_region(x, i)); at the observation of its latest entry into i (drv.motion.entering_region(x, i), read through a past operator) x came in through a carrier c with st.lane_enters(c, i) (drv.position.entered_via(x, i, c)) and a traffic signal s that governs c or i (dev.governs) displayed circular_red together with green_arrow(d), d left or right; and at the leaving observation the heading change since that entry (drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry(x, i) with step p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph) shows a straight-through passage (its absolute value below p.turn_recognition_angle) or a turn opposite d (at most minus p.turn_recognition_angle where d is left, at least p.turn_recognition_angle where d is right).","obligation":"A halt before the entry, searched in the past (the approach convention). Event: x's entry into i that the applicability names, made through carrier c (the carrier x occupied at the observation before the entry with st.lane_enters(c, i)). Place, in order: a stop line recorded as marking c (st.entrance_of(line, c)); where c's marks are observed and include no stop line, a crosswalk recorded as marking c; where neither is recorded for c, the entrance end of c at i. Act: an observation at which x is halted (drv.motion.halted with p.speed_resolution) while occupying c, its body within p.stop_point_tolerance of the place (st.region_geometry distance), not past it along c's designated direction (prim.region_offset_along of the place from x not negative), and its footprint overlapping neither i nor, where the place is a crosswalk, that crosswalk. Search: back from the entry, ending at the approach start (the last observation before the entry at which x, on c, is outside the place's stopping zone upstream: off the mark, short of it and farther from it than p.stop_point_tolerance) or at x's previous entry into i through the same place; nothing else ends it. Verdict: complied where the search finds the act; violated where it reaches either end without it; unknown only where it reaches neither (the recording begins inside the approach) or where c's association with a mark, c's direction or x's place relative to the mark is unobserved and the verdict turns on it. Judged at the leaving observation, the search running from the entry.","params":["p.speed_resolution","p.stop_point_tolerance","p.turn_recognition_angle","p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph"],"narrowings":[{"span":"c2","why":"'A person driving' is read through the machine's controlled motion: the duty binds the motorcycle's or moped's conduct whoever controls it.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"c4","why":"'riding' is read through the machine's controlled motion: the duty binds the conduct of the bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter whoever rides it.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"c8","why":"The places are read in the order the words give them under the ontology's approach convention: the pavement marking indicating where the stop must be made is the stop line marking the approach; failing one, the crosswalk on the near side is the crosswalk marking the approach; failing both, the entrance of the intersection. A sign that indicates a stopping point without a line is not carried by any atom and is not read.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"x (ru.motorcycle) approaches i on lane c, which a stop line marks (st.entrance_of); it never halts on c, enters i while s governing c displays circular_red with green_arrow(left), and leaves straight through. The search back from the entry reaches the approach start without a halt."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"x (ru.bicycle) halts on c within p.stop_point_tolerance of the stop line marking c, short of it, then enters i under circular_red with green_arrow(left) and leaves straight through."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"x (ru.motorcycle) enters i while s displays circular_green and leaves straight through."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x halts on c short of a stop line within p.stop_point_tolerance and then goes straight through under circular_red with green_arrow(left), but the source does not observe which carriers the line marks, so whether the halt was at the governing place is unknown.","masked":["st.entrance_of"]},{"name":"history_boundary","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x's recording begins with x already on c inside the stopping zone of the stop line, rolling slowly; no halt is recorded before it enters i under circular_red with green_arrow(left) and leaves straight through. The search reaches neither the approach start nor a previous entry.","boundary":"the start of x's approach on c, outside the stop line's stopping zone upstream, which lies before the recording"}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.speed_resolution","unit":"m/s","value":0.2,"convention":"Sensor resolution: the smallest speed the acquisition standard separates from standstill; a speed at or below it counts as no motion.","source":"speed resolution of the carla_scene_graph acquisition standard"},{"name":"p.stop_point_tolerance","unit":"m","value":2.0,"convention":"Stop-point tolerance: the largest ground distance between a halted body and the line, crossing or intersection edge at which the halt counts as made at that place; a body farther upstream is outside the stopping zone.","source":"MUTCD stop-line placement practice"},{"name":"p.turn_recognition_angle","unit":"deg","value":45,"convention":"Turn recognition: the heading change through an intersection beyond which a passage counts as a turn rather than a straight crossing; half the right angle of a turn at a right-angled junction, leaving room for skewed junctions and lane offsets.","source":"intersection geometry design conventions (AASHTO Green Book)"}],"gaps":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_307_9b_o2","law_refs":["NRS-484B-307-9b"],"subject":{"binder":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"c1","text":"Where the signal is a steady red with a green turn arrow:","role":"trigger"},{"id":"c2","text":"A person driving a motorcycle, moped or","role":"subject"},{"id":"c3","text":"trimobile","role":"subject"},{"id":"c4","text":"or riding a bicycle, an electric bicycle or an electric scooter","role":"subject"},{"id":"c5","text":"facing the signal","role":"trigger"},{"id":"c6","text":"may proceed straight through or turn in the direction opposite that indicated by the green turn arrow","role":"trigger"},{"id":"c7","text":"if:","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"c8","text":"(1) The person stops before entering the crosswalk on the nearest side of the intersection where the sign or pavement marking indicates where the stop must be made or, in the absence of any such crosswalk, sign or marking, before entering the intersection;","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c9","text":"(2) The person waits for two complete cycles of the lights or lighted arrows of the applicable official traffic-control device and the signal does not change because of a malfunction or because the signal failed to detect the presence of the motorcycle, moped, trimobile, bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter;","role":"obligation"},{"id":"c11","text":"(3) No other device at the place prohibits the turn, if applicable;","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c12","text":"and","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"c13","text":"(4) The person yields the right-of-way","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c15","text":"to pedestrians lawfully within an adjacent crosswalk and to other traffic lawfully using the intersection.","role":"sibling"}],"elements":[{"span":"c1","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"dev.traffic_signal: \"a signal head; state ∈ {... circular_red, ... green_arrow(dir) ...}\" and \"several states may be displayed at once\": a steady red with a green turn arrow is circular_red displayed together with green_arrow(dir), dir left or right."},{"span":"c2","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped"],"derived":[],"justification":"The admitted aggregates DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle (\"every motor vehicle equipped with a seat or saddle for the use of the driver and designed to travel on not more than three wheels in contact with the ground\") and DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped (\"a motor-driven scooter, motor-driven cycle or similar vehicle\"), claimed by id. 'A person driving' is read through the machine's controlled motion."},{"span":"c4","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"],"derived":[],"justification":"The admitted aggregates DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle (\"a device propelled by human power upon which a person may ride\"), DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle (\"a device upon which a person may ride, having two or three wheels\") and DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter (\"a vehicle with handlebars and an electric motor\")."},{"span":"c5","atoms":["dev.governs","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region","st.intersection","rel.occupies"],"derived":["drv.position.entered_via"],"justification":"Facing the signal: dev.governs (\"the travel regions whose traffic the device controls ... or an intersection\") on the carrier c with st.lane_enters(c, i) that x came in through (drv.position.entered_via: \"came in through region c\"), or on i itself."},{"span":"c6","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.intersection","kin.yaw_rate"],"derived":["drv.motion.entering_region","drv.motion.leaving_region","drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry"],"justification":"The passage from x's entry into i (drv.motion.entering_region) to its leaving (drv.motion.leaving_region); straight through or opposite the arrow is read at the leaving by drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry (\"in degrees, left positive\", from kin.yaw_rate) against the turn recognition angle."},{"span":"c9","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal","dev.governs","kin.speed","rel.occupies","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region"],"derived":["drv.motion.halted"],"justification":"Waiting is remaining halted (drv.motion.halted: \"complete cessation from movement\", kin.speed at or below the resolution) on the approach carrier c (rel.occupies, st.lane_enters). The applicable official traffic-control device is the signal s facing x (dev.governs on c or i; its presence is the evidence of its official status). A complete cycle of its lights is the span between two successive rises of the same display; the rises of s's circular_red with green_arrow(d) display (dev.traffic_signal) are counted from the start of the wait, the first rise opening the first complete cycle, so two complete cycles need more rises than the literal. That the signal does not change because it malfunctions or fails to detect x is read through its outcome on the head: during the wait s never displays an indication permitting x's movement, neither circular_green nor a green_arrow in the direction of x's movement (dev.traffic_signal state). Why the head stayed as it was (a fault, a detector) is not observable."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[{"span":"c3","why":"Every trimobile, a motor vehicle with a seat designed to travel on three wheels, is already a member of the motorcycle aggregate claimed on span c2 (\"every motor vehicle equipped with a seat or saddle for the use of the driver and designed to travel on not more than three wheels in contact with the ground\"): the duty is the same whether or not the word is read.","scope":"none"}],"binders":[{"name":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"]}],"applicability":"As NRS_484B_307_9b_o1: x carries one of the five aggregates of spans c2 and c4; at the observation x leaves intersection i (drv.motion.leaving_region(x, i)); at its latest entry into i (read through a past operator) it came in through carrier c with st.lane_enters(c, i) (drv.position.entered_via(x, i, c)) while a traffic signal s that governs c or i (dev.governs) displayed circular_red together with green_arrow(d), d left or right; and at the leaving the heading change since that entry (drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry(x, i) with step p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph) shows a straight-through passage (absolute value below p.turn_recognition_angle) or a turn opposite d.","obligation":"Read at the observation of x's latest entry into i, through a past operator from the leaving observation. Let the wait be the latest run of consecutive observations before the entry at which x is halted (drv.motion.halted with p.speed_resolution) while occupying c. Counted from the start of that run (Formula.count with edge: s displays circular_red together with green_arrow(d) and did not at the observation before; since: x halted while occupying c), the rises of that display number more than the literal of span c9 (comparison gt): the first rise counted opens the first complete cycle and each later one closes a cycle. And at no observation of the wait does s display circular_green, or green_arrow in the direction of x's movement (straight for a straight-through passage, the side of the turn for a turn). Where the wait began before the recording (x halted on c at its first observation), the count is unknown, not a violation.","params":["p.speed_resolution","p.turn_recognition_angle","p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph"],"narrowings":[{"span":"c2","why":"'A person driving' is read through the machine's controlled motion.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"c4","why":"'riding' is read through the machine's controlled motion.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"c9","why":"'the applicable official traffic-control device' is the signal head governing the person's approach; its presence on the road is read as the evidence of its official status.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"status"},{"span":"c9","why":"'does not change because of a malfunction or because the signal failed to detect the presence' turns on the device's detection, which is not observable; it is read through the outcome the condition secures: throughout the wait the head never displays an indication that permits the person's movement. A wait the signal ends by serving the person is not a failure to detect, and the permission then does not cover a later entry against the red.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"perception"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"x (ru.motorcycle) halts on c; s governing c rises to circular_red with green_arrow(left) once during the wait; x then enters i under that display and leaves straight through: the rises counted do not exceed the literal."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"x (ru.bicycle) halts on c and stays halted while s's circular_red with green_arrow(left) display rises more times than the literal, never showing circular_green or green_arrow(straight); x then enters under the display and leaves straight through."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"x is a ru.motor_vehicle that carries none of the five aggregates (a passenger car); it waits and then goes straight through under circular_red with green_arrow(left)."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x halts on c, waits and then goes straight through, but the source does not observe s's state during the wait.","masked":["dev.traffic_signal"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"violated","narrative":"x halts on c through more rises of circular_red with green_arrow(left) than the literal, but during the wait s also displays circular_green for c, which x lets pass; x later enters straight through under the red with the arrow: the signal did change, so the condition fails."},{"name":"history_boundary","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x's recording begins with x already halted on c; a single rise of circular_red with green_arrow(left) is recorded before x enters i straight through, and the start of the wait is not recorded.","boundary":"the start of x's halt on c, which lies before the recording"}],"literals":[{"span":"c9","text":"two","value":2,"unit":"count"}],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.speed_resolution","unit":"m/s","value":0.2,"convention":"Sensor resolution: the smallest speed the acquisition standard separates from standstill; a speed at or below it counts as no motion.","source":"speed resolution of the carla_scene_graph acquisition standard"},{"name":"p.turn_recognition_angle","unit":"deg","value":45,"convention":"Turn recognition: the heading change through an intersection beyond which a passage counts as a turn rather than a straight crossing; half the right angle of a turn at a right-angled junction, leaving room for skewed junctions and lane offsets.","source":"intersection geometry design conventions (AASHTO Green Book)"}],"gaps":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_307_9b_o3","law_refs":["NRS-484B-307-9b"],"subject":{"binder":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"c1","text":"Where the signal is a steady red with a green turn arrow:","role":"trigger"},{"id":"c2","text":"A person driving a motorcycle, moped or","role":"subject"},{"id":"c3","text":"trimobile","role":"subject"},{"id":"c4","text":"or riding a bicycle, an electric bicycle or an electric scooter","role":"subject"},{"id":"c5","text":"facing the signal","role":"trigger"},{"id":"c6","text":"may proceed straight through or turn in the direction opposite that indicated by the green turn arrow","role":"trigger"},{"id":"c7","text":"if:","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"c8","text":"(1) The person stops before entering the crosswalk on the nearest side of the intersection where the sign or pavement marking indicates where the stop must be made or, in the absence of any such crosswalk, sign or marking, before entering the intersection;","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c9","text":"(2) The person waits for two complete cycles of the lights or lighted arrows of the applicable official traffic-control device and the signal does not change because of a malfunction or because the signal failed to detect the presence of the motorcycle, moped, trimobile, bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter;","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c11","text":"(3) No other device at the place prohibits the turn, if applicable;","role":"obligation"},{"id":"c12","text":"and","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"c13","text":"(4) The person yields the right-of-way","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c15","text":"to pedestrians lawfully within an adjacent crosswalk and to other traffic lawfully using the intersection.","role":"sibling"}],"elements":[{"span":"c1","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"dev.traffic_signal: \"several states may be displayed at once\": circular_red displayed together with green_arrow(dir), dir left or right."},{"span":"c2","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped"],"derived":[],"justification":"The admitted aggregates DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle (\"every motor vehicle equipped with a seat or saddle for the use of the driver\") and DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped (\"a motor-driven scooter, motor-driven cycle or similar vehicle\"), claimed by id."},{"span":"c4","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"],"derived":[],"justification":"The admitted aggregates DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle (\"a device propelled by human power upon which a person may ride\"), DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle (\"a device upon which a person may ride, having two or three wheels\") and DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter (\"a vehicle with handlebars and an electric motor\")."},{"span":"c5","atoms":["dev.governs","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region","st.intersection","rel.occupies"],"derived":["drv.position.entered_via"],"justification":"Facing the signal: dev.governs (\"the travel regions whose traffic the device controls ... or an intersection\") on the carrier c with st.lane_enters(c, i) that x came in through (drv.position.entered_via), or on i itself."},{"span":"c6","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.intersection","kin.yaw_rate"],"derived":["drv.motion.entering_region","drv.motion.leaving_region","drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry"],"justification":"The passage from x's entry into i to its leaving; straight through or opposite the arrow read at the leaving by drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry (\"in degrees, left positive\", from kin.yaw_rate) against the turn recognition angle."},{"span":"c11","atoms":["dev.regulatory_sign","dev.traffic_signal","dev.governs","prim.conditions_hold","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region","st.intersection"],"derived":[],"justification":"A device at the place that prohibits the turn: a dev.regulatory_sign (\"a point regulation by catalogue code\") of code no_left_turn for a left turn or no_right_turn for a right turn, whose structured conditions hold for x at the entry (prim.conditions_hold: \"the structured conditions of a device ... hold at the observation for a road user\"), or a traffic signal head displaying red_arrow(dir) in the turn's direction (dev.traffic_signal); either governing (dev.governs) the carrier c x entered through (st.lane_enters(c, i)) or the intersection i. 'if applicable': a straight-through passage makes no turn, and the condition is met. A prohibition sign is 'not a stand-in' for a manoeuvre: it is read as the condition it is."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[{"span":"c3","why":"Every trimobile, a motor vehicle with a seat designed to travel on three wheels, is already a member of the motorcycle aggregate claimed on span c2 (\"every motor vehicle equipped with a seat or saddle for the use of the driver and designed to travel on not more than three wheels in contact with the ground\"): the duty is the same whether or not the word is read.","scope":"none"}],"binders":[{"name":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"]}],"applicability":"As NRS_484B_307_9b_o1: x carries one of the five aggregates of spans c2 and c4; at the observation x leaves intersection i (drv.motion.leaving_region(x, i)); at its latest entry into i (read through a past operator) it came in through carrier c with st.lane_enters(c, i) (drv.position.entered_via(x, i, c)) while a traffic signal s that governs c or i (dev.governs) displayed circular_red together with green_arrow(d), d left or right; and at the leaving the heading change since that entry (drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry(x, i) with step p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph) shows a straight-through passage (absolute value below p.turn_recognition_angle) or a turn opposite d.","obligation":"Where the passage is a turn (the heading change since the entry at least p.turn_recognition_angle in absolute value; its sign gives the side): at the observation of x's entry into i (read through a past operator) no device governing c or i (dev.governs) prohibits a turn to that side: no dev.regulatory_sign of code no_left_turn (for a left turn) or no_right_turn (for a right turn) whose conditions hold for x there (prim.conditions_hold), and no traffic signal head displaying red_arrow toward that side. A straight-through passage meets this condition.","params":["p.turn_recognition_angle","p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph"],"narrowings":[{"span":"c2","why":"'A person driving' is read through the machine's controlled motion.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"c4","why":"'riding' is read through the machine's controlled motion.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"c11","why":"'No other device at the place prohibits the turn' is read as the turn prohibitions the closed set carries: a no-left-turn or no-right-turn sign whose posted conditions hold, or a red arrow toward the turn's side, governing the approach or the intersection, at the entry.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"x (ru.motorcycle) enters i through c under circular_red with green_arrow(left) and turns right; a dev.regulatory_sign of code no_right_turn with empty conditions governs c."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"x (ru.bicycle) enters i through c under circular_red with green_arrow(left) and turns right; no sign or red arrow prohibiting a right turn governs c or i."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"x (ru.motorcycle) enters under circular_red with green_arrow(left) and turns left, the movement the arrow indicates."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x turns right under circular_red with green_arrow(left); a no_right_turn sign stands at the approach but the source does not observe which regions it governs.","masked":["dev.governs"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"compliant","narrative":"x (ru.moped) enters under circular_red with green_arrow(left) and goes straight through while a no_right_turn sign governs c: no turn is made, so the condition is met."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.turn_recognition_angle","unit":"deg","value":45,"convention":"Turn recognition: the heading change through an intersection beyond which a passage counts as a turn rather than a straight crossing; half the right angle of a turn at a right-angled junction, leaving room for skewed junctions and lane offsets.","source":"intersection geometry design conventions (AASHTO Green Book)"}],"gaps":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_307_9b_o4","law_refs":["NRS-484B-307-9b"],"subject":{"binder":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"c1","text":"Where the signal is a steady red with a green turn arrow:","role":"trigger"},{"id":"c2","text":"A person driving a motorcycle, moped or","role":"subject"},{"id":"c3","text":"trimobile","role":"subject"},{"id":"c4","text":"or riding a bicycle, an electric bicycle or an electric scooter","role":"subject"},{"id":"c5","text":"facing the signal","role":"trigger"},{"id":"c6","text":"may proceed straight through or turn in the direction opposite that indicated by the green turn arrow","role":"trigger"},{"id":"c7","text":"if:","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"c8","text":"(1) The person stops before entering the crosswalk on the nearest side of the intersection where the sign or pavement marking indicates where the stop must be made or, in the absence of any such crosswalk, sign or marking, before entering the intersection;","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c9","text":"(2) The person waits for two complete cycles of the lights or lighted arrows of the applicable official traffic-control device and the signal does not change because of a malfunction or because the signal failed to detect the presence of the motorcycle, moped, trimobile, bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter;","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c11","text":"(3) No other device at the place prohibits the turn, if applicable;","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c12","text":"and","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"c13","text":"(4) The person yields the right-of-way","role":"standard"},{"id":"c15","text":"to pedestrians lawfully within an adjacent crosswalk and to other traffic lawfully using the intersection.","role":"obligation"}],"elements":[{"span":"c1","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"dev.traffic_signal: \"several states may be displayed at once\": circular_red displayed together with green_arrow(dir), dir left or right."},{"span":"c2","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped"],"derived":[],"justification":"The admitted aggregates DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle (\"every motor vehicle equipped with a seat or saddle for the use of the driver\") and DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped (\"a motor-driven scooter, motor-driven cycle or similar vehicle\"), claimed by id."},{"span":"c4","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"],"derived":[],"justification":"The admitted aggregates DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle (\"a device propelled by human power upon which a person may ride\"), DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle (\"a device upon which a person may ride, having two or three wheels\") and DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter (\"a vehicle with handlebars and an electric motor\")."},{"span":"c5","atoms":["dev.governs","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region","st.intersection","rel.occupies"],"derived":["drv.position.entered_via"],"justification":"Facing the signal: dev.governs (\"the travel regions whose traffic the device controls ... or an intersection\") on the carrier c with st.lane_enters(c, i) that x came in through (drv.position.entered_via), or on i itself."},{"span":"c6","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.intersection","kin.yaw_rate"],"derived":["drv.motion.entering_region","drv.motion.leaving_region","drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry"],"justification":"The passage from x's entry into i to its leaving; straight through or opposite the arrow read at the leaving by drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry (\"in degrees, left positive\", from kin.yaw_rate) against the turn recognition angle."},{"span":"c15","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","rel.occupies","st.crosswalk","st.entrance_of","st.lane_enters","st.intersection"],"derived":[],"justification":"The parties yielded to. 'pedestrians' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian (\"a person afoot, a person in a manual or motorized wheelchair\"); 'within an adjacent crosswalk' is the pedestrian's footprint overlapping (rel.occupies) a st.crosswalk recorded as marking the entrance of a carrier entering i (st.entrance_of: \"the carrier whose entrance into an intersection a stop line or a crosswalk marks\"; st.lane_enters). Distance is not used for adjacency. 'other traffic' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic (\"pedestrians, ridden or herded animals, vehicles and other conveyances\"), every member other than x; 'using the intersection' is its footprint overlapping i (rel.occupies)."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"c13","standard":"yields the right-of-way: not proceeding where the parties' \"direction, speed and proximity\" \"give rise to the danger of a crash unless one grants precedence to the other\" (DEF-NRS-484A-210)","concepts":["drv.motion.moving","kin.speed","prim.closest_approach_within","prim.closest_approach_distance"],"params":["p.speed_resolution","p.immediate_hazard_gap","p.conflict_clearance"],"convention":"Gap-acceptance and surrogate-safety convention: the person grants precedence where they do not proceed (not moving, drv.motion.moving) while a party is in danger of a crash with them; that danger is the predicted closest approach under constant velocities, within the critical gap, coming nearer than the conflict radius, so direction, speed and proximity all enter the prediction by their degree.","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[{"span":"c3","why":"Every trimobile, a motor vehicle with a seat designed to travel on three wheels, is already a member of the motorcycle aggregate claimed on span c2 (\"every motor vehicle equipped with a seat or saddle for the use of the driver and designed to travel on not more than three wheels in contact with the ground\"): the duty is the same whether or not the word is read.","scope":"none"}],"binders":[{"name":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"]}],"applicability":"As NRS_484B_307_9b_o1: x carries one of the five aggregates of spans c2 and c4; at the observation x leaves intersection i (drv.motion.leaving_region(x, i)); at its latest entry into i (read through a past operator) it came in through carrier c with st.lane_enters(c, i) (drv.position.entered_via(x, i, c)) while a traffic signal s that governs c or i (dev.governs) displayed circular_red together with green_arrow(d), d left or right; and at the leaving the heading change since that entry (drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry(x, i) with step p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph) shows a straight-through passage (absolute value below p.turn_recognition_angle) or a turn opposite d.","obligation":"At every observation from that entry up to the leaving (read through a past operator from the leaving observation) at which x occupies i and is moving (drv.motion.moving with p.speed_resolution): for every road user p carrying ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian that occupies a crosswalk w recorded as marking the entrance of some carrier c2 entering i (st.entrance_of(w, c2), st.lane_enters(c2, i)), and for every road user u other than x carrying ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic that occupies i, it is not the case that x and that road user approach within p.immediate_hazard_gap (prim.closest_approach_within) with a closest-approach centre distance (prim.closest_approach_distance) below p.conflict_clearance.","params":["p.speed_resolution","p.immediate_hazard_gap","p.conflict_clearance","p.turn_recognition_angle","p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph"],"narrowings":[{"span":"c2","why":"'A person driving' is read through the machine's controlled motion.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"c4","why":"'riding' is read through the machine's controlled motion.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"c15","why":"'lawfully' is not read: every pedestrian in such a crosswalk and every other member of traffic inside the intersection is yielded to. 'an adjacent crosswalk' is read as a crosswalk recorded as marking the entrance of a carrier entering the intersection; a crosswalk across the exit of a one-way leg is not read.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"x (ru.motorcycle) goes straight through i under circular_red with green_arrow(left); while it moves inside i a ru.pedestrian occupies the crosswalk at the far side, marking the entrance of the opposing carrier, and prim.closest_approach_within holds over p.immediate_hazard_gap with a prim.closest_approach_distance below p.conflict_clearance."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"x (ru.bicycle) goes straight through i under circular_red with green_arrow(left) with no other road user in the scene."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"x (ru.motorcycle) enters i under circular_red with green_arrow(left) and turns left, the movement the arrow indicates."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x goes straight through i under circular_red with green_arrow(left) near a crossing pedestrian, but the source does not observe x's footprint overlap with i.","masked":["rel.occupies"]}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.speed_resolution","unit":"m/s","value":0.2,"convention":"Sensor resolution: the smallest speed the acquisition standard separates from standstill; a speed at or below it counts as no motion.","source":"speed resolution of the carla_scene_graph acquisition standard"},{"name":"p.immediate_hazard_gap","unit":"s","value":4.1,"convention":"Critical gap: the time within which another road user's arrival at the conflict area, or its predicted closest approach, counts as an immediate hazard to a road user about to cross or join its path.","source":"Highway Capacity Manual critical-gap values"},{"name":"p.conflict_clearance","unit":"m","value":3.0,"convention":"Conflict radius: the centre distance at predicted closest approach below which two road users' paths count as in conflict; about the half-length plus half-width of two passenger cars.","source":"surrogate safety measures (closest-approach conflict radius)"},{"name":"p.turn_recognition_angle","unit":"deg","value":45,"convention":"Turn recognition: the heading change through an intersection beyond which a passage counts as a turn rather than a straight crossing; half the right angle of a turn at a right-angled junction, leaving room for skewed junctions and lane offsets.","source":"intersection geometry design conventions (AASHTO Green Book)"}],"gaps":[]}
{"concept_id":"drv.motion.u_turn","kind":"formula","contract":"Road user x has turned so as to proceed in the opposite direction: the turning that the corpus defines as \"the turning of a vehicle upon a highway so as to proceed in the opposite direction, whether accomplished by one continuous movement or not\", observed as a reversal of x's heading. It holds at an observation where the absolute value of x's signed heading change over the window behind it (prim.heading_change with window; degrees, left positive) differs from the literal half turn by no more than reversal_tolerance: the heading now points the opposite way within the tolerance, and a heading change that has gone past the half turn by more than the tolerance (a loop back toward the first direction) does not count. A turning made in several movements, forward and backing, counts, since the heading change is integrated through all of them. The act begins within the window behind the observation of recognition; it is recognized at the observation at which this condition rises; it holds at the later observations at which the reversal still lies within the window behind them, which are not the act again, and it ends when the reversal leaves that window. Unknown where the window is truncated, sampled too sparsely, or a yaw rate is missing. Not denoted: a turning by less than a reversal, or the place of the turning: the caller states the highway or the zone.","definition":"DEF-NRS-484B-077","args":[{"name":"x","sort":"track"}],"params":[{"name":"window","unit":"s","meaning":"the longest time over which a reversal of heading, in one movement or several, is recognized as one turning: the window behind the observation over which the heading change is integrated"},{"name":"reversal_tolerance","unit":"deg","meaning":"the largest difference between the size of the heading change and the half turn within which the road user counts as proceeding in the opposite direction"}],"act":{"boundary":"window","window":"window","onset":"The act begins within the window behind the observation of recognition","recognition":"it is recognized at the observation at which this condition rises","extent":"it holds at the later observations at which the reversal still lies within the window behind them, which are not the act again, and it ends when the reversal leaves that window","history":"Unknown where the window is truncated, sampled too sparsely, or a yaw rate is missing"},"elements":[{"span":"the absolute value of x's signed heading change over the window behind it (prim.heading_change with window; degrees, left positive)","atoms":["prim.heading_change"],"concepts":[],"justification":"prim.heading_change: \"the signed heading change (degrees, left positive) of a road user over the window behind the observation, integrated from kin.yaw_rate; unknown where the window is truncated, sampled too sparsely, or a yaw rate is missing\"; its window is the formal window. Integration through forward and backing movements carries \"whether accomplished by one continuous movement or not\"."}],"residues":[{"span":"upon a highway","why":"The place is the caller's: the concept reads x's heading only, and the calling rule states the region (the highway or the zone) the turning is made in."},{"span":"so as to proceed in the opposite direction","why":"Read as the reversal of x's own heading. A road user following a bend of the way that itself turns through a half turn within the window also reverses its heading; no atom of the closed set states the course of the way along x's path, so the two are not told apart."}],"literals":[{"value":180,"unit":"deg","why":"the half turn: a heading pointing the opposite way"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"holds","expected":"compliant","narrative":"x drives along a street, swings left across the centre line and completes the turning heading the opposite way within the window; the size of prim.heading_change differs from the half turn by less than reversal_tolerance."},{"name":"fails","expected":"violated","narrative":"x turns right at a junction; the size of prim.heading_change over the window is about a quarter turn."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x reverses its heading, but its yaw rate is missing during the window.","masked":["kin.yaw_rate"]}],"used_by":["NRS_484B_363_3"],"supersedes":null}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_363_3","law_refs":["NRS-484B-363-3"],"subject":{"binder":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"d1","text":"The driver of a vehicle","role":"subject"},{"id":"d2","text":"shall not make a U-turn","role":"obligation"},{"id":"d3","text":"in an area designated as a school zone or school crossing zone","role":"trigger"},{"id":"d4","text":"except:","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"d5","text":"(a) When there are no children present;","role":"exception"},{"id":"d6","text":"(b) On a day on which school is not in session;","role":"exception"},{"id":"d7","text":"(c) During the period from a half hour after school is no longer in operation to a half hour before school is next in operation;","role":"exception"},{"id":"d8","text":"(d) If the zone is designated by an operational speed limit beacon,","role":"exception"},{"id":"d9","text":"during the hours when the pupils of the school are in class","role":"exception"},{"id":"d10","text":"and the yellow lights of the speed limit beacon are not flashing in the manner which indicates that the speed limit is in effect;","role":"exception"},{"id":"d11","text":"or","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"d12","text":"(e) If the zone is not designated by an operational speed limit beacon,","role":"exception"},{"id":"d13","text":"during the times when the sign designating the school zone or school crossing zone indicates that the speed limit is not in effect.","role":"exception"},{"id":"d14","text":"As used in this section, “speed limit beacon” means a device which is used in conjunction with a sign and equipped with two or more yellow lights that flash alternately to indicate when the speed limit in a school zone or school crossing zone is in effect.","role":"definitional"}],"elements":[{"span":"d1","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle (\"every device in, upon or by which any person or property is or may be transported or drawn upon a highway\", with its exceptions), claimed by id. 'The driver of' names who controls it (DEF-NRS-484A-080, \"every person who drives or is in actual physical control of a vehicle\"), a role read through the vehicle's controlled motion (observable_reading agency), not a membership."},{"span":"d2","atoms":["prim.heading_change"],"derived":["drv.motion.u_turn"],"justification":"'U-turn' is defined by DEF-NRS-484B-077 (\"the turning of a vehicle upon a highway so as to proceed in the opposite direction, whether accomplished by one continuous movement or not\"); the proposed definition-born concept drv.motion.u_turn carries it, recognizing the reversal of x's heading over a window through prim.heading_change. The place, upon a highway inside the zone, is stated by span d3."},{"span":"d3","atoms":["dev.zone_sign","dev.governs","rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"A school zone or school crossing zone (DEF-NRS-484B-063 \"those sections of streets which are adjacent to school property\"; DEF-NRS-484B-060) is a legal region class that is also marked on the road; the ontology's section on what is not an atom: \"Where the same category is also marked on the road by a sign (dev.zone_sign), the sign is the atom and the category is not.\" dev.zone_sign: \"a sign that begins or ends a signed zone along the road; kind ∈ {school, school_crossing, ...}\". The area designated is the travel regions the sign governs (dev.governs: \"the travel regions whose traffic the device controls\"), and x is in it where its footprint overlaps one (rel.occupies). dev.zone_sign is 'not a stand-in' for whether its condition holds now; that is read only in span d13 through prim.conditions_hold."},{"span":"d5","atoms":["ru.child","st.region_geometry","dev.zone_sign","dev.governs","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"Children present in the zone: a road user of class ru.child (\"pedestrian who is visibly a child\") whose body lies within the presence reach of a travel region the zone sign governs (st.region_geometry: \"the ground distance from a road user's body outline to it (zero when they overlap)\"), so that children on the sidewalks beside the zone's lanes count. A reach relates the region to the child, not two regions. No children present: no such road user."},{"span":"d8","atoms":["dev.speed_limit_beacon","dev.governs","rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"The zone designated by a speed limit beacon: a dev.speed_limit_beacon (\"a pair or more of yellow lamps mounted with a speed sign, flashing alternately when the sign's limit is in effect\", which is the section's own definition in span d14) governing (dev.governs) the travel region x occupies (rel.occupies) or a region the zone sign governs. 'operational' is read through the beacon's presence (observable_reading status)."},{"span":"d10","atoms":["dev.speed_limit_beacon"],"derived":[],"justification":"dev.speed_limit_beacon \"flashing attribute\": the beacon's lights not flashing in the manner that indicates the limit is in effect is its flashing attribute false."},{"span":"d12","atoms":["dev.speed_limit_beacon","dev.governs","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"A zone not designated by a speed limit beacon: no dev.speed_limit_beacon governs (dev.governs) the travel region x occupies or a region the zone sign governs."},{"span":"d13","atoms":["dev.zone_sign","prim.conditions_hold"],"derived":[],"justification":"The sign designating the zone is the dev.zone_sign of span d3, whose \"conditions attribute: a structured reading of the sign's legend\" states when its limit is in effect; that it indicates the limit is not in effect is prim.conditions_hold (\"the structured conditions of a device ... hold at the observation for a road user\") false for x. The sign is 'not a stand-in' for the condition holding, which is why the primitive reads it."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[{"span":"d6","id":"asm.school_not_in_session_day","meaning":"The calendar day of the observation is one on which the school the zone serves is not in session, as declared for the map or the trace."},{"span":"d7","id":"asm.outside_school_operation_margin","meaning":"The time of the observation lies at least a half hour after the school the zone serves last ceased operation and at least a half hour before it next begins operation, as declared for the map or the trace."},{"span":"d9","id":"asm.pupils_in_class","meaning":"The time of the observation lies within the hours during which the pupils of the school the zone serves are in class, as declared for the map or the trace."}],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[{"span":"d14","why":"The section's own definition of a speed limit beacon; dev.speed_limit_beacon's contract (\"a pair or more of yellow lamps mounted with a speed sign, flashing alternately when the sign's limit is in effect\") already states it, and the elements of spans d8, d10 and d12 read that atom; it imposes no duty of its own."}],"binders":[{"name":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"x carries ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; at the observation x's U-turn is recognized (drv.motion.u_turn(x) with p.u_turn_window and p.u_turn_reversal_tolerance rises there); and at some observation of that act (an observation within p.u_turn_window behind the recognition at which x yaws, drv.motion.yawing with p.yaw_rate_resolution) x's footprint overlapped a travel region r governed (dev.governs) by a dev.zone_sign z of kind school or school_crossing that is not an end sign.","obligation":"The U-turn is made only where one exception covers the whole act: for one of the alternatives below, that alternative holds at every observation of the act (each observation within p.u_turn_window behind the recognition at which x yaws). (a) No road user of class ru.child lies within p.child_presence_reach (st.region_geometry distance) of a travel region z governs. (b) asm.school_not_in_session_day holds. (c) asm.outside_school_operation_margin holds. (d) A dev.speed_limit_beacon governs the region x occupies or a region z governs, asm.pupils_in_class holds, and that beacon is not flashing. (e) No dev.speed_limit_beacon governs the region x occupies or a region z governs, and z's conditions do not hold for x (prim.conditions_hold false). Where none of them covers the whole act, the duty is violated.","params":["p.u_turn_window","p.u_turn_reversal_tolerance","p.yaw_rate_resolution","p.child_presence_reach"],"narrowings":[{"span":"d1","why":"'The driver of a vehicle' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion: the duty binds the vehicle's conduct whoever or whatever controls it.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"d3","why":"'an area designated as a school zone or school crossing zone' is read through the zone sign on the road and the travel regions it governs; the designation is presumed from the sign's presence.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"status"},{"span":"d8","why":"'operational' is read through the beacon's presence governing the zone's regions; a beacon that is installed but out of order is not told apart.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"status"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"x (ru.motor_vehicle) makes a U-turn on a lane governed by a school zone sign z; a ru.child stands within p.child_presence_reach of z's lane at every observation, asm.school_not_in_session_day and asm.outside_school_operation_margin are declared false, and a speed limit beacon governing the lane is flashing."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"x makes a U-turn on z's lane while no ru.child lies within p.child_presence_reach of any region z governs at any observation of the act."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"x makes a U-turn on a street no school zone or school crossing zone sign governs."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x drives along z's lane with children on the sidewalk and turns about, but its yaw rate is missing, so whether a U-turn was made is unknown.","masked":["kin.yaw_rate"]},{"name":"occasion_d3","expected":"violated","narrative":"Baseline as in forbid (children present, school in session, inside the operation margin, beacon flashing): x begins its U-turn on z's lane and completes it on a lane beyond the stretch z governs; it occupied z's lane for part of the act only."},{"name":"occasion_d3_outside","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"x drove along z's lane, left the governed stretch, and only afterwards, on a lane no zone sign governs, makes its U-turn: it was in the zone before the act began only."},{"name":"occasion_d5","expected":"violated","narrative":"U-turn on z's lane; no ru.child is within p.child_presence_reach at the first observations of the act, then a child walks up beside the lane before the act is recognized; the other alternatives fail throughout."},{"name":"occasion_d5_outside","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Children stood beside z's lane before the act began and left; at every observation of the U-turn none lies within p.child_presence_reach; the other alternatives fail."},{"name":"occasion_d8","expected":"violated","narrative":"A beacon governs the region x occupies at the start of the U-turn only; x ends the turn on a region no beacon governs; asm.pupils_in_class holds and the beacon is not flashing; z's conditions hold; children present, school in session, inside the margin: neither (d) nor (e) covers the whole act."},{"name":"occasion_d8_outside","expected":"compliant","narrative":"No beacon governs the region x occupied before the act; a non-flashing beacon governs every region x occupies during the U-turn and asm.pupils_in_class holds throughout it; children present."},{"name":"occasion_d10","expected":"violated","narrative":"A beacon governs z's lane and asm.pupils_in_class holds throughout; the beacon is not flashing for the first part of the U-turn and flashing for the rest; children present."},{"name":"occasion_d10_outside","expected":"compliant","narrative":"A beacon governs z's lane and asm.pupils_in_class holds throughout; the beacon was flashing before the act and is not flashing at any observation of the U-turn; children present."},{"name":"occasion_d12","expected":"violated","narrative":"No beacon governs the region x occupies at the start of the U-turn, a flashing beacon governs the region it ends on; z's conditions do not hold throughout; children present, school in session, inside the margin."},{"name":"occasion_d12_outside","expected":"compliant","narrative":"A beacon governed the region x occupied before the act; no beacon governs any region x occupies or z governs during the U-turn; z's conditions do not hold throughout; children present."},{"name":"occasion_d13","expected":"violated","narrative":"No beacon; env.civil_time leaves z's posted window during the U-turn, so z's conditions do not hold for the first part of the act and hold for the rest; children present, school in session, inside the margin."},{"name":"occasion_d13_outside","expected":"compliant","narrative":"No beacon; z's conditions held before the act and do not hold at any observation of the U-turn; children present."},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"compliant","narrative":"x makes a U-turn on z's lane with children present while asm.school_not_in_session_day is declared true at every observation of the act."}],"occasion":{"act":"drv.motion.u_turn","boundary":"window","window":"p.u_turn_window","under_way":{"words":"make a U-turn","atoms":["kin.yaw_rate"],"derived":["drv.motion.yawing"],"justification":"An observation inside the act is one within the U-turn window behind the recognition at which x's heading is changing (drv.motion.yawing: \"the absolute value of its yaw rate exceeds yaw_floor\", kin.yaw_rate): the turning is motion, and x occupied the zone's lanes before the turning began, so no region alone tells the act apart."},"spans":{"d3":"some_moment","d5":"throughout","d8":"throughout","d10":"throughout","d12":"throughout","d13":"throughout"}},"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.u_turn_window","unit":"s","value":20,"convention":"U-turn recognition window: the longest time over which a reversal of heading, made in one movement or in several forward and backing movements, is recognized as one turning; a multi-point turn on a narrow street.","source":"observed durations of three-point turns (naturalistic driving studies)"},{"name":"p.u_turn_reversal_tolerance","unit":"deg","value":30,"convention":"Reversal tolerance: the largest difference between the size of the heading change over the window and a half turn within which the road user counts as proceeding in the opposite direction; covers the offset of a turn into a lane of the opposite direction and heading noise.","source":"trajectory-classification practice for U-turn detection"},{"name":"p.yaw_rate_resolution","unit":"deg/s","value":2.0,"convention":"Sensor resolution: the smallest yaw rate the acquisition standard separates from a straight path; a yaw rate at or below it counts as no heading change.","source":"yaw-rate resolution of the carla_scene_graph acquisition standard"},{"name":"p.child_presence_reach","unit":"m","value":5.0,"convention":"Presence reach: the ground distance from a child's body to a travel region of a school zone within which the child counts as present in the zone; the width of a sidewalk and verge beside the roadway.","source":"urban street cross-section conventions (sidewalk and buffer widths)"}],"gaps":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_400_1_o1","law_refs":["NRS-484B-400-1"],"subject":{"binder":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"e1","text":"If the driver of a vehicle","role":"subject"},{"id":"e2","text":"intends to turn","role":"trigger"},{"id":"e3","text":"at an intersection","role":"trigger"},{"id":"e4","text":"and:","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"e5","text":"The turn is a right turn,","role":"trigger"},{"id":"e6","text":"both the approach for the right turn and the right turn must be made from the right turn lane","role":"obligation"},{"id":"e7","text":"if the highway has a right turn lane","role":"condition"},{"id":"e8","text":"as set forth in subsection 4 of NRS 484B.223 [NRS-484B-223-4a, NRS-484B-223-4b],","role":"reference"},{"id":"e9","text":"or must be made from the extreme right lane.","role":"sibling"}],"elements":[{"span":"e1","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle (\"every device in, upon or by which any person or property is or may be transported or drawn upon a highway\"), claimed by id. 'the driver of' is a role read through the vehicle's controlled motion (observable_reading agency)."},{"span":"e3","atoms":["st.intersection","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region","rel.occupies"],"derived":["drv.motion.entering_region"],"justification":"The intersection the intention is declared at and the turn is made in: st.intersection (\"the region where two roadways meet\"), entered by x (drv.motion.entering_region: \"its footprint overlaps r (rel.occupies) at the observation and did not at the observation before\") from the approach carrier it occupies whose entrance end is i (st.lane_enters: \"the intersection region a directed approach carrier runs into at its entrance end\")."},{"span":"e5","atoms":["kin.yaw_rate","rel.occupies"],"derived":["drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry"],"justification":"The turn made is a right turn where the heading change of x since it entered i (drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry: \"The signed heading change of road user x since its footprint last began to overlap region r, in degrees, left positive\", from kin.yaw_rate) reaches the turn recognition angle to the right. The concept is 'not' a turn by itself; the rule compares it with its bound."},{"span":"e6","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.turn_lane","st.lane_enters","st.intersection","kin.path_length"],"derived":[],"justification":"The approach for the turn and the turn are made from the right turn lane R where x's footprint overlaps R (rel.occupies) at its entry into i and at every observation of the approach length of path travelled before it at which x occupies a carrier entering i (a .path window, which reads kin.path_length, \"distance travelled along the body's path\"). R is the st.turn_lane (\"a lane designated only for turning; side ∈ {left, right}\") of side right that enters i (st.lane_enters)."},{"span":"e7","atoms":["st.highway","st.on_way","st.turn_lane","st.lane_enters","st.lane_direction"],"derived":["drv.road.opposed_directions"],"source_spans":["e8"],"justification":"The highway has a right turn lane as subsection 4 of NRS 484B.223 sets forth, whose words are borrowed: NRS-484B-223-4a and NRS-484B-223-4b both quote \"a single right lane to be used only for turning\". That is a st.turn_lane (\"a lane designated only for turning\") of side right, entering i (st.lane_enters), lying on the same highway (st.on_way: \"the public way (a highway region) a structure region lies on\"; st.highway) as the carrier x approached through, and serving x's direction: its designated direction (st.lane_direction) not opposed to that carrier's (drv.road.opposed_directions false), so that a turn lane on the opposing approach of the same way is not read."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[{"span":"e2","id":"int.turn","meaning":"The source's current plan for the road user includes a turn, to either hand, at the target region."}],"compositions":[{"span":"e8","as":"definition","source":"NRS-484B-223-4a","quote":"a single right lane to be used only for turning","why":"It borrows only the description of the lane, a single right lane to be used only for turning, to say which lane counts as a right turn lane here; whether a vehicle in that lane complies with paragraph (4)(a), driving in it only to turn right, decides nothing in this duty, so that rule need not apply, hold or be complied with."},{"span":"e8","as":"definition","source":"NRS-484B-223-4b","quote":"a single right lane to be used only for turning","why":"It borrows only the same description of the lane; whether a vehicle in that lane complies with paragraph (4)(b), not travelling through the intersection, decides nothing in this duty, so that rule need not apply, hold or be complied with."}],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"x carries ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; at the observation x's right turn in intersection i is recognized: the heading change since x's latest entry into i (drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry(x, i) with step p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph) is at most minus p.turn_recognition_angle there and was not at the observation before; the source declared int.turn for x at i at the observation of that entry (Formula.intent, read through a past operator); and the highway has a right turn lane for x's approach: x entered i from a carrier c with st.lane_enters(c, i) lying on a highway h (st.on_way(c, h)), and some st.turn_lane R of side right enters i (st.lane_enters(R, i)), lies on h (st.on_way(R, h)) and has a designated direction not opposed to c's (drv.road.opposed_directions(R, c) with p.opposed_carriers_cosine false).","obligation":"At the observation of that entry into i (read through a past operator), x's footprint overlaps such a lane R, and at every observation of the path window of length p.turn_approach_length behind the entry (measured in x's path, kin.path_length) at which x occupies a carrier entering i, it occupies that R: both the approach and the turn are made from the right turn lane.","params":["p.turn_recognition_angle","p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph","p.opposed_carriers_cosine","p.turn_approach_length"],"narrowings":[{"span":"e1","why":"'the driver of a vehicle' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"e6","why":"'the approach for the right turn' is read as the stretch of path, of the approach length, just before the entry into the intersection, during which every carrier of the intersection x is on must be the right turn lane; a lane change into the turn lane earlier than that stretch complies.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"x (ru.motor_vehicle) approaches i on a through lane c of highway h whose approach also has a right st.turn_lane R entering i; int.turn is declared for x at i; x enters i from c and turns right beyond p.turn_recognition_angle."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same highway; x, with int.turn declared at i, is on R for the whole approach length before its entry, enters i from R and turns right."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"x, with int.turn declared at i, turns left in i (heading change positive beyond p.turn_recognition_angle)."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x turns right in i from a through lane with int.turn declared, but the source does not record which intersection the turn lane beside it enters, so whether the highway has a right turn lane for this approach is unknown.","masked":["st.lane_enters"]}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.turn_recognition_angle","unit":"deg","value":45,"convention":"Turn recognition: the heading change through an intersection beyond which a passage counts as a turn rather than a straight crossing; half the right angle of a turn at a right-angled junction, leaving room for skewed junctions and lane offsets.","source":"intersection geometry design conventions (AASHTO Green Book)"},{"name":"p.opposed_carriers_cosine","unit":"ratio","value":0.7,"convention":"Direction tolerance: minus the cosine of the narrowest angle between two carriers' designated directions that counts as opposite directions; carriers within about 45 degrees of exactly opposed count.","source":"road-network direction conventions of map data"},{"name":"p.turn_approach_length","unit":"m","value":15.0,"convention":"Turn approach: the distance travelled just before entering an intersection over which a turning vehicle's approach is judged; about two passenger-car lengths, shorter than the storage of a short turn bay.","source":"AASHTO Green Book turn-lane storage practice"}],"gaps":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_400_1_o2","law_refs":["NRS-484B-400-1"],"subject":{"binder":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"e1","text":"If the driver of a vehicle","role":"subject"},{"id":"e2","text":"intends to turn","role":"trigger"},{"id":"e3","text":"at an intersection","role":"trigger"},{"id":"e4","text":"and:","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"e5","text":"The turn is a right turn,","role":"trigger"},{"id":"e6","text":"both the approach for the right turn and the right turn must be made from the right turn lane","role":"sibling"},{"id":"e7","text":"if the highway has a right turn lane","role":"condition"},{"id":"e8","text":"as set forth in subsection 4 of NRS 484B.223 [NRS-484B-223-4a, NRS-484B-223-4b],","role":"reference"},{"id":"e9","text":"or must be made from the extreme right lane.","role":"obligation"}],"elements":[{"span":"e1","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle (\"every device in, upon or by which any person or property is or may be transported or drawn upon a highway\"), claimed by id. 'the driver of' is a role read through the vehicle's controlled motion."},{"span":"e3","atoms":["st.intersection","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region","rel.occupies"],"derived":["drv.motion.entering_region"],"justification":"st.intersection (\"the region where two roadways meet\"), entered by x (drv.motion.entering_region) from the approach carrier whose entrance end is i (st.lane_enters)."},{"span":"e5","atoms":["kin.yaw_rate","rel.occupies"],"derived":["drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry"],"justification":"A right turn: the heading change since x entered i (drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry, \"in degrees, left positive\", from kin.yaw_rate) reaches the turn recognition angle to the right."},{"span":"e7","atoms":["st.highway","st.on_way","st.turn_lane","st.lane_enters","st.lane_direction"],"derived":["drv.road.opposed_directions"],"source_spans":["e8"],"justification":"Read negated here: the 'or' alternative applies where the highway has no right turn lane as subsection 4 of NRS 484B.223 sets forth, borrowing \"a single right lane to be used only for turning\" (NRS-484B-223-4a, NRS-484B-223-4b): no st.turn_lane of side right enters i (st.lane_enters) on the same highway (st.on_way, st.highway) with a designated direction (st.lane_direction) not opposed to x's approach (drv.road.opposed_directions)."},{"span":"e9","atoms":["st.lane","st.lane_adjacency","st.lane_enters","rel.occupies","kin.path_length"],"derived":[],"justification":"The extreme right lane: a st.lane entering i whose ordinal within the carriageway equals the count of lanes in its direction (st.lane_adjacency: \"lane ordinal within the carriageway and the count of lanes in that direction; ordinal 1 is the leftmost lane, looking along the lane's direction\"). The approach and the turn are made from it where x's footprint overlaps it (rel.occupies) at the entry and over the approach length of path before it (.path window, kin.path_length). Lane adjacency is 'not a stand-in' for a marking and is not used as one."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[{"span":"e2","id":"int.turn","meaning":"The source's current plan for the road user includes a turn, to either hand, at the target region."}],"compositions":[{"span":"e8","as":"definition","source":"NRS-484B-223-4a","quote":"a single right lane to be used only for turning","why":"It borrows only the description of the lane, a single right lane to be used only for turning, to say which lane counts as a right turn lane, here to establish that there is none; whether a vehicle complies with paragraph (4)(a) decides nothing in this duty, so that rule need not apply, hold or be complied with."},{"span":"e8","as":"definition","source":"NRS-484B-223-4b","quote":"a single right lane to be used only for turning","why":"It borrows only the same description of the lane; whether a vehicle complies with paragraph (4)(b) decides nothing in this duty, so that rule need not apply, hold or be complied with."}],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"x carries ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; at the observation x's right turn in intersection i is recognized (drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry(x, i) with step p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph at most minus p.turn_recognition_angle there and not at the observation before); int.turn was declared for x at i at the observation of its latest entry into i (read through a past operator); x entered i from a carrier c with st.lane_enters(c, i) on highway h (st.on_way(c, h)); and no st.turn_lane of side right enters i on h with a designated direction not opposed to c's (drv.road.opposed_directions with p.opposed_carriers_cosine).","obligation":"At the observation of that entry into i (read through a past operator), x's footprint overlaps a st.lane L that enters i (st.lane_enters(L, i)), lies on h, has a designated direction not opposed to c's, and whose st.lane_adjacency ordinal equals its lane count (the rightmost lane looking along its direction); and at every observation of the path window of length p.turn_approach_length behind the entry (kin.path_length) at which x occupies a carrier entering i, it occupies that L.","params":["p.turn_recognition_angle","p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph","p.opposed_carriers_cosine","p.turn_approach_length"],"narrowings":[{"span":"e1","why":"'the driver of a vehicle' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"e9","why":"'the extreme right lane' is read as the lane whose ordinal equals the count of lanes in its direction on the approach; the approach is the stretch of path of the approach length before the entry. An approach with no lanes mapped has no such lane, and the duty is not decided there.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"x (ru.motor_vehicle) approaches i on a two-lane approach with no right turn lane, in the leftmost lane; int.turn is declared at i; x turns right from that lane."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same approach; x is in the lane whose ordinal equals the lane count for the whole approach length, enters i from it and turns right."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The approach has a right st.turn_lane entering i on the same highway in x's direction; x turns right (NRS_484B_400_1_o1 governs that case)."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x turns right from a two-lane approach with no right turn lane, with int.turn declared, but the source does not observe lane ordinals and counts.","masked":["st.lane_adjacency"]}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.turn_recognition_angle","unit":"deg","value":45,"convention":"Turn recognition: the heading change through an intersection beyond which a passage counts as a turn rather than a straight crossing; half the right angle of a turn at a right-angled junction, leaving room for skewed junctions and lane offsets.","source":"intersection geometry design conventions (AASHTO Green Book)"},{"name":"p.opposed_carriers_cosine","unit":"ratio","value":0.7,"convention":"Direction tolerance: minus the cosine of the narrowest angle between two carriers' designated directions that counts as opposite directions; carriers within about 45 degrees of exactly opposed count.","source":"road-network direction conventions of map data"},{"name":"p.turn_approach_length","unit":"m","value":15.0,"convention":"Turn approach: the distance travelled just before entering an intersection over which a turning vehicle's approach is judged; about two passenger-car lengths, shorter than the storage of a short turn bay.","source":"AASHTO Green Book turn-lane storage practice"}],"gaps":[]}
{"concept_id":"drv.motion.veering_left","kind":"formula","contract":"Road user x departs to the left of a travel carrier's designated direction at the observation: it moves forward along the carrier while its velocity points to the left of the carrier's direction by more than a tolerance. It holds where x is moving (drv.motion.moving with speed_floor), the component of its velocity (kin.velocity, m/s, world frame) along the carrier's designated direction (st.lane_direction, read normalised) is positive, and the cross product of that direction with the velocity, left positive, exceeds sine_tolerance times x's speed (kin.speed): the sine of the angle from the designated direction to the velocity is above sine_tolerance. Unknown where the carrier carries no designated direction. Not denoted: x's heading (a body may point across a carrier while moving along it), motion against the carrier's direction, x being on the carrier (the caller states occupancy), a signal, or how far x has moved sideways.","definition":null,"args":[{"name":"x","sort":"track"},{"name":"c","sort":"region"}],"params":[{"name":"speed_floor","unit":"m/s","meaning":"the source's speed resolution, below which a reading counts as no motion"},{"name":"sine_tolerance","unit":"ratio","meaning":"the sine of the angle between the velocity and the designated direction above which the motion counts as departing to one side rather than tracking the carrier"}],"elements":[{"span":"x is moving (drv.motion.moving with speed_floor)","atoms":[],"concepts":["drv.motion.moving"],"justification":"drv.motion.moving: \"A road user is in motion at the observation: its speed exceeds speed_floor\"."},{"span":"its velocity (kin.velocity, m/s, world frame)","atoms":["kin.velocity"],"concepts":[],"justification":"kin.velocity: \"velocity vector\", m/s, world frame; the direction of motion, not the heading."},{"span":"the carrier's designated direction (st.lane_direction, read normalised)","atoms":["st.lane_direction"],"concepts":[],"justification":"st.lane_direction: \"direction of travel designated for a structure a vehicle travels in\", read normalised; unknown where the carrier carries none."},{"span":"x's speed (kin.speed)","atoms":["kin.speed"],"concepts":[],"justification":"kin.speed: \"magnitude of velocity\"; the cross product is compared with the tolerance times the speed, so no division by a measurement."}],"residues":[],"scenarios":[{"name":"holds","expected":"compliant","narrative":"x moves along lane c with its velocity turned to the left of c's designated direction by more than the angle whose sine is sine_tolerance, as at the start of a lane change to the left."},{"name":"fails","expected":"violated","narrative":"x moves along lane c with its velocity parallel to c's designated direction."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x moves to the left across lane c, but c's designated direction is not observed.","masked":["st.lane_direction"]}],"used_by":["NRS_484B_413_2"],"supersedes":null}
{"concept_id":"drv.motion.veering_right","kind":"formula","contract":"Road user x departs to the right of a travel carrier's designated direction at the observation: it moves forward along the carrier while its velocity points to the right of the carrier's direction by more than a tolerance. It holds where x is moving (drv.motion.moving with speed_floor), the component of its velocity (kin.velocity, m/s, world frame) along the carrier's designated direction (st.lane_direction, read normalised) is positive, and the cross product of that direction with the velocity, left positive, is below minus sine_tolerance times x's speed (kin.speed): the sine of the angle from the designated direction to the velocity is below minus sine_tolerance. Unknown where the carrier carries no designated direction. Not denoted: x's heading (a body may point across a carrier while moving along it), motion against the carrier's direction, x being on the carrier (the caller states occupancy), a signal, or how far x has moved sideways.","definition":null,"args":[{"name":"x","sort":"track"},{"name":"c","sort":"region"}],"params":[{"name":"speed_floor","unit":"m/s","meaning":"the source's speed resolution, below which a reading counts as no motion"},{"name":"sine_tolerance","unit":"ratio","meaning":"the sine of the angle between the velocity and the designated direction above which the motion counts as departing to one side rather than tracking the carrier"}],"elements":[{"span":"x is moving (drv.motion.moving with speed_floor)","atoms":[],"concepts":["drv.motion.moving"],"justification":"drv.motion.moving: \"A road user is in motion at the observation: its speed exceeds speed_floor\"."},{"span":"its velocity (kin.velocity, m/s, world frame)","atoms":["kin.velocity"],"concepts":[],"justification":"kin.velocity: \"velocity vector\", m/s, world frame; the direction of motion, not the heading."},{"span":"the carrier's designated direction (st.lane_direction, read normalised)","atoms":["st.lane_direction"],"concepts":[],"justification":"st.lane_direction: \"direction of travel designated for a structure a vehicle travels in\", read normalised; unknown where the carrier carries none."},{"span":"x's speed (kin.speed)","atoms":["kin.speed"],"concepts":[],"justification":"kin.speed: \"magnitude of velocity\"; the cross product is compared with the tolerance times the speed, so no division by a measurement."}],"residues":[],"scenarios":[{"name":"holds","expected":"compliant","narrative":"x moves along lane c with its velocity turned to the right of c's designated direction by more than the angle whose sine is sine_tolerance, as at the start of a turn into a side street on the right."},{"name":"fails","expected":"violated","narrative":"x moves along lane c with its velocity parallel to c's designated direction."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x moves to the right across lane c, but c's designated direction is not observed.","masked":["st.lane_direction"]}],"used_by":["NRS_484B_413_2"],"supersedes":null}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_413_2","law_refs":["NRS-484B-413-2"],"subject":{"binder":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"f1","text":"A signal of intention to turn right or left, or otherwise turn a vehicle from a direct course, shall be given continuously during not less than the last 100 feet traveled","role":"obligation"},{"id":"f5","text":"in a business or residential district","role":"condition"},{"id":"f6","text":"and not less than the last 300 feet traveled","role":"condition"},{"id":"f7","text":"in any other area","role":"condition"},{"id":"f8","text":"prior to changing the course","role":"trigger"},{"id":"f9","text":"of a vehicle.","role":"subject"},{"id":"f10","text":"This rule shall be observed, regardless of the weather.","role":"condition"}],"elements":[{"span":"f1","atoms":["sig.turn_indicator","sig.hand_signal","kin.path_length","st.lane_direction","kin.velocity","kin.speed","rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":["drv.motion.veering_left","drv.motion.veering_right"],"justification":"A signal of intention to turn is the signal itself, not a declared intention (the ontology: \"a signal 'of intention' is the signal\"): sig.turn_indicator (\"the turn indicator state ∈ {off, left, right}\") or sig.hand_signal (\"a driver's or rider's arm signal; meaning ∈ {no_signal, left, right, stop_or_slow, re_enter}\") showing the side of the change of course; sig.turn_indicator is 'not a stand-in' for the turn itself, which is read separately. A direct course is travel along the designated direction of the carrier x occupies (rel.occupies a st.travel_region carrying st.lane_direction); turning right or left or otherwise from it is x's velocity departing to one side of that direction, the proposed concepts drv.motion.veering_left and drv.motion.veering_right (\"it moves forward along the carrier while its velocity points to the left [right] of the carrier's direction by more than a tolerance\", from kin.velocity and kin.speed); following a bend of the carrier is not a departure, since the designated direction bends with it. 'given continuously during not less than the last 100 feet traveled' is a window measured in distance travelled (a .path window, which reads kin.path_length: \"distance travelled along the body's path since the start of the trace, monotone\") at every observation of which the signal of the departure's side is shown; the figure is the law's literal."},{"span":"f6","atoms":["kin.path_length"],"derived":[],"justification":"The same .path window (kin.path_length) with the law's other literal, the bound selected where the place is not in a business or residence district (span f7)."},{"span":"f8","atoms":["rel.occupies"],"derived":["drv.motion.veering_left","drv.motion.veering_right"],"justification":"Changing the course is the observation at which a departure to one side begins: drv.motion.veering_left or drv.motion.veering_right holds for a carrier x occupies (rel.occupies) and held for none at the observation before. The signal window ends there."},{"span":"f9","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle (\"every device in, upon or by which any person or property is or may be transported or drawn upon a highway\"), claimed by id: the subject x whose course changes."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[{"span":"f5","id":"asm.within_business_or_residence_district","meaning":"The place of the observation lies inside a business district or a residence district declared for the map or the trace."},{"span":"f7","id":"asm.within_business_or_residence_district","meaning":"The place of the observation lies inside a business district or a residence district declared for the map or the trace."}],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[{"span":"f10","why":"The duty is the same in every weather: the words exclude no weather and add no condition, so no environment atom is read.","scope":"none"}],"binders":[{"name":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"x carries ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle and at the observation begins a change of course: for some travel region c that x occupies (rel.occupies), drv.motion.veering_left(x, c) or drv.motion.veering_right(x, c) (with p.speed_resolution and p.course_departure_sine) holds there, and at the observation before neither held for any region x occupied.","obligation":"For a departure to the left, x showed a left signal (sig.turn_indicator left, or sig.hand_signal left) at every observation of the window behind the observation measured in x's distance travelled (.path, kin.path_length), whose length is the literal of span f1 where asm.within_business_or_residence_district holds at the observation and the literal of span f6 where it does not (a bound selected by the condition); for a departure to the right, the right signal likewise. A departure to both sides at once owes the signal of either.","params":["p.speed_resolution","p.course_departure_sine"],"narrowings":[{"span":"f1","why":"'otherwise turn a vehicle from a direct course' is read as the velocity departing to one side of the designated direction of the carrier the vehicle occupies, on lanes, roadways and other carriers that carry a direction; a turn begun where the vehicle occupies only an intersection, which carries no direction, is not recognized.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"x (ru.motor_vehicle) on a rural road (asm.within_business_or_residence_district declared false) begins a lane change to the left; its sig.turn_indicator showed left only over a path shorter than the literal of span f6 before the departure began, off before that."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same rural lane change; sig.turn_indicator showed left at every observation of a path longer than the literal of span f6 before the departure."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"x drives along its lane following its designated direction, never departing to either side."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x begins a lane change to the left, but the source observes neither its turn indicator nor any arm signal.","masked":["sig.turn_indicator","sig.hand_signal"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"compliant","narrative":"In a declared business district x begins a departure to the right with sig.turn_indicator right shown over a path longer than the literal of span f1 but shorter than that of span f6."},{"name":"branch_2","expected":"violated","narrative":"x begins a departure to the right with sig.turn_indicator left shown over the whole window: the signal is not of the side of the change."}],"literals":[{"span":"f1","text":"100 feet","value":100,"unit":"ft"},{"span":"f6","text":"300 feet","value":300,"unit":"ft"}],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.speed_resolution","unit":"m/s","value":0.2,"convention":"Sensor resolution: the smallest speed the acquisition standard separates from standstill; a speed at or below it counts as no motion.","source":"speed resolution of the carla_scene_graph acquisition standard"},{"name":"p.course_departure_sine","unit":"ratio","value":0.05,"convention":"Course-departure tolerance: the sine of the angle between a road user's velocity and its carrier's designated direction beyond which it counts as leaving its direct course rather than tracking the carrier; about three degrees, above heading noise and lane-keeping drift.","source":"lane-change onset detection practice in naturalistic driving studies"}],"gaps":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_440_1_o1","law_refs":["NRS-484B-440-1"],"subject":{"binder":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"g1","text":"Upon any highway","role":"trigger"},{"id":"g2","text":"outside of a business or residence district","role":"condition"},{"id":"g3","text":"no person shall stop, park or leave standing","role":"obligation"},{"id":"g4","text":"any vehicle, whether attended or unattended,","role":"subject"},{"id":"g5","text":"upon the paved or main-traveled part of the highway","role":"condition"},{"id":"g6","text":"when it is practicable to stop, park or so leave such vehicle off such part of the highway,","role":"standard"},{"id":"g7","text":"but in every event","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"g8","text":"an unobstructed width of the highway","role":"sibling"},{"id":"g9","text":"opposite a standing vehicle","role":"sibling"},{"id":"g10","text":"shall be left for the free passage of other vehicles","role":"sibling"},{"id":"g11","text":"and","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"g12","text":"a clear view of such stopped vehicles shall be available from a distance of 200 feet in each direction upon such highway.","role":"sibling"},{"id":"g13","text":"This section shall not apply to the driver of any vehicle which is disabled while on the paved or main-traveled portion of a highway in such manner and to such extent that it is impossible to avoid stopping and temporarily leaving such disabled vehicle in such position.","role":"exception"}],"elements":[{"span":"g1","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.highway"],"derived":[],"justification":"st.highway: \"the entire public way between its boundary lines, including sidewalks and shoulders\" (DEF-NRS-484A-095, \"the entire width between the boundary lines of every way\"); x is upon it where its footprint overlaps it (rel.occupies)."},{"span":"g3","atoms":["kin.speed","rel.ahead_behind_in_lane","rel.surface_gap","dev.human_direction","dev.traffic_signal","dev.stop_sign","dev.governs","rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":["drv.motion.halted"],"justification":"'stop', prohibited here, takes DEF-NRS-484A-260 (\"any halting, even momentarily, of a vehicle, whether occupied or not, except when necessary to avoid conflict with other traffic or in compliance with the directions of a police officer or official traffic-control device\"); 'park' (DEF-NRS-484A-155, \"the standing of a vehicle\") and 'leave standing' (DEF-NRS-484A-250, \"the halting of a vehicle\") are halts too. The halt is drv.motion.halted (\"speed ... at or below speed_floor ... with no minimum duration\", kin.speed), which observes any halting, even momentary. The definition's exclusions are carried beside it: a halt behind another road user ahead in the same lane (rel.ahead_behind_in_lane) within the conflict standoff gap (rel.surface_gap) avoids a conflict; a halt while a police officer's stop direction (dev.human_direction, indication stop) or a signal showing a red indication or a stop sign (dev.traffic_signal, dev.stop_sign) governs (dev.governs) the travel region x occupies is in compliance with directions. Purposes of parking and standing (loading, passengers) are not observable and are read through the halt (observable_reading purpose)."},{"span":"g4","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, claimed by id; 'whether attended or unattended' excludes no member."},{"span":"g5","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.roadway"],"derived":[],"justification":"The paved or main-traveled part of the highway is the st.roadway (\"the part of a highway improved for vehicular traffic, excluding shoulder\"; DEF-NRS-484A-220, \"that portion of a highway which is improved and ordinarily used for vehicular traffic, exclusive of the shoulder\"); x halts upon it where its footprint overlaps it (rel.occupies). A paved shoulder is off it: the words set the main-traveled part against the part off it where the vehicle may be left. st.roadway is 'not a stand-in' for the sidewalk."},{"span":"g13","atoms":["kin.engine_running","sig.hazard","rel.occupies","st.roadway"],"derived":[],"justification":"A vehicle disabled on the roadway so that stopping cannot be avoided is read through its nearest observables, the same as the earlier mapping of 'a disabled vehicle' in this iteration: its engine or motor not running, so that propulsion is unavailable (kin.engine_running: \"the vehicle's engine or motor is running, so that propulsion is available\", false), with its hazard lamps flashing (sig.hazard: \"both indicators flashing together\"), while it occupies the roadway (rel.occupies, st.roadway). kin.engine_running is 'not a stand-in' for motion or a halt, and is not used as either; the gap records that the disability itself has no atom."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"g6","standard":"practicable to stop, park or so leave such vehicle off such part of the highway","concepts":["st.shoulder","st.region_geometry"],"params":["p.offroad_stop_reach"],"convention":"Off-road stopping convention: moving off the main-traveled part is practicable where a shoulder lies within the reach of a short lateral move from the halted vehicle's body; the ground distance from the body to the nearest shoulder is the measured magnitude compared with the reach.","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[{"span":"g2","id":"asm.within_business_or_residence_district","meaning":"The place of the observation lies inside a business district or a residence district declared for the map or the trace."}],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"x carries ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; at the observation x's footprint overlaps a st.highway (rel.occupies) and asm.within_business_or_residence_district does not hold; and x is not disabled there: not (kin.engine_running false and sig.hazard on while x occupies a st.roadway).","obligation":"It is not the case that, at the observation, x is halted (drv.motion.halted with p.speed_resolution) with its footprint overlapping a st.roadway, while some st.shoulder lies within p.offroad_stop_reach of x's body (st.region_geometry distance), unless the halt falls under the exclusions of the defined 'stop': some other road user is ahead of x in the same lane (rel.ahead_behind_in_lane) with a surface gap (rel.surface_gap) at most p.stopping_conflict_gap, or a dev.human_direction with indication stop, a dev.traffic_signal displaying circular_red, a red_arrow or flashing_red, or a dev.stop_sign governs (dev.governs) a travel region x occupies.","params":["p.speed_resolution","p.offroad_stop_reach","p.stopping_conflict_gap"],"narrowings":[{"span":"g3","why":"'stop, park or leave standing' are read through the halt itself; the purposes that set parking and standing apart (loading, receiving passengers) are not observable, and every halt is a stop under the definition that applies, so none is lost.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"purpose"},{"span":"g6","why":"'practicable' is read through the distance to a shoulder only; the shoulder's width, surface and load-bearing are not read.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"x (ru.motor_vehicle) on a rural highway (asm.within_business_or_residence_district declared false) halts with its footprint on the st.roadway, engine running, no hazard lamps, nothing ahead and no device governing; a st.shoulder lies within p.offroad_stop_reach of its body."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"x halts on the roadway of a rural bridge with no shoulder within p.offroad_stop_reach; no other road user is in the scene."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"x halts on the roadway in a declared residence district (asm.within_business_or_residence_district true)."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x halts on the rural roadway beside a mapped shoulder, but the source maps regions without their outline, so the distance to the shoulder is unknown.","masked":["st.region_geometry"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"x halts on the rural roadway with its engine not running and its hazard lamps flashing: the disabled-vehicle exception applies."},{"name":"branch_2","expected":"compliant","narrative":"x halts on the rural roadway behind a halted truck ahead in its lane at a surface gap below p.stopping_conflict_gap, a shoulder within reach: the halt avoids a conflict and is no prohibited stop."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.speed_resolution","unit":"m/s","value":0.2,"convention":"Sensor resolution: the smallest speed the acquisition standard separates from standstill; a speed at or below it counts as no motion.","source":"speed resolution of the carla_scene_graph acquisition standard"},{"name":"p.offroad_stop_reach","unit":"m","value":5.0,"convention":"Off-road stopping reach: the ground distance from a halted vehicle's body to a shoulder within which moving off the main-traveled part counts as practicable; about one lane width of lateral movement.","source":"AASHTO Green Book lane and shoulder widths"},{"name":"p.stopping_conflict_gap","unit":"m","value":5.0,"convention":"Conflict standoff: the largest surface gap from a halted road user's body to another road user ahead of it at which the halt counts as necessary to avoid a conflict; a queue spacing at standstill.","source":"queue spacing at standstill (traffic-flow jam-density conventions)"}],"gaps":[{"span":"g13","kind":"atom","proposal":"`ru.disabled` | a vehicle that cannot proceed under its own power, by a mechanical failure, crash damage or a flat tyre, as the source records it **Not a stand-in for:** a vehicle parked with its engine off, or one showing hazard lamps | general — decides whether moving the vehicle off the roadway can be carried out, which the disabled-vehicle exception turns on","nearest":["kin.engine_running","sig.hazard"]}]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_440_1_o2","law_refs":["NRS-484B-440-1"],"subject":{"binder":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"g1","text":"Upon any highway","role":"trigger"},{"id":"g2","text":"outside of a business or residence district","role":"condition"},{"id":"g3","text":"no person shall stop, park or leave standing","role":"sibling"},{"id":"g4","text":"any vehicle, whether attended or unattended,","role":"subject"},{"id":"g5","text":"upon the paved or main-traveled part of the highway","role":"trigger"},{"id":"g6","text":"when it is practicable to stop, park or so leave such vehicle off such part of the highway,","role":"sibling"},{"id":"g7","text":"but in every event","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"g8","text":"an unobstructed width of the highway","role":"obligation"},{"id":"g9","text":"opposite a standing vehicle","role":"trigger"},{"id":"g10","text":"shall be left for the free passage of other vehicles","role":"standard"},{"id":"g11","text":"and","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"g12","text":"a clear view of such stopped vehicles shall be available from a distance of 200 feet in each direction upon such highway.","role":"sibling"},{"id":"g13","text":"This section shall not apply to the driver of any vehicle which is disabled while on the paved or main-traveled portion of a highway in such manner and to such extent that it is impossible to avoid stopping and temporarily leaving such disabled vehicle in such position.","role":"exception"}],"elements":[{"span":"g1","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.highway"],"derived":[],"justification":"st.highway: \"the entire public way between its boundary lines, including sidewalks and shoulders\"; x is upon it where its footprint overlaps it (rel.occupies)."},{"span":"g4","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, claimed by id; 'whether attended or unattended' excludes no member."},{"span":"g5","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.roadway"],"derived":[],"justification":"The standing vehicles 'in every event' are those of the first clause, upon the paved or main-traveled part: the st.roadway (\"the part of a highway improved for vehicular traffic, excluding shoulder\"), overlapped by x's footprint (rel.occupies)."},{"span":"g8","atoms":["st.lane","st.on_way","st.highway","rel.occupies","st.region_geometry"],"derived":[],"justification":"A width of the highway opposite the vehicle is a lane beside it: a st.lane (\"a longitudinal strip of roadway for one line of vehicles\") on the same highway (st.on_way, st.highway) whose ground distance from x's body (st.region_geometry) is at most the beside reach, so that a lane segment far along the way is not read, and that x's footprint does not overlap (rel.occupies). Unobstructed: no other halted road user beside x occupies it."},{"span":"g9","atoms":["kin.speed","rel.longitudinal_overlap"],"derived":["drv.motion.halted"],"justification":"'a standing vehicle' (DEF-NRS-484A-250, \"the halting of a vehicle, whether occupied or not\") is x halted (drv.motion.halted, kin.speed at or below the resolution); its purpose is not observable (observable_reading purpose). Opposite it is the stretch alongside its body: another halted road user is opposite where their footprints overlap along x's heading (rel.longitudinal_overlap positive), a projection, 'not' a contact or a distance."},{"span":"g13","atoms":["kin.engine_running","sig.hazard","rel.occupies","st.roadway"],"derived":[],"justification":"A vehicle disabled on the roadway is read through its nearest observables, as in the first obligation of this line: engine or motor not running (kin.engine_running: \"so that propulsion is available\", false) with hazard lamps flashing (sig.hazard: \"both indicators flashing together\"), while it occupies the roadway (rel.occupies, st.roadway). kin.engine_running is 'not a stand-in' for motion or a halt; the gap records that the disability itself has no atom."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"g10","standard":"an unobstructed width left for the free passage of other vehicles","concepts":["st.lane_width","rel.longitudinal_overlap","drv.motion.halted"],"params":["p.free_passage_width","p.opposite_lane_reach","p.speed_resolution"],"convention":"Free-passage convention: the width left for passage is a lane beside the standing vehicle, not overlapped by it and not taken by another halted road user alongside it, whose measured width (st.lane_width) is at least a design passenger-car width plus lateral clearance.","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[{"span":"g2","id":"asm.within_business_or_residence_district","meaning":"The place of the observation lies inside a business district or a residence district declared for the map or the trace."}],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"x carries ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; at the observation x is halted (drv.motion.halted with p.speed_resolution) with its footprint overlapping a st.roadway of a st.highway h (rel.occupies, st.on_way); asm.within_business_or_residence_district does not hold; and x is not disabled there: not (kin.engine_running false and sig.hazard on).","obligation":"Some st.lane L on h (st.on_way(L, h)) that x's footprint does not overlap, within p.opposite_lane_reach of x's body (st.region_geometry distance), has st.lane_width at least p.free_passage_width, and no road user other than x that is halted (drv.motion.halted with p.speed_resolution) and overlaps x along x's heading (rel.longitudinal_overlap positive) occupies L.","params":["p.speed_resolution","p.free_passage_width","p.opposite_lane_reach"],"narrowings":[{"span":"g8","why":"'an unobstructed width of the highway' is read as a whole lane beside the vehicle, free of halted road users alongside it; a part-lane, a shoulder, or an obstruction that is not a road user (st.obstruction) is not counted.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"On a rural two-lane highway x (ru.motor_vehicle) halts in one lane while another vehicle halts in the other lane alongside it (rel.longitudinal_overlap positive): no lane beside x is free."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"x halts in one lane of a rural two-lane highway; the other lane, within p.opposite_lane_reach, has st.lane_width above p.free_passage_width and no other road user is in the scene."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"x drives along the rural roadway without halting."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x halts in one lane of a rural two-lane highway with the other lane empty, but the source does not observe lane widths.","masked":["st.lane_width"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"x halts with its engine not running and its hazard lamps flashing: the disabled-vehicle exception applies."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.speed_resolution","unit":"m/s","value":0.2,"convention":"Sensor resolution: the smallest speed the acquisition standard separates from standstill; a speed at or below it counts as no motion.","source":"speed resolution of the carla_scene_graph acquisition standard"},{"name":"p.free_passage_width","unit":"m","value":3.0,"convention":"Free-passage width: the smallest width of an unoccupied lane beside a standing vehicle that lets another vehicle pass; a design passenger-car width plus lateral clearance.","source":"AASHTO Green Book design-vehicle widths and lane widths"},{"name":"p.opposite_lane_reach","unit":"m","value":1.0,"convention":"Beside reach: the largest ground distance from a standing vehicle's body to a lane within which the lane counts as opposite the vehicle; covers the lateral gap between the body and the next lane's edge.","source":"lane-keeping offset conventions"}],"gaps":[{"span":"g13","kind":"atom","proposal":"`ru.disabled` | a vehicle that cannot proceed under its own power, by a mechanical failure, crash damage or a flat tyre, as the source records it **Not a stand-in for:** a vehicle parked with its engine off, or one showing hazard lamps | general — decides whether moving the vehicle off the roadway can be carried out, which the disabled-vehicle exception turns on","nearest":["kin.engine_running","sig.hazard"]}]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_440_1_o3","law_refs":["NRS-484B-440-1"],"subject":{"binder":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"g1","text":"Upon any highway","role":"trigger"},{"id":"g2","text":"outside of a business or residence district","role":"condition"},{"id":"g3","text":"no person shall stop, park or leave standing","role":"sibling"},{"id":"g4","text":"any vehicle, whether attended or unattended,","role":"subject"},{"id":"g5","text":"upon the paved or main-traveled part of the highway","role":"trigger"},{"id":"g6","text":"when it is practicable to stop, park or so leave such vehicle off such part of the highway,","role":"sibling"},{"id":"g7","text":"but in every event","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"g8","text":"an unobstructed width of the highway","role":"sibling"},{"id":"g9","text":"opposite a standing vehicle","role":"sibling"},{"id":"g10","text":"shall be left for the free passage of other vehicles","role":"sibling"},{"id":"g11","text":"and","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"g12","text":"a clear view of such stopped vehicles shall be available from a distance of 200 feet in each direction upon such highway.","role":"obligation"},{"id":"g13","text":"This section shall not apply to the driver of any vehicle which is disabled while on the paved or main-traveled portion of a highway in such manner and to such extent that it is impossible to avoid stopping and temporarily leaving such disabled vehicle in such position.","role":"exception"}],"elements":[{"span":"g1","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.highway"],"derived":[],"justification":"st.highway: \"the entire public way between its boundary lines, including sidewalks and shoulders\"; x is upon it where its footprint overlaps it (rel.occupies)."},{"span":"g4","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, claimed by id; 'whether attended or unattended' excludes no member."},{"span":"g5","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.roadway"],"derived":[],"justification":"'such stopped vehicles' are those of the first clause, upon the paved or main-traveled part: the st.roadway (\"the part of a highway improved for vehicular traffic, excluding shoulder\"), overlapped by x's footprint (rel.occupies)."},{"span":"g12","atoms":["st.sight_distance","kin.speed"],"derived":["drv.motion.halted"],"justification":"A stopped vehicle is x halted (drv.motion.halted, kin.speed at or below the resolution); the stop is not a prohibited one here, so the definition of stopping when prohibited adds no exclusion. A clear view of it from a distance along the highway is st.sight_distance at its place: \"the distance along the road within which a vehicle at a point and another vehicle on the road could see each other ... both the view of approaching traffic from that point and its being seen by drivers approaching it\"; it is at least the law's literal. It is 'not a stand-in' for whether an actual road user saw x (rel.visible), and is not used as one."},{"span":"g13","atoms":["kin.engine_running","sig.hazard","rel.occupies","st.roadway"],"derived":[],"justification":"A vehicle disabled on the roadway is read through its nearest observables, as in the first obligation of this line: engine or motor not running (kin.engine_running: \"so that propulsion is available\", false) with hazard lamps flashing (sig.hazard: \"both indicators flashing together\"), while it occupies the roadway (rel.occupies, st.roadway). kin.engine_running is 'not a stand-in' for motion or a halt; the gap records that the disability itself has no atom."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[{"span":"g2","id":"asm.within_business_or_residence_district","meaning":"The place of the observation lies inside a business district or a residence district declared for the map or the trace."}],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"x carries ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; at the observation x is halted (drv.motion.halted with p.speed_resolution) with its footprint overlapping a st.roadway of a st.highway (rel.occupies); asm.within_business_or_residence_district does not hold; and x is not disabled there: not (kin.engine_running false and sig.hazard on).","obligation":"The sight distance at x's place (st.sight_distance) is at least the literal of span g12.","params":["p.speed_resolution"],"narrowings":[{"span":"g12","why":"'in each direction' is read through the sight distance the source reports for the place, which states both the view from it and its being seen along the road without separating the two directions of the way.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"x (ru.motor_vehicle) halts on the roadway of a rural highway just beyond a crest, where st.sight_distance is below the literal of span g12."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"x halts on a straight, level rural roadway where st.sight_distance is well above the literal."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"x drives along the rural roadway without halting."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x halts on the rural roadway near a crest, but the source does not supply sight distances.","masked":["st.sight_distance"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"x halts just beyond a crest with its engine not running and its hazard lamps flashing: the disabled-vehicle exception applies."}],"literals":[{"span":"g12","text":"200 feet","value":200,"unit":"ft"}],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.speed_resolution","unit":"m/s","value":0.2,"convention":"Sensor resolution: the smallest speed the acquisition standard separates from standstill; a speed at or below it counts as no motion.","source":"speed resolution of the carla_scene_graph acquisition standard"}],"gaps":[{"span":"g13","kind":"atom","proposal":"`ru.disabled` | a vehicle that cannot proceed under its own power, by a mechanical failure, crash damage or a flat tyre, as the source records it **Not a stand-in for:** a vehicle parked with its engine off, or one showing hazard lamps | general — decides whether moving the vehicle off the roadway can be carried out, which the disabled-vehicle exception turns on","nearest":["kin.engine_running","sig.hazard"]}]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_450_1c","law_refs":["NRS-484B-450-1c"],"subject":{"binder":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"h1","text":"A person shall not stop, stand or park","role":"obligation"},{"id":"h2","text":"a vehicle,","role":"subject"},{"id":"h3","text":"except when necessary to avoid conflict with","role":"standard"},{"id":"h4","text":"other traffic","role":"exception"},{"id":"h5","text":"or in compliance with law","role":"exception"},{"id":"h6","text":"or the directions of a police officer or official traffic-control device,","role":"exception"},{"id":"h7","text":"in any of the following places:","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"h8","text":"Within an intersection.","role":"trigger"}],"elements":[{"span":"h1","atoms":["kin.speed"],"derived":["drv.motion.halted"],"justification":"'stop', prohibited here, takes DEF-NRS-484A-260 (\"any halting, even momentarily, of a vehicle, whether occupied or not\"), whose exclusions the law's own spans h3 to h6 restate; 'stand' (DEF-NRS-484A-250, \"the halting of a vehicle\") and 'park' (DEF-NRS-484A-155, \"the standing of a vehicle\") are halts too. The halt is drv.motion.halted (kin.speed at or below the resolution, \"with no minimum duration\"), observing any halting, even momentary. 'A person' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion (observable_reading agency); the purposes setting parking and standing apart are read through the halt (observable_reading purpose)."},{"span":"h2","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, claimed by id."},{"span":"h4","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic"],"derived":[],"justification":"'other traffic' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic (\"pedestrians, ridden or herded animals, vehicles and other conveyances\"), every member other than x."},{"span":"h5","atoms":["ru.emergency_vehicle","sig.warning_lamp","sig.siren"],"derived":[],"justification":"A halt in compliance with law is a halt some rule requires. The nearest observables are those of the commonest such halt inside an intersection, yielding to an emergency vehicle showing its warning lamps or sounding its siren (ru.emergency_vehicle with sig.warning_lamp flashing or rotating, or sig.siren); ru.emergency_vehicle is 'not a stand-in' for a responding vehicle, which is why its lamp or siren is read. The gap records that no operator reads whether any rule requires the halt."},{"span":"h6","atoms":["dev.human_direction","dev.traffic_signal","dev.stop_sign","dev.governs","rel.occupies","st.travel_region","st.lane_enters","st.intersection"],"derived":[],"justification":"The directions of a police officer: dev.human_direction (\"a person directing traffic and the direction given; role ∈ {police_officer, ...}; indication ∈ {stop, ...}\") with role police_officer and indication stop; of an official traffic-control device: a dev.traffic_signal displaying circular_red, a red_arrow or flashing_red, or a dev.stop_sign; either governing (dev.governs) the intersection x occupies or the carrier it entered through (st.lane_enters, rel.occupies). The device's presence is the evidence of its official status (observable_reading status)."},{"span":"h8","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.intersection"],"derived":[],"justification":"Within an intersection: x's footprint overlaps (rel.occupies) a st.intersection (\"the region where two roadways meet\"; DEF-NRS-484A-105). st.intersection is 'not a stand-in' for a crosswalk or a stop line, which are not read."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"h3","standard":"necessary to avoid conflict","concepts":["rel.bearing","rel.surface_gap"],"params":["p.stopping_conflict_gap"],"convention":"Conflict-standoff convention: a halt is necessary to avoid a conflict where another member of traffic lies ahead of the halted vehicle (the longitudinal component of rel.bearing positive, in the vehicle's frame) at a surface gap no greater than a queue spacing at standstill; the measured gap is compared with the bound.","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"x","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"x carries ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle and at the observation its footprint overlaps an intersection i (rel.occupies, st.intersection).","obligation":"It is not the case that x is halted (drv.motion.halted with p.speed_resolution) at the observation, unless: some road user other than x carrying ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic lies ahead of x (rel.bearing longitudinal component positive) at a surface gap (rel.surface_gap) at most p.stopping_conflict_gap; or a ru.emergency_vehicle showing sig.warning_lamp flashing or rotating or sounding sig.siren is in the scene; or a dev.human_direction of role police_officer with indication stop, a dev.traffic_signal displaying circular_red, a red_arrow or flashing_red, or a dev.stop_sign governs (dev.governs) i or the carrier x entered i through.","params":["p.speed_resolution","p.stopping_conflict_gap"],"narrowings":[{"span":"h1","why":"'A person' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion; the purposes that set standing and parking apart from stopping are not observable and every halt is read as a stop.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"h6","why":"'official' is read through the device's presence on the road.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"status"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"x (ru.motor_vehicle) halts inside intersection i with nothing ahead of it, no emergency vehicle in the scene and no device or officer directing a stop."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"x crosses i without halting; no other road user is in the scene."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"x halts in a lane away from any intersection."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"x halts at the edge of i, but the source does not observe whether its footprint overlaps i.","masked":["rel.occupies"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"compliant","narrative":"x halts inside i behind a halted car ahead of it at a surface gap below p.stopping_conflict_gap."},{"name":"branch_2","expected":"compliant","narrative":"x halts inside i while a dev.human_direction of role police_officer with indication stop governs i."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.speed_resolution","unit":"m/s","value":0.2,"convention":"Sensor resolution: the smallest speed the acquisition standard separates from standstill; a speed at or below it counts as no motion.","source":"speed resolution of the carla_scene_graph acquisition standard"},{"name":"p.stopping_conflict_gap","unit":"m","value":5.0,"convention":"Conflict standoff: the largest surface gap from a halted road user's body to another road user ahead of it at which the halt counts as necessary to avoid a conflict; a queue spacing at standstill.","source":"queue spacing at standstill (traffic-flow jam-density conventions)"}],"gaps":[{"span":"h5","kind":"operator","proposal":"`Formula.haltRequired (subject)` — true at an observation where some rule of the set, engaged for the subject there, is complied with only if the subject is halted; decides whether a halt was made in compliance with law, the action the law requires, which the exception 'in compliance with law' turns on and which no single composed rule names","nearest":["ru.emergency_vehicle","sig.warning_lamp","sig.siren"]}]}

